\p \v 17 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb they will call|יִקְרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb The Throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb* \rb will be gathered|וְנִקְוּ֨וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb to honor the name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb They will no longer|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb follow|יֵלְכ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֕י\rb* \rb the stubbornness|שְׁרִר֖וּת\rb* \rb of their evil|הָרָֽע׃ס\rb* \rb hearts.|לִבָּ֥ם\rb* \v 18 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔מָּה\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb will walk|יֵלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and they will come|וְיָבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּו֙\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave to your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb as an inheritance.|הִנְחַ֖לְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Then I|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb said,|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb ‘How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb I long to make you|אֲשִׁיתֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb My sons|בַּבָּנִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and give|וְאֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לָךְ֙\rb* \rb a desirable|חֶמְדָּ֔ה\rb* \rb land,|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb the most beautiful|צְבִ֖י\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb*
\q2 \rb of all|צִבְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb the nations!’|גּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb I thought|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb you would call Me|תִּקְרְאוּ\rb*\rb |לִ֔י\rb* \rb ‘Father’|אָבִי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb turn away|תָשׁוּבוּ׃\rb* \rb from following Me.|וּמֵאַחֲרַ֖י\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb But|אָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb as a woman|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb may betray|בָּגְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb her husband,|מֵרֵעָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you have betrayed|בְּגַדְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb Me,|בִּ֛י\rb* \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel,”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb A voice|ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb is heard|נִשְׁמָ֔ע\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the barren heights,|שְׁפָיִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb the children|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb weeping|בְּכִ֥י\rb* \rb and begging for mercy,|תַחֲנוּנֵ֖י\rb*
\q1 \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they have perverted|הֶעֱוּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ways|דַּרְכָּ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and forgotten|שָׁכְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֥ה\rb* \rb their God.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb “Return,|שׁ֚וּבוּ\rb* \rb O faithless|שׁוֹבָבִ֔ים\rb* \rb children,|בָּנִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and I will heal|אֶרְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb your faithlessness.”|מְשׁוּבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Here we are.|הִנְנוּ֙\rb* \rb We come|אָתָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb to You,|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are the LORD|יְהֹוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 23 \rb Surely|אָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb deception|לַשֶּׁ֛קֶר\rb* \rb comes from the hills,|מִגְּבָע֖וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and commotion|הָמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb from the mountains.|הָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q1 \rb Surely|אָכֵן֙\rb* \rb the salvation|תְּשׁוּעַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\q2 \rb is in the LORD|בַּיהֹוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 24 \rb From our youth,|מִנְּעוּרֵ֑ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that shameful god|וְהַבֹּ֗שֶׁת\rb*
\q2 \rb has consumed|אָֽכְלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb have worked for—|יְגִ֥יעַ\rb*
\q1 \rb their flocks|צֹאנָם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and herds,|בְּקָרָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters.|בְּנוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 25 \rb Let us lie down|נִשְׁכְּבָ֣ה\rb* \rb in our shame;|בְּבָשְׁתֵּ֗נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb let our disgrace|כְּלִמָּתֵנוּ֒\rb*\rb |כִּי֩\rb* \rb cover us.|וּֽתְכַסֵּנוּ֮\rb*
\q1 \rb We have sinned|חָטָ֗אנוּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֜ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb both we|אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb and our fathers;|וַאֲבוֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb from our youth|מִנְּעוּרֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb even to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb we have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמַ֔עְנוּ\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.”|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*
\c 4
\s1 A Plea to Return
\q1 \v 1 \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb you will return,|תָּשׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל׀\rb*
\q2 \rb return|תָּשׁ֑וּב\rb* \rb to Me,”|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*
\q1 \rb “If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you will remove|תָּסִ֧יר\rb* \rb your detestable idols|שִׁקּוּצֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb from My sight|מִפָּנַ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb and no longer|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb waver,|תָנֽוּד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb and if you can swear,|וְנִשְׁבַּ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives,’|חַי־\rb*
\q2 \rb in truth,|בֶּאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb in justice,|בְּמִשְׁפָּ֣ט\rb* \rb and in righteousness,|וּבִצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb then the nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb will be blessed|וְהִתְבָּ֥רְכוּ\rb* \rb by Him,|וּב֥וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and in Him|ב֛וֹ\rb* \rb they will glory.”|יִתְהַלָּֽלוּ׃ס\rb*
\b 
\p \v 3 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the men|לְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem:|וְלִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Break up|נִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb unplowed ground,|נִ֑יר\rb*
\q2 \rb and do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb sow|תִּזְרְע֖וּ\rb* \rb among|אֶל־\rb* \rb the thorns.|קוֹצִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Circumcise yourselves|הִמֹּ֣לוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַיהֹוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and remove|וְהָסִ֙רוּ֙\rb* \rb the foreskins|עָרְל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of your hearts,|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb O men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb Otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֗י\rb* \rb will break out|תֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb like fire|כָאֵ֜שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and burn|וּבָעֲרָה֙\rb* \rb with no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one to extinguish it,|מְכַבֶּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your evil|רֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb deeds.”|מַעַלְלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Disaster from the North
\p \v 5 \rb Announce|הַגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb in Judah,|בִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb proclaim|הַשְׁמִ֔יעוּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and say:|וְאִמְר֕וּ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Blow|וְתִקְעוּ\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb* \rb throughout the land.|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb Cry aloud|קִרְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |מַלְאוּ֙\rb* \rb and say,|וְאִמְר֔וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Assemble yourselves|הֵאָסְפ֥וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and let us flee|וְנָב֖וֹאָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַמִּבְצָֽר׃\rb* \rb cities.’|עָרֵ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Raise|שְׂאוּ־\rb* \rb a signal flag|נֵ֣ס\rb* \rb toward Zion.|צִיּ֔וֹנָה\rb*
\q2 \rb Seek refuge!|הָעִ֖יזוּ\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb delay!|תַּעֲמֹ֑דוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am bringing|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb from the north,|מִצָּפ֖וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and terrible|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb destruction.|וְשֶׁ֥בֶר\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb A lion|אַרְיֵה֙\rb* \rb has gone up|עָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb from his thicket,|מִֽסֻּבְּכ֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and a destroyer|וּמַשְׁחִ֣ית\rb* \rb of nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb has set out.|נָסַ֖ע\rb*
\q1 \rb He has left|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb his lair|מִמְּקֹמ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb to lay|לָשׂ֤וּם\rb* \rb waste|לְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb your land.|אַרְצֵךְ֙\rb*
\q1 \rb Your cities|עָרַ֥יִךְ\rb* \rb will be reduced|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to ruins|תִּצֶּ֖ינָה\rb*
\q2 \rb and lie uninhabited.|יוֹשֵֽׁב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |זֹ֛את\rb* \rb put on|חִגְר֥וּ\rb* \rb sackcloth,|שַׂקִּ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb mourn|סִפְד֣וּ\rb* \rb and wail,|וְהֵילִ֑ילוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the fierce|חֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turned away|שָׁ֛ב\rb* \rb from us.”|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃פ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb |וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb “In that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day,”|בַיּוֹם־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb “the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and officials|הַשָּׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb will lose|יֹאבַ֥ד\rb* \rb their courage.|לֵב־\rb*
\q1 \rb The priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb will tremble in fear,|וְנָשַׁ֙מּוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the prophets|וְהַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb will be astounded.”|יִתְמָֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then I said,|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb “Ah,|אֲהָ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb how completely|אָכֵן֩\rb* \rb You have deceived|הַשֵּׁ֨א\rb*\rb |הִשֵּׁ֜אתָ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|לָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וְלִירוּשָׁלִַ֣ם\rb* \rb by saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘You will have|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְנָגְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb peace,’|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb while a sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb is at|עַד־\rb* \rb our throats.”|הַנָּֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb it will be said|יֵאָמֵ֤ר\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|לָֽעָם־\rb* \rb and to Jerusalem,|וְלִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb “A searing|צַ֤ח\rb* \rb wind|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb from the barren heights|שְׁפָיִים֙\rb* \rb in the desert|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb blows toward|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of My people,|עַמִּ֑י\rb* \rb but not|ל֥וֹא\rb* \rb to winnow|לִזְר֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb or to sift;|לְהָבַֽר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb a wind|ר֧וּחַ\rb* \rb too strong|מָלֵ֛א\rb* \rb for that|מֵאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb comes|יָ֣בוֹא\rb* \rb from Me.|לִ֑י\rb* \rb Now|עַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb pronounce|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb judgments|מִשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb* \rb against them.”|אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb he advances|יַעֲלֶ֗ה\rb* \rb like the clouds,|כַּעֲנָנִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb his chariots|מַרְכְּבוֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb like the whirlwind.|וְכַסּוּפָה֙\rb*
