\q2 \rb terror|מָג֖וֹר\rb* \rb is on every side.|מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 26 \rb O daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of my people,|עַמִּ֤י\rb*
\q2 \rb dress|חִגְרִי־\rb* \rb yourselves in sackcloth|שָׂק֙\rb* \rb and roll|וְהִתְפַּלְּשִׁ֣י\rb* \rb in ashes.|בָאֵ֔פֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb Mourn|אֵ֤בֶל\rb* \rb with bitter|תַּמְרוּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb wailing,|מִסְפַּ֖ד\rb*
\q2 \rb as you would|עֲשִׂ֣י\rb* \rb for an only son,|יָחִיד֙\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb suddenly|פִתְאֹ֔ם\rb* \rb the destroyer|הַשֹּׁדֵ֖ד\rb*
\q2 \rb will come|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb upon us.|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb “I have appointed you|נְתַתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb to examine|בָּח֛וֹן\rb* \rb My people|בְעַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb like ore,|מִבְצָ֑ר\rb*\f + \fr 6:27 \ft Or \fqa to examine My people, a fortress\f*
\q2 \rb so you may know|וְתֵדַ֕ע\rb* \rb and try|וּבָחַנְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ways.|דַּרְכָּֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 28 \rb All|כֻּלָּם֙\rb* \rb are hardened|סֽוֹרְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb rebels,|סָרֵ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb walking around|הֹלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb as slanderers.|רָכִ֖יל\rb*
\q1 \rb They are bronze|נְחֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron;|וּבַרְזֶ֑ל\rb*
