\c 7
\s1 Jeremiah’s Message at the Temple Gate
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Stand|עֲמֹ֗ד\rb* \rb in the gate|בְּשַׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and proclaim|וְקָרָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאָמַרְתָּ֞\rb* \rb message:|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb Hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you people of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb who enter|הַבָּאִים֙\rb* \rb through these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb gates|בַּשְּׁעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \v 3 \rb Thus|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb Correct|הֵיטִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and deeds,|וּמַֽעַלְלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will let you live|וַאֲשַׁכְּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place.|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \v 4 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb trust|תִּבְטְח֣וּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb deceptive|הַשֶּׁ֖קֶר\rb* \rb words,|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘This is|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD.’|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you really correct|הֵיטֵיב֙\rb*\rb |תֵּיטִ֔יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your ways|דַּרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and deeds,|מַֽעַלְלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you act|עָשׂ֤וֹ\rb*\rb |תַֽעֲשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb justly|מִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb toward one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb if you no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer oppress|תַֽעֲשֹׁ֔קוּ\rb* \rb the foreigner|גֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb and the fatherless|יָת֤וֹם\rb* \rb and the widow,|וְאַלְמָנָה֙\rb* \rb and if you no|אַֽל־\rb* \rb longer shed|תִּשְׁפְּכ֖וּ\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֔י\rb* \rb blood|וְדָ֣ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb or follow|וְאַחֲרֵ֨י\rb*\rb |תֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֛ים\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֧ים\rb* \rb to your own harm,|לְרַ֥ע\rb* \v 7 \rb then I will let you live|וְשִׁכַּנְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place,|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb forever|לְמִן־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb ever.|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb But look,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb keep trusting|בֹּטְחִ֣ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb deceptive|הַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb to no|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb avail.|הוֹעִֽיל׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Will you steal|הֲגָנֹ֤ב׀\rb* \rb and murder,|רָצֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb commit adultery|וְֽנָאֹ֔ף\rb* \rb and perjury,|וְהִשָּׁבֵ֥עַ\rb*\rb |לַשֶּׁ֖קֶר\rb* \rb burn incense|וְקַטֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to Baal,|לַבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb and follow|וְהָלֹ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known,|יְדַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb and then come|וּבָאתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb and stand|וַעֲמַדְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֗י\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb house,|בַּבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb which bears|נִקְרָא־\rb* \rb My Name,|שְׁמִ֣י\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and say,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb ‘We are delivered,|נִצַּ֑לְנוּ\rb* \rb so|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb we can continue with|עֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb abominations’?|הַתּוֹעֵב֖וֹת\rb* \v 11 \rb Has this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb house,|הַבַּ֧יִת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb bears|נִקְרָֽא־\rb* \rb My Name,|שְׁמִ֥י\rb* \rb become|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a den|הַמְעָרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of robbers|פָּרִצִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:11 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 21:13|MAT 21:13\ref*, Mark 11:17, and Luke 19:46\f* \rb in|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb your sight?|בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Yes,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb too|גַּ֧ם\rb* \rb have seen it,|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb go|לְכוּ־\rb* \rb now|נָ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְקוֹמִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Shiloh|בְּשִׁיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I first|בָּרִֽאשׁוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb made a dwelling|שִׁכַּ֧נְתִּֽי\rb* \rb for My Name,|שְׁמִ֛י\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I did|עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to it|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֕י\rb* \rb the wickedness|רָעַ֖ת\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb because|יַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשׂוֹתְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb things,|הַמַּֽעֲשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and because I have spoken|וָאֲדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb again and again|הַשְׁכֵּ֤ם\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \ft Literally \fqa I have spoken to you, rising up early and speaking,\f* \rb |וְדַבֵּר֙\rb*\rb but you would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen,|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb and I have called|וָאֶקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but you would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer,|עֲנִיתֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb therefore what I did|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb to Shiloh|לְשִׁלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb I will now do|וְעָשִׂ֜יתִי\rb* \rb to the house|לַבַּ֣יִת׀\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb bears|נִֽקְרָא־\rb* \rb My Name,|שְׁמִ֣י\rb*\rb |עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb the house in which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb trust,|בֹּטְחִ֣ים\rb* \rb the place|וְלַ֨מָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your fathers.|וְלַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \v 15 \rb And I will cast|וְהִשְׁלַכְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My presence,|פָּנָ֑י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have cast out|הִשְׁלַ֙כְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your brothers,|אֲחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the descendants|זֶ֥רַע\rb* \rb of Ephraim.|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Judah’s Idolatry Persists
\p \v 16 \rb As for you,|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb pray|תִּתְפַּלֵּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb offer|תִּשָּׂ֧א\rb* \rb a plea|רִנָּ֥ה\rb* \rb or petition|וּתְפִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb on their behalf,|בַעֲדָ֛ם\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb beg|תִּפְגַּע־\rb* \rb Me,|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb I will not|אֵינֶ֥נִּי\rb* \rb listen|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb to you.|אֹתָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Do you not|הַֽאֵינְךָ֣\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb what|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem?|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb The sons|הַבָּנִ֞ים\rb* \rb gather|מְלַקְּטִ֣ים\rb* \rb wood,|עֵצִ֗ים\rb* \rb the fathers|וְהָֽאָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb light|מְבַעֲרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fire,|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and the women|וְהַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb knead|לָשׁ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the dough|בָּצֵ֑ק\rb* \rb to make|לַעֲשׂ֨וֹת\rb* \rb cakes|כַּוָּנִ֜ים\rb* \rb for the Queen|לִמְלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of Heaven;|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb* \rb they pour out|וְהַסֵּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִים֙\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb provoke Me to anger.|הַכְעִסֵֽנִי׃\rb* \v 19 \rb |הַאֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb But am I the One|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb they are provoking?|מַכְעִסִ֖ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Is it not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb themselves|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb they spite,|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb to their own shame?|בֹּ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּ֤י\rb* \rb and My fury|וַֽחֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb will|נִתֶּ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb be poured out on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place,|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb and beast,|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the trees|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the produce|פְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the land,|הָֽאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and it will burn|וּבָעֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be extinguished.|תִכְבֶּֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb Add your burnt offerings|עֹלוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |סְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your other sacrifices|זִבְחֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and eat|וְאִכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb the meat yourselves!|בָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb when|בְּי֛וֹם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb I brought|הוֹצִיא\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb I did not merely|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דִבַּ֤רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb command them|צִוִּיתִ֔ים\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and sacrifices,|וָזָֽבַח׃\rb* \v 23 \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this is what|הַ֠זֶּה\rb* \rb I commanded them:|צִוִּ֨יתִי\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֤ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֙\rb* \rb Obey Me,|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |בְקוֹלִ֔י\rb* \rb and I will be|וְהָיִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb your|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb God,|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb will be|תִּֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people.|לְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb You must walk|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have commanded|אֲצַוֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb it may go well|יִיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb with you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Yet they did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb incline|הִטּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ear,|אָזְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb but they followed|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb the stubborn|בִּשְׁרִר֖וּת\rb* \rb inclinations|בְּמֹ֣עֵצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of their own evil|הָרָ֑ע\rb* \rb hearts.|לִבָּ֣ם\rb* \rb They went|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb backward|לְאָח֖וֹר\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb forward.|לְפָנִֽים׃\rb* \v 25 \rb From|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb came out|יָצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I have sent|וָאֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb*\rb |י֖וֹם\rb* \rb again and again.|הַשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 7:25 \ft Literally \fqa I have sent you all My servants the prophets daily, rising up early and sending (them).\f* \rb |וְשָׁלֹֽחַ׃\rb*\v 26 \rb Yet they would not|וְל֤וֹא\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb incline|הִטּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ear,|אָזְנָ֑ם\rb* \rb but they stiffened|וַיַּקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb their necks|עָרְפָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and did more evil|הֵרֵ֖עוּ\rb* \rb than their fathers.|מֵאֲבוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb When you tell|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb things,|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb When you call|וְקָרָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb they will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer.|יַעֲנֽוּכָה׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Therefore you must say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb ‘This|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb is the nation|הַגּוֹי֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb would not|לֽוֹא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֗וּ\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb receive|לָקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb correction.|מוּסָ֑ר\rb* \rb Truth|הָֽאֱמוּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb has perished;|אָֽבְדָה֙\rb* \rb it has disappeared|וְנִכְרְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb from their lips.|מִפִּיהֶֽם׃ס\rb* \v 29 \rb Cut off|גָּזִּ֤י\rb* \rb your hair|נִזְרֵךְ֙\rb* \rb and throw it away.|וְֽהַשְׁלִ֔יכִי\rb* \rb Raise up|וּשְׂאִ֥י\rb* \rb a lamentation|קִינָ֑ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the barren heights,|שְׁפָיִ֖ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has rejected|מָאַ֣ס\rb* \rb and forsaken|וַיִּטֹּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the generation|דּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of His wrath.’|עֶבְרָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\s1 The Valley of Slaughter
\p \v 30 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the people|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb have done|עָשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in My sight,|בְּעֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻום־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb They have set up|שָׂ֣מוּ\rb* \rb their abominations|שִׁקּֽוּצֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb bears|נִקְרָא־\rb* \rb My Name,|שְׁמִ֥י\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb and so have defiled it.|לְטַמְּאֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 31 \rb They have built|וּבָנ֞וּ\rb* \rb the high places|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Topheth|הַתֹּ֗פֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the Valley of Ben-hinnom|בְּגֵ֣יא\rb* \rb so they could burn|לִשְׂרֹ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their sons|בֶן־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּ֔ם\rb*\rb |בְּנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the fire—|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb something I never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb commanded,|צִוִּ֔יתִי\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb did it even enter|עָלְתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb My mind.|לִבִּֽי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb So|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִים֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb when this place will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb be called|יֵאָמֵ֨ר\rb* \rb Topheth|הַתֹּ֙פֶת֙\rb* \rb and the Valley of Ben-hinnom,|וְגֵ֣יא\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּ֔ם\rb* \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the Valley|גֵּ֣יא\rb* \rb of Slaughter.|הַהֲרֵגָ֑ה\rb* \rb For they will bury the dead|וְקָבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb in Topheth|בְתֹ֖פֶת\rb* \rb until there is no|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb more room.|מָקֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 33 \rb The corpses|נִבְלַ֨ת\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb will become|וְֽהָ֨יְתָ֜ה\rb* \rb food|לְמַֽאֲכָ֔ל\rb* \rb for the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the beasts|וּלְבֶהֱמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the earth,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and there will be no one|וְאֵ֖ין\rb* \rb to scare them away.|מַחֲרִֽיד׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb I will remove|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb from the cities|מֵעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the streets|וּמֵֽחֻצוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb the sounds|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of joy|שָׂשׂוֹן֙\rb* \rb and gladness|שִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb*\rb |ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb and the voices|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the bride|כַּלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb bridegroom,|חָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb will become|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a wasteland.”|לְחָרְבָּ֖ה\rb*
\c 8
\s1 Judah’s Sin and Punishment
\p \v 1 \rb “At that|הַהִ֣יא\rb* \rb time,”|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb “the bones|עַצְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמוֹת־\rb* \rb of the officials,|שָׂרָיו֩\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the prophets,|הַנְּבִיאִ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and the bones|עַצְמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the people|יוֹשְׁבֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֖ם\rb* \rb will be removed|וְיֹצִיאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from their graves.|מִקִּבְרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb They will be exposed|וּשְׁטָחוּם֩\rb* \rb to the sun|לַשֶּׁ֨מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and moon,|וְלַיָּרֵ֜חַ\rb* \rb and to all|וּלְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they have loved,|אֲהֵב֜וּם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb served,|עֲבָדוּם֙\rb*\rb |וַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb followed,|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb consulted,|דְּרָשׁ֔וּם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and worshiped.|הִֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb Their bones will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be gathered up|יֵאָֽסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb buried,|יִקָּבֵ֔רוּ\rb* \rb but will become|יִֽהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb like dung|לְדֹ֛מֶן\rb* \rb lying on|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ground.|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \v 3 \rb And wherever|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּקֹמ֤וֹת\rb*\rb |הַנִּשְׁאָרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have banished them,|הִדַּחְתִּ֣ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |לְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the remnant|הַשְּׁאֵרִית֙\rb*\rb |הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb evil|הָֽרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb family|הַמִּשְׁפָּחָ֥ה\rb* \rb will choose|וְנִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb death|מָ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb over|מִן־\rb* \rb life,”|מֵֽחַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So you are to tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
