\c 11
\s1 The Broken Covenant
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Listen|שִׁמְע֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb and tell them|וְדִבַּרְתָּם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the residents|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb You must tell them that|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb Cursed is|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|יִשְׁמַ֔ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb covenant,|הַבְּרִ֥ית\rb* \v 4 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your forefathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֡ם\rb* \rb when|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb I brought them out|הוֹצִיאִֽי־\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַיִם֩\rb* \rb out of the iron|הַבַּרְזֶ֜ל\rb* \rb furnace,|מִכּ֨וּר\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Obey Me,|שִׁמְע֤וּ\rb*\rb |בְקוֹלִי֙\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I command you,|אֲצַוֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you will be|וִהְיִ֤יתֶם\rb* \rb My|לִי֙\rb* \rb people,|לְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and I|וְאָ֣נֹכִ֔י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God.’|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 5 \rb This was in order to|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb establish|הָקִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבוּעָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb to your forefathers,|לַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to give them|לָתֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֛ב\rb* \rb and honey,|וּדְבַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb as it is to this day.”|כַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb “Amen,|אָמֵ֥ן׀\rb* \rb LORD,”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb I answered.|וָאַ֥עַן\rb*\rb |וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb “Proclaim|קְרָ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb Hear|שִׁמְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb and carry them out.|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb from the time|בְּיוֹם֩\rb* \rb I brought|הַעֲלוֹתִ֨י\rb* \rb your fathers|בַּאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb today,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb I strongly warned them|הָעֵ֨ד\rb*\rb |הַעִדֹ֜תִי\rb* \rb again and again,|הַשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 11:7 \ft Literally \fqa I earnestly warned them, rising up early and warning (them),\f* \rb |וְהָעֵ֖ד\rb*\rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘Obey|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb My voice.’|בְּקוֹלִֽי׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Yet they would|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb obey|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb or incline|הִטּ֣וּ\rb* \rb their ears,|אָזְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb but each one|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb followed|וַיֵּ֣לְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb the stubbornness|בִּשְׁרִיר֖וּת\rb* \rb of his evil|הָרָ֑ע\rb* \rb heart.|לִבָּ֣ם\rb* \rb So I brought|וָאָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb them|אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the curses|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb covenant|הַבְּרִית־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had commanded them|צִוִּ֥יתִי\rb* \rb to follow|עָשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb* \rb but they did not keep.”|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb “There is|נִֽמְצָא־\rb* \rb a conspiracy|קֶ֙שֶׁר֙\rb* \rb among the men|בְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the residents|וּבְיֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb They have returned|שָׁ֩בוּ֩\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the sins|עֲוֺנֹ֨ת\rb* \rb of their forefathers|אֲבוֹתָ֜ם\rb*\rb |הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb refused|מֵֽאֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb to obey|לִשְׁמ֣וֹעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My words.|דְּבָרַ֔י\rb* \rb They|וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb have followed|הָלְכ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb to serve them.|לְעָבְדָ֑ם\rb* \rb The house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and the house|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have broken|הֵפֵ֤רוּ\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִיתִ֕י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I made|כָּרַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb their fathers.|אֲבוֹתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘I am about to bring|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb upon them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb a disaster|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they cannot|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יוּכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb escape.|לָצֵ֣את\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb* \rb They will cry out|וְזָעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb but I will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|אֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Then the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the residents|וְיֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb will go|וְהָֽלְכ֞וּ\rb* \rb and cry out|וְזָֽעֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gods|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb have been burning incense,|מְקַטְּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb but these gods certainly will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb save|וְהוֹשֵׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |יוֹשִׁ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in their time|בְּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb of disaster.|רָעָתָֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Your gods|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb are|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb indeed|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb as numerous|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb as your cities,|עָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb O Judah;|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb the altars|מִזְבְּחוֹת֙\rb* \rb of shame|לַבֹּ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb you have set up—|שַׂמְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb the altars|מִזְבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְקַטֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Baal—|לַבָּֽעַל׃ס\rb* \rb are as many|וּמִסְפַּ֞ר\rb* \rb as the streets|חֻצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.’|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb As for you,|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb pray|תִּתְפַּלֵּל֙\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people.|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb raise up|תִּשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb a cry|רִנָּ֣ה\rb* \rb or a prayer|וּתְפִלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb on their behalf,|בַעֲדָ֖ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I will not|אֵינֶ֣נִּי\rb* \rb be listening|שֹׁמֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb when they call out|קָרְאָ֥ם\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb in their time|בְּעֵ֛ת\rb* \rb of disaster.|רָעָתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb What right|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb has My beloved|לִֽידִידִ֞י\rb* \rb in My house,|בְּבֵיתִ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb having carried out|עֲשׂוֹתָ֤הּ\rb* \rb so many|הָֽרַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb evil schemes?|הַֽמְזִמָּ֙תָה֙\rb*
\q1 \rb Can consecrated|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb meat|וּבְשַׂר־\rb* \rb avert|יַעַבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb your doom?|מֵֽעָלָ֑יִךְ\rb* \rb When|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you are wicked,|רָעָתֵ֖כִי\rb*
\q2 \rb then|אָ֥ז\rb* \rb you rejoice.|תַּעֲלֹֽזִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb once called|קָרָ֥א\rb* \rb you|שְׁמֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb a flourishing|רַֽעֲנָן֙\rb* \rb olive tree,|זַ֤יִת\rb*
\q2 \rb beautiful|יְפֵ֣ה\rb* \rb with well-formed|תֹ֔אַר\rb* \rb fruit.|פְרִי־\rb*
\q1 \rb But with a mighty|גְדֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb roar|לְק֣וֹל׀\rb*\rb |הֲמוּלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb He will set it on fire,|הִצִּ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֵשׁ֙\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and its branches|דָּלִיּוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb will be consumed.|וְרָע֖וּ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb The LORD|וַיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb who planted|הַנּוֹטֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb you,|אוֹתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb has decreed|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb on account of|בִּ֠גְלַל\rb* \rb the evil that|רָעַ֨ת\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb and the house|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb have brought upon themselves,|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb provoking Me to anger|לְהַכְעִסֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb by burning incense|לְקַטֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Baal.”|לַבָּֽעַל׃ס\rb*
\s1 A Plot against Jeremiah
\r \ref Jeremiah 18:18–23|JER 18:18-23\ref*)
\q1 \v 18 \rb And the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb informed me,|הֽוֹדִיעַ֖נִי\rb* \rb so I knew.|וָֽאֵדָ֑עָה\rb*
\q2 \rb Then|אָ֖ז\rb* \rb You showed me|הִרְאִיתַ֥נִי\rb* \rb their deeds.|מַעַלְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb For I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb was like a gentle|אַלּ֖וּף\rb* \rb lamb|כְּכֶ֥בֶשׂ\rb* \rb led|יוּבַ֣ל\rb* \rb to slaughter;|לִטְב֑וֹחַ\rb*
\q2 \rb I did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֜עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they had plotted|חָשְׁב֣וּ\rb*\rb |מַחֲשָׁב֗וֹת\rb* \rb against me:|עָלַ֣י׀\rb*
\q1 \rb “Let us destroy|נַשְׁחִ֨יתָה\rb* \rb the tree|עֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb with its fruit;|בְּלַחְמוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb let us cut him off|וְנִכְרְתֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living,|חַיִּ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb that his name|וּשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb may be remembered|יִזָּכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb more.”|עֽוֹד׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb O LORD|וַֽיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb who judges|שֹׁפֵ֣ט\rb* \rb righteously,|צֶ֔דֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb who examines|בֹּחֵ֥ן\rb* \rb the heart|כְּלָי֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 11:20 \ft Hebrew \fqa the kidneys\f* \rb and mind,|וָלֵ֑ב\rb*
\q1 \rb let me see|אֶרְאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb Your vengeance|נִקְמָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb upon them,|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb I have committed|גִּלִּ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my cause.|רִיבִֽי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Anathoth|עֲנָת֔וֹת\rb* \rb who are seeking|הַֽמְבַקְשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb and saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb prophesy|תִנָּבֵא֙\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or you will die|תָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb by our hand.”|בְּיָדֵֽנוּ׃ס\rb* \v 22 \rb So|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb “I will punish them.|פֹקֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Their young men|הַבַּֽחוּרִים֙\rb* \rb will die|יָמֻ֣תוּ\rb* \rb by the sword,|בַחֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנ֣וֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |יָמֻ֖תוּ\rb* \rb by famine.|בָּרָעָֽב׃\rb* \v 23 \rb There will be|תִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb remnant,|וּשְׁאֵרִ֕ית\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will bring|אָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Anathoth|עֲנָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb in the year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of their punishment.”|פְּקֻדָּתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\c 12
\s1 The Prosperity of the Wicked
\q1 \v 1 \rb Righteous|צַדִּ֤יק\rb* \rb are You,|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I plead|אָרִ֖יב\rb* \rb before You.|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Yet|אַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb about Your judgments|מִשְׁפָּטִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb I wish to contend|אֲדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with You:|אוֹתָ֔ךְ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Why|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb does the way|דֶּ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִים֙\rb* \rb prosper?|צָלֵ֔חָה\rb*
\q2 \rb Why do all the faithless|בָֽגֶד׃\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |בֹּ֥גְדֵי\rb* \rb live at ease?|שָׁל֖וּ\rb*
