\s1 A Message for Israel’s Neighbors
\r \ref Amos 1:1–15|AMO 1:1-15\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “As for|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My evil|הָֽרָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb neighbors|שְׁכֵנַי֙\rb* \rb who attack|הַנֹּֽגְעִים֙\rb* \rb the inheritance|בַּֽנַּחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I bequeathed|הִנְחַ֥לְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb I am about to uproot them|נֹֽתְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their land,|אַדְמָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will uproot|אֶתּ֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb from among them.|מִתּוֹכָֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb But|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb I have uprooted them,|נָתְשִׁ֣י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb I will once again|אָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb have compassion on them|וְרִֽחַמְתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb and return|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֛ים\rb* \rb each one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his inheritance|לְנַחֲלָת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and to his land.|לְאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And|וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb they will diligently learn|לָמֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |יִלְמְדוּ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ways|דַּֽרְכֵ֨י\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֜י\rb* \rb and swear|לְהִשָּׁבֵ֤עַ\rb* \rb by My name, saying,|בִּשְׁמִי֙\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives’—|חַי־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they once taught|לִמְּדוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb to swear|לְהִשָּׁבֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb by Baal—|בַּבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb then they will be established|וְנִבְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb My people.|עַמִּֽי׃\rb* \v 17 \rb But if|וְאִ֖ם\rb* \rb they will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey,|יִשְׁמָ֑עוּ\rb* \rb then I will uproot|וְנָ֨תַשְׁתִּ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|הַה֛וּא\rb* \rb nation;|הַגּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb I will uproot it|נָת֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and destroy it,|וְאַבֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 13
\s1 The Linen Loincloth
\p \v 1 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Go|הָל֞וֹךְ\rb* \rb and buy|וְקָנִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb yourself|לְּךָ֙\rb* \rb a linen|פִּשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb loincloth|אֵז֣וֹר\rb* \rb and put|וְשַׂמְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb it around|עַל־\rb* \rb your waist,|מָתְנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb but do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb let it touch|תְבִאֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb water.”|וּבַמַּ֖יִם\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb So I bought|וָאֶקְנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a loincloth|הָאֵז֖וֹר\rb* \rb in accordance with the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and I put|וָאָשִׂ֖ם\rb* \rb it around|עַל־\rb* \rb my waist.|מָתְנָֽי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb a second time:|שֵׁנִ֥ית\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 4 \rb “Take|קַ֧ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the loincloth|הָאֵז֛וֹר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you bought|קָנִ֖יתָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and are wearing,|עַל־\rb*\rb |מָתְנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb at once|וְקוּם֙\rb* \rb to Perath|פְּרָ֔תָה\rb*\f + \fr 13:4 \ft Or possibly \fqa to the Euphrates\ft ; similarly in verses 5–7\f* \rb and hide|וְטָמְנֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb in a crevice|בִּנְקִ֥יק\rb* \rb of the rocks.”|הַסָּֽלַע׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So I went|וָאֵלֵ֕ךְ\rb* \rb and hid it|וָאֶטְמְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Perath,|בִּפְרָ֑ת\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתִֽי׃\rb* \rb had commanded me.|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb Many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb later|מִקֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Arise,|ק֚וּם\rb* \rb go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to Perath,|פְּרָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and get|וְקַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the loincloth|הָ֣אֵז֔וֹר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּיתִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you to hide|לְטָמְנוֹ־\rb* \rb there.”|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb So I went|וָאֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to Perath|פְּרָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and dug up|וָאֶחְפֹּ֗ר\rb* \rb the loincloth,|הָ֣אֵז֔וֹר\rb* \rb and I took|וָֽאֶקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it from|מִן־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had hidden it.|טְמַנְתִּ֣יו\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb But now|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb it|הָאֵז֔וֹר\rb* \rb was ruined—|נִשְׁחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb use|יִצְלַ֖ח\rb* \rb at all.|לַכֹּֽל׃פ\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb In the same way|כָּ֠כָה\rb* \rb I will ruin|אַשְׁחִ֞ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pride|גְּא֧וֹן\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the great|הָרָֽב׃\rb* \rb pride|גְּא֥וֹן\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \v 10 \rb These|הַזֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרָ֜ע\rb* \rb people,|הָעָם֩\rb* \rb who refuse|הַֽמֵּאֲנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמ֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb to My words,|דְּבָרַ֗י\rb* \rb who follow|הַהֹֽלְכִים֙\rb* \rb the stubbornness|בִּשְׁרִר֣וּת\rb* \rb of their own hearts,|לִבָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and who go|וַיֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb to serve|לְעָבְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and worship|וּלְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb they will be|וִיהִי֙\rb* \rb like this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb loincloth—|כָּאֵז֣וֹר\rb*  \rb of no|לֹא־\rb* \rb use|יִצְלַ֖ח\rb* \rb at all.|לַכֹּֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb a loincloth|הָאֵז֜וֹר\rb* \rb clings|יִדְבַּ֨ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a man’s|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb waist,|מָתְנֵי־\rb* \rb so I have made|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb cling|הִדְבַּ֣קְתִּי\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵ֠לַי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb so that they might be|לִֽהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb My|לִי֙\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb for My renown|וּלְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and praise|וְלִתְהִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and glory.|וּלְתִפְאָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb But they did not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb listen.|שָׁמֵֽעוּ׃\rb*
