\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb pray|תִּתְפַּלֵּ֛ל\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb the well-being|לְטוֹבָֽה׃\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people.|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \v 12 \rb Although|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they may fast,|יָצֻ֗מוּ\rb* \rb I will not|אֵינֶ֤נִּי\rb* \rb listen to|שֹׁמֵ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb their cry;|רִנָּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb although|וְכִ֧י\rb* \rb they may offer|יַעֲל֛וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and grain offerings,|וּמִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb I will not|אֵינֶ֣נִּי\rb* \rb accept them.|רֹצָ֑ם\rb* \rb Instead,|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will finish them off|מְכַלֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb and famine|וּבָרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague.”|וּבַדֶּ֔בֶר\rb*
