\c 16
\s1 Disaster Predicted
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb marry|תִקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb have|יִהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb or daughters|וּבָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place.”|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the sons|הַבָּנִים֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb daughters|הַבָּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb born in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place,|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb the mothers|אִמֹּתָ֞ם\rb* \rb who bore them,|הַיִּלּוֹדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |הַמּוֹלִדִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb who fathered|הַיֹּלְד֣וֹת\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb land:|בָּאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \v 4 \rb “They will die|יָמֻ֗תוּ\rb* \rb from deadly|מְמוֹתֵ֨י\rb* \rb diseases.|תַחֲלֻאִ֜ים\rb* \rb They will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be mourned|יִסָּֽפְדוּ֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or buried,|יִקָּבֵ֔רוּ\rb* \rb but will lie|יִֽהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb like dung|לְדֹ֛מֶן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ground.|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb They will be finished off|יִכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb by sword|וּבַחֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb and famine,|וּבָֽרָעָב֙\rb* \rb and their corpses|נִבְלָתָם֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb food|לְמַאֲכָ֔ל\rb* \rb for the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and beasts|וּלְבֶהֱמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth.”|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Indeed,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb enter|תָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb a house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb where there is a funeral meal.|מַרְזֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb go|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to mourn|לִסְפּ֔וֹד\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or show sympathy,|תָּנֹ֖ד\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have removed|אָסַ֨פְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם־\rb* \rb My peace,|שְׁלוֹמִ֜י\rb* \rb My loving devotion,|הַחֶ֖סֶד\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My compassion,”|הָֽרַחֲמִֽים׃\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb “Both great|גְדֹלִ֧ים\rb* \rb and small|וּקְטַנִּ֛ים\rb* \rb will die|וּמֵ֨תוּ\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land.|בָּאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb They will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be buried|יִקָּבֵ֑רוּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb mourned,|יִסְפְּד֣וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will anyone cut himself|יִתְגֹּדַ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or shave his head|יִקָּרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb for them.|לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb No food|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb will be offered|יִפְרְס֥וּ\rb* \rb to comfort|לְנַחֲמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb those who mourn|אֵ֖בֶל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the dead;|מֵ֑ת\rb* \rb not even|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb a cup|כּ֣וֹס\rb* \rb of consolation|תַּנְחוּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb will be given|יַשְׁק֤וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the loss of a father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb or mother.|אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb enter|תָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb a house|וּבֵית־\rb* \rb where there is feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and sit down|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb with them|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb and drink.|וְלִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃ס\rb* \v 9 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb I am going to remove|מַשְׁבִּ֜ית\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb place,|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb before your very eyes|לְעֵינֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and in your days,|וּבִֽימֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the sounds|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of joy|שָׂשׂוֹן֙\rb* \rb and gladness,|שִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb*\rb |ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb the voices|וְק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |וְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the bride|כַּלָּֽה׃\rb* \rb and bridegroom.|חָתָ֖ן\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you tell|תַגִּיד֙\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb people|לָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things,|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb they will ask|וְאָמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb you,|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb ‘Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מֶה֩\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb pronounced|דִבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb against us?|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb What|וּמֶ֤ה\rb* \rb is our iniquity?|עֲוֺנֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb What|וּמֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the sin|חַטָּאתֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we have committed|חָטָ֖אנוּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God?’|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then you are to answer them:|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb ‘It is because|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb have forsaken|עָזְב֨וּ\rb* \rb Me,|אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and followed|וַיֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּם\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲו֣וּ\rb* \rb them.|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb They abandoned Me|עָזָ֔בוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb keep|שָׁמָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb My instruction.|תּוֹרָתִ֖י\rb* \v 12 \rb And you|וְאַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb have done|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb more evil|הֲרֵעֹתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb than your fathers.|מֵאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb See how|וְהִנְּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb each of you|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb follows|הֹלְכִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the stubbornness|שְׁרִר֣וּת\rb* \rb of his evil|הָרָ֔ע\rb* \rb heart|לִבּֽוֹ־\rb* \rb instead of|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb obeying|שְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb Me.|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 13 \rb So I will cast|וְהֵטַלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb out of|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb a land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb neither|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb nor your fathers|וַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb have known.|יְדַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb There|שָׁ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you will serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּם־\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִים֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night,|וָלַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I will show|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb favor.’|חֲנִינָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 God Will Restore Israel
\p \v 14 \rb Yet|לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb when they will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb say,|יֵאָמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites up|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Instead they will say,|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites up|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and all|וּמִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the other lands|הָֽאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had banished them.’|הִדִּיחָ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb For I will return them|וַהֲשִֽׁבֹתִים֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to their forefathers.|לַאֲבוֹתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But for now|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will send for|שֹׁלֵ֜חַ\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֛ים\rb* \rb fishermen,|לְדַוָּגִים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and they will catch them.|וְדִיג֑וּם\rb* \rb After that|וְאַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb I will send|אֶשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb for many|לְרַבִּ֣ים\rb* \rb hunters,|צַיָּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and they will hunt them down|וְצָד֞וּם\rb* \rb on|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb mountain|הַר֙\rb*\rb |וּמֵעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb and hill,|גִּבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb even from the clefts|וּמִנְּקִיקֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the rocks.|הַסְּלָעִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb My eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb are on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their ways.|דַּרְכֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb They are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb hidden|נִסְתְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb from My face,|מִלְּפָנָ֑י\rb* \rb and their guilt|עֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb* \rb is not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb concealed|נִצְפַּ֥ן\rb* \rb from|מִנֶּ֥גֶד\rb* \rb My eyes.|עֵינָֽי׃\rb* \v 18 \rb And I will first|רִֽאשׁוֹנָ֗ה\rb* \rb repay them|וְשִׁלַּמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb double|מִשְׁנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb their iniquity|עֲוֺנָם֙\rb* \rb and their sin,|וְחַטָּאתָ֔ם\rb* \rb because|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb they have defiled|חַלְּלָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My land|אַרְצִ֑י\rb* \rb with the carcasses|בְּנִבְלַ֤ת\rb* \rb of their detestable idols,|שִׁקּֽוּצֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and they have filled|מָלְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My inheritance|נַחֲלָתִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb with their abominations.”|וְתוֹעֲב֣וֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb my strength|עֻזִּ֧י\rb* \rb and my fortress,|וּמָעֻזִּ֛י\rb*
\q2 \rb my refuge|וּמְנוּסִ֖י\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of distress,|צָרָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb the nations|גּוֹיִ֤ם\rb* \rb will come|יָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb from the ends|מֵֽאַפְסֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth,|אָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and they will say,|וְיֹאמְר֗וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb “Our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb inherited|נָחֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb nothing but|אַךְ־\rb* \rb lies,|שֶׁ֙קֶר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb worthless idols|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb of no|וְאֵֽין־\rb* \rb benefit at all.|מוֹעִֽיל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb Can man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb make|הֲיַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb for himself?|לּ֥וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb Such|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb gods!”|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb “Therefore|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb behold,|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I will inform them,|מֽוֹדִיעָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb time|בַּפַּ֣עַם\rb* \rb I will make them know|אוֹדִיעֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb My power|יָדִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and My might;|גְּבֽוּרָתִ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֥י\rb* \rb is the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*[’’]
\c 17
\s1 The Sin and Punishment of Judah
\q1 \v 1 \rb “The sin|חַטַּ֣את\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb is written|כְּתוּבָ֛ה\rb* \rb with an iron|בַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb* \rb stylus,|בְּעֵ֥ט\rb*
\q2 \rb engraved|חֲרוּשָׁה֙\rb* \rb with a diamond|שָׁמִ֑יר\rb* \rb point|בְּצִפֹּ֣רֶן\rb*
\q1 \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tablets|ל֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of their hearts|לִבָּ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and on the horns|וּלְקַרְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of their altars.|מִזְבְּחוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Even their children|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb remember|כִּזְכֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb their altars|מִזְבְּחוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and Asherah poles|וַאֲשֵׁרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the green|רַֽעֲנָ֑ן\rb* \rb trees|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb and on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the high|הַגְּבֹהֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb hills.|גְּבָע֥וֹת\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb O My mountain|הֲרָרִי֙\rb* \rb in the countryside,|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I will give over|אֶתֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb your wealth|חֵילְךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb your treasures|אוֹצְרוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as plunder,|לָבַ֣ז\rb*
\q1 \rb because of the sin|בְּחַטָּ֖את\rb* \rb of your high places,|בָּמֹתֶ֕יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb within all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your borders.|גְּבוּלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb And you yourself will relinquish|וְשָׁמַטְתָּ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the inheritance|מִנַּחֲלָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb you.|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb I will enslave you|וְהַעֲבַדְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your enemies|אֹ֣יְבֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb in a land|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know,|יָדָ֑עְתָּ\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have kindled|אֵ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |קְדַחְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb My anger;|בְּאַפִּ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb it will burn|תּוּקָֽד׃ס\rb* \rb forever.”|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Cursed is|אָר֤וּר\rb* \rb the man|הַגֶּ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb trusts|יִבְטַ֣ח\rb* \rb in mankind,|בָּֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb who makes|וְשָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb mere flesh|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb his strength|זְרֹע֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 17:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa arm\f*
\q2 \rb and turns|יָס֥וּר\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb He will be|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb like a shrub|כְּעַרְעָ֣ר\rb* \rb in the desert;|בָּֽעֲרָבָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb he will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|יִרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb when|כִּי־\rb* \rb prosperity|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb comes.|יָב֣וֹא\rb*
\q1 \rb He will dwell|וְשָׁכַ֤ן\rb* \rb in the parched places|חֲרֵרִים֙\rb* \rb of the desert,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*
\q2 \rb in a salt|מְלֵחָ֖ה\rb* \rb land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb where no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb one lives.|תֵשֵֽׁב׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb But blessed|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb is the man|הַגֶּ֔בֶר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb trusts|יִבְטַ֖ח\rb* \rb in the LORD,|בַּֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb whose confidence|מִבְטַחֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb in Him.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb He is|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb like a tree|כְּעֵ֣ץ׀\rb* \rb planted|שָׁת֣וּל\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֗יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb that sends out its roots|שָֽׁרָשָׁ֔יו\rb*\rb |יְשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb toward|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the stream.|יוּבַל֙\rb*
\q1 \rb It does not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb fear|יִרָא\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the heat|חֹ֔ם\rb* \rb comes,|יָבֹ֣א\rb*
\q2 \rb and its leaves|עָלֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb are always|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb green.|רַֽעֲנָ֑ן\rb*
\q1 \rb It does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb worry|יִדְאָ֔ג\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb in a year|וּבִשְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb of drought,|בַּצֹּ֙רֶת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb nor does it cease|יָמִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to produce|מֵעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb fruit.|פֶּֽרִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb The heart|הַלֵּ֛ב\rb* \rb is deceitful|עָקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb above all things|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and beyond cure.|וְאָנֻ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*
