\p \v 19 \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Go|הָלֹ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and stand|וְעָֽמַדְתָּ֙\rb* \rb at the gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of the people,|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עָם\rb* \rb through which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb go in|יָבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb and out;|יֵ֣צְאוּ\rb* \rb and stand|ב֑וֹ\rb* \rb at all the other|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them,|אֲ֠לֵיהֶם\rb* \rb ‘Hear|שִׁמְע֨וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb O kings|מַלְכֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb all people|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb who enter|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb through these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃ס\rb* \rb gates.|בַּשְּׁעָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 21 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Take heed|הִשָּׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves;|בְּנַפְשֽׁוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb carry|תִּשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb a load|מַשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb or bring it|וַהֲבֵאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb through the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb day.|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \v 22 \rb You must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb carry a load|מַשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb out|תוֹצִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb of your houses|מִבָּֽתֵּיכֶם֙\rb* \rb or do|תַֽעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb day,|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb but you must keep|וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb day holy,|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your forefathers.|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Yet they would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or incline|הִטּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ear,|אָזְנָ֑ם\rb* \rb but they stiffened|וַיַּקְשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their necks|עָרְפָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and would not|לְבִלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb listen|שׁוֹמֵעַ\rb*\rb |וּלְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb or receive|קַ֥חַת\rb* \rb My discipline.|מוּסָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb If,|אִם־\rb* \rb however,|וְ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb you listen carefully|שָׁמֹ֨עַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְע֤וּן\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb says|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and bring|הָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb no|לְבִלְתִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb load|מַשָּׂ֗א\rb* \rb through the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb day,|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְקַדֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb day holy,|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb and do|עֲשֽׂוֹת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb no|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \rb on it,|בֹּה\rb* \v 25 \rb then kings|מְלָכִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb and princes|וְשָׂרִ֡ים\rb* \rb will enter|וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb through the gates|בְשַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֡את\rb* \rb city.|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb They will sit|יֹשְׁבִים֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֨א\rb* \rb of David,|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb riding|רֹכְבִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb in chariots|בָּרֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb and on horses|וּבַסּוּסִ֗ים\rb* \rb with their|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb officials,|וְשָׂ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb along with the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the residents|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָֽעִיר־\rb* \rb will be inhabited|וְיָשְׁבָ֥ה\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb And people will come|וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb from the cities|מֵעָרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְ֠הוּדָה\rb* \rb and the places around|וּמִסְּבִיב֨וֹת\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb from the land|וּמֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* \rb and from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the foothills,|הַשְּׁפֵלָ֤ה\rb*\f + \fr 17:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb the hill country,|הָהָר֙\rb* \rb and|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Negev,|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb bringing|מְבִאִ֛ים\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and sacrifices,|וְזֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb grain offerings|וּמִנְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb and frankincense,|וּלְבוֹנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּמְבִאֵ֥י\rb* \rb and thank offerings|תוֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb listen|תִשְׁמְע֜וּ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb to keep|לְקַדֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb day holy|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb by not|וּלְבִלְתִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb carrying|שְׂאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb a load|מַשָּׂ֗א\rb* \rb while entering|וּבֹ֛א\rb* \rb the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb day,|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb then I will kindle|וְהִצַּ֧תִּי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb an unquenchable|תִכְבֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in its gates|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb to consume|וְאָֽכְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb the citadels|אַרְמְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.’”|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*
\c 18
\s1 The Potter and the Clay
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Go down|וְיָרַדְתָּ֖\rb* \rb at once|ק֥וּם\rb* \rb to the potter’s|הַיּוֹצֵ֑ר\rb* \rb house,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb I will give you|אַשְׁמִֽיעֲךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My message.”|דְּבָרָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So I went down|וָאֵרֵ֖ד\rb* \rb to the potter’s|הַיּוֹצֵ֑ר\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and saw him|וְהִנֵּהוּ\rb* \rb working|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the wheel.|הָאָבְנָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb But the vessel|הַכְּלִ֗י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was shaping|עֹשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb from the clay|בַּחֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb became flawed|וְנִשְׁחַ֣ת\rb* \rb in his|הַיּוֹצֵ֑ר\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֗ב\rb* \rb hand;|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb so he formed|וַֽיַּעֲשֵׂ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb it into another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb vessel,|כְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it seemed|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb best|יָשַׁ֛ר\rb* \rb for him|הַיּוֹצֵ֖ר\rb* \rb to do.|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃פ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֽוֹר׃\rb* \v 6 \rb “O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb can|אוּכַ֨ל\rb* \rb I not|לֹא־\rb* \rb treat|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb potter treats his clay?|הֲכַיּוֹצֵ֨ר\rb* \rb Just|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb like clay|כַחֹ֙מֶר֙\rb* \rb in the potter’s|הַיּוֹצֵ֔ר\rb* \rb hand,|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb so|כֵּן־\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in My hand,|בְּיָדִ֖י\rb* \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb At any time|רֶ֣גַע\rb* \rb I might announce|אֲדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb that|עַל־\rb* \rb a nation|גּ֖וֹי\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb or kingdom|מַמְלָכָ֑ה\rb* \rb will be uprooted,|לִנְת֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb torn down,|וְלִנְת֖וֹץ\rb* \rb and destroyed.|וּֽלְהַאֲבִֽיד׃\rb* \v 8 \rb But if that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֣וֹי\rb* \rb I warned|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb turns|וְשָׁב֙\rb* \rb from its evil,|מֵרָ֣עָת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb then I will relent|וְנִֽחַמְתִּי֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had planned|חָשַׁ֖בְתִּי\rb* \rb to bring.|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And if at another time|וְרֶ֣גַע\rb* \rb I announce|אֲדַבֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb that I will build up|לִבְנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and establish|וְלִנְטֹֽעַ׃\rb* \rb a nation|גּ֖וֹי\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb or kingdom,|מַמְלָכָ֑ה\rb* \v 10 \rb and if it does|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרָעָה\rb* \rb in My sight|בְּעֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb and does not|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb listen|שְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb to My voice,|בְּקוֹלִ֑י\rb* \rb then I will relent|וְנִֽחַמְתִּי֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had intended for it.|אָמַ֖רְתִּי\rb*\rb |לְהֵיטִ֥יב\rb*\rb |אוֹתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb therefore,|נָ֣א\rb* \rb tell|אֱמָר־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the residents|יוֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb am planning|יוֹצֵ֤ר\rb* \rb a disaster|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb for you|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and devising|וְחֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb a plan|מַֽחֲשָׁבָ֑ה\rb* \rb against you.|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Turn|שׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb now,|נָ֗א\rb* \rb each of you,|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb from your evil|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb ways,|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and correct|וְהֵיטִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and deeds.’|וּמַעַלְלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But they will reply,|וְאָמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb ‘It is hopeless.|נוֹאָ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb We will follow|נֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb our own plans,|מַחְשְׁבוֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and each of us|וְאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb will act|נַעֲשֶֽׂה׃ס\rb* \rb according to the stubbornness|שְׁרִר֥וּת\rb* \rb of his evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb heart.’”|לִבּֽוֹ־\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Inquire|שַֽׁאֲלוּ־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb among the nations:|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb has ever heard|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb things like these?|כָּאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*
\q2 \rb Virgin|בְּתוּלַ֖ת\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb has done|עָשְׂתָ֣ה\rb* \rb a most|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb terrible thing.|שַֽׁעֲרֻרִת֙\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb Does the snow|שֶׁ֣לֶג\rb* \rb of Lebanon|לְבָנ֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb ever leave|הֲיַעֲזֹ֥ב\rb* \rb its rocky|מִצּ֛וּר\rb* \rb slopes?|שָׂדַ֖י\rb*
\q1 \rb Or|אִם־\rb* \rb do its cool|קָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֛יִם\rb* \rb flowing|נוֹזְלִֽים׃\rb* \rb from a distance|זָרִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb ever run dry?|יִנָּתְשׁ֗וּ\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb have forgotten Me.|שְׁכֵחֻ֥נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb They burn incense|יְקַטֵּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb to worthless idols|לַשָּׁ֣וְא\rb*
\q2 \rb that make them stumble|וַיַּכְשִׁל֤וּם\rb* \rb in their ways,|בְּדַרְכֵיהֶם֙\rb*
\q1 \rb leaving the ancient|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb roads|שְׁבִילֵ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb to walk|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb on rutted|נְתִיב֔וֹת\rb* \rb bypaths|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb instead of|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb on the highway.|סְלוּלָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb They have made|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָ֛ם\rb* \rb a desolation,|לְשַׁמָּ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb a perpetual|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb object of scorn;|שְׁרוּקַת\rb*
\q1 \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb who pass|עוֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb by|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb will be appalled|יִשֹּׁ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and shake|וְיָנִ֥יד\rb* \rb their heads.|בְּרֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb I will scatter them|אֲפִיצֵ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the enemy|אוֹיֵ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb like the east|קָדִ֥ים\rb* \rb wind.|כְּרֽוּחַ־\rb*
\q1 \rb I will show them|אֶרְאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb My back|עֹ֧רֶף\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb My face|פָנִ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of their calamity.”|אֵידָֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Another Plot against Jeremiah
\r \ref Jeremiah 11:18–23|JER 11:18-23\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb Then some said,|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Come,|לְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb let us make plans|וְנַחְשְׁבָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מַחֲשָׁבוֹת֒\rb* \rb against|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָהוּ֮\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the law|תּוֹרָ֜ה\rb* \rb will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb be lost|תֹאבַ֨ד\rb* \rb to the priest,|מִכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb nor counsel|וְעֵצָה֙\rb* \rb to the wise,|מֵֽחָכָ֔ם\rb* \rb nor an oracle|וְדָבָ֖ר\rb* \rb to the prophet.|מִנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb Come,|לְכוּ֙\rb* \rb let us denounce him|וְנַכֵּ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |בַלָּשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and pay no|וְאַל־\rb* \rb heed|נַקְשִׁ֖יבָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of his words.”|דְּבָרָֽיו׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Attend|הַקְשִׁ֥יבָה\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb O LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Hear|וּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb what my accusers|יְרִיבָֽי׃\rb* \rb are saying!|לְק֥וֹל\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb Should good|טוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb be repaid|הַיְשֻׁלַּ֤ם\rb* \rb with|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb evil?|רָעָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have dug|כָר֥וּ\rb* \rb a pit|שׁוּחָ֖ה\rb* \rb for me.|לְנַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb Remember|זְכֹ֣ר׀\rb* \rb how I stood|עָמְדִ֣י\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb on their behalf,|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb to turn|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your wrath|חֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb from them.|מֵהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Therefore,|לָכֵן֩\rb* \rb hand their children|בְּנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb over|תֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to famine;|לָרָעָ֗ב\rb*
\q2 \rb pour out|וְהַגִּרֵם֮\rb* \rb the power|יְדֵי־\rb* \rb of the sword|חֶרֶב֒\rb* \rb upon them.|עַל־\rb*
\q1 \rb Let their wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb become|וְתִֽהְיֶ֨נָה\rb* \rb childless|שַׁכֻּלוֹת֙\rb* \rb and widowed;|וְאַלְמָנ֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb let their husbands|וְאַ֨נְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |יִֽהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb be slain|הֲרֻ֣גֵי\rb* \rb by disease,|מָ֑וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb their young men|בַּח֣וּרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb struck down|מֻכֵּי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb in battle.|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb Let a cry|זְעָקָה֙\rb* \rb be heard|תִּשָּׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb from their houses|מִבָּ֣תֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You suddenly|פִּתְאֹ֑ם\rb* \rb bring|תָבִ֧יא\rb* \rb raiders|גְּד֖וּד\rb* \rb against them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have dug|כָר֤וּ\rb* \rb a pit|שִׁיחָה\rb* \rb to capture me|לְלָכְדֵ֔נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and have hidden|טָמְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb snares|וּפַחִ֖ים\rb* \rb for my feet.|לְרַגְלָֽי׃\rb*
\b 
