\c 19
\s1 The Broken Jar
\p \v 1 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “Go|הָל֛וֹךְ\rb* \rb and buy|וְקָנִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a clay|חָ֑רֶשׂ\rb* \rb jar|בַקְבֻּ֖ק\rb* \rb from a potter.|יוֹצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Take some of the elders|וּמִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and leaders|וּמִזִּקְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and go|וְיָצָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb out to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Valley|גֵּ֣יא\rb* \rb of Ben-hinnom|בֶן־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb near the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb of the Potsherd|הַחֲרָסוּת\rb* \rb Gate.|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*
\p \rb Proclaim|וְקָרָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I speak|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to you,|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb saying,|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘Hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb O kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and residents|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb I am going to bring|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb such disaster|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the ears|אָזְנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who hear of it|שֹׁמְעָ֖הּ\rb* \rb will ring,|תִּצַּ֥לְנָה\rb* \v 4 \rb because|יַ֣עַן׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have abandoned Me|עֲזָבֻ֗נִי\rb* \rb and made this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb a foreign|וַֽיְנַכְּר֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb place.|הַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb They have burned incense|וַיְקַטְּרוּ־\rb* \rb in this place|בוֹ֙\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb neither they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb nor their fathers|וַאֲבֽוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb nor the kings|וּמַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb have ever|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known.|יְדָע֛וּם\rb* \rb They have filled|וּמָֽלְא֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb with the blood|דַּ֥ם\rb* \rb of the innocent.|נְקִיִּֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb They have built|וּבָנ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb high places|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb to Baal|הַבַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb on which to burn|לִשְׂרֹ֧ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their children|בְּנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb as offerings|עֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb to Baal—|לַבָּ֑עַל\rb*  \rb something|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוִּ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb or mentioned,|דִבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb did it even enter|עָלְתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb My mind.|לִבִּֽי׃פ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִים֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb when this|הַזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֨וֹם\rb* \rb will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb be called|יִקָּרֵא֩\rb* \rb Topheth|הַתֹּ֖פֶת\rb* \rb or the Valley|וְגֵ֣יא\rb* \rb of Ben-hinnom,|בֶן־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּ֑ם\rb* \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the Valley|גֵּ֥יא\rb* \rb of Slaughter.|הַהֲרֵגָֽה׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And in this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will ruin|וּ֠בַקֹּתִי\rb*\f + \fr 19:7 \ft The Hebrew term for \fqa ruin \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa jar\ft ; see verses 1 and 10.\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plans|עֲצַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem.|וִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb I will make them fall|וְהִפַּלְתִּ֤ים\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their enemies,|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by the hands|וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of those who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb their lives,|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their carcasses|נִבְלָתָם֙\rb* \rb as food|לְמַֽאֲכָ֔ל\rb* \rb to the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the beasts|וּלְבֶהֱמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb a desolation|לְשַׁמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and an object of scorn.|וְלִשְׁרֵקָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 19:8 \ft Literally \fqa and a hissing\f* \rb All|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb who pass|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb by|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb will be appalled|יִשֹּׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and will scoff|וְיִשְׁרֹ֖ק\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her wounds.|מַכֹּתֶֽהָ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb I will make them eat|וְהַֽאֲכַלְתִּ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb daughters,|בְּנֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and they will eat|יֹאכֵ֑לוּ\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another’s|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb flesh|בְּשַׂר־\rb* \rb in the siege|בְּמָצוֹר֙\rb* \rb and distress|וּבְמָצ֔וֹק\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb inflicted|יָצִ֧יקוּ\rb* \rb on them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb by their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb who seek|וּמְבַקְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb their lives.’|נַפְשָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then you are to shatter|וְשָׁבַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb the jar|הַבַּקְבֻּ֑ק\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb of the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who accompany|הַהֹלְכִ֖ים\rb* \rb you,|אוֹתָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb and you are to proclaim|וְאָמַרְתָּ֨\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb I will shatter|אֶשְׁבֹּ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb nation|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb and this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city,|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb one shatters|יִשְׁבֹּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a potter’s|הַיּוֹצֵ֔ר\rb* \rb jar|כְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb can|יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb be repaired.|לְהֵרָפֵ֖ה\rb* \rb They will bury the dead|יִקְבְּר֔וּ\rb* \rb in Topheth|וּבְתֹ֣פֶת\rb* \rb until there is no more|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb room|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb to bury them.|לִקְבּֽוֹר׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb This is what|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb I will do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֞ה\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and to its residents,|וּלְיֽוֹשְׁבָ֑יו\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb I will make|וְלָתֵ֛ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb like Topheth.|כְּתֹֽפֶת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb The houses|בָּתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb and the houses|וּבָתֵּי֙\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be|וְהָי֞וּ\rb* \rb defiled|הַטְּמֵאִ֑ים\rb* \rb like that place,|כִּמְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Topheth—|הַתֹּ֖פֶת\rb* \rb all|לְכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the houses|הַבָּתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb whose rooftops|גַּגֹּֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb they burned incense|קִטְּר֜וּ\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and poured out|וְהַסֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb gods.”|לֵאלֹהִ֥ים\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb from Topheth,|מֵֽהַתֹּ֔פֶת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb had sent him|שְׁלָח֧וֹ\rb* \rb to prophesy,|לְהִנָּבֵ֑א\rb* \rb and he stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and proclaimed|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb* \v 15 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am about to bring|מֵבִי\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the villages around it|עָרֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have pronounced|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb against them,|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they have stiffened|הִקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb their necks|עָרְפָּ֔ם\rb* \rb so as not|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to heed|שְׁמ֥וֹעַ\rb* \rb My words.’”|דְּבָרָֽי׃\rb*
\c 20
\s1 Pashhur Persecutes Jeremiah
\p \v 1 \rb When Pashhur|פַּשְׁחוּר֙\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Immer|אִמֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb and the chief|נָגִ֖יד\rb* \rb official|פָקִ֥יד\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb prophesying|נִבָּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb things,|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 2 \rb he|פַשְׁח֔וּר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb had Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb beaten|וַיַּכֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the stocks|הַמַּהְפֶּ֗כֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb at the Upper|הָֽעֶלְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb Gate|בְּשַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִן֙\rb* \rb which was|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb by the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day,|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb when Pashhur|פַשְׁח֛וּר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb released|וַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the stocks,|הַמַּהְפָּ֑כֶת\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb call|קָרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שְׁמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb you Pashhur,|פַשְׁחוּר֙\rb* \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |מָג֥וֹר\rb* \rb Magor-missabib.|מִסָּבִֽיב׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 20:3 \fqa Magor-missabib \ft means \fqa terror on every side \ft or \fqa the man who lives in terror\ft .\f* \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘I will make you|נֹתֶנְךָ֨\rb* \rb a terror|לְמָג֜וֹר\rb* \rb to yourself|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb and to all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb your friends.|אֹהֲבֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb They will fall|וְנָֽפְל֛וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בְּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb before your very eyes.|וְעֵינֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |רֹא֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb And I will hand Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb over to|אֶתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and he will carry them away|וְהִגְלָ֥ם\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶ֖לָה\rb* \rb and put them|וְהִכָּ֥ם\rb* \rb to the sword.|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 5 \rb I will give away|וְנָתַתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wealth|חֹ֙סֶן֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb city—|הָעִ֣יר\rb*  \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its products|יְגִיעָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and valuables,|יְקָרָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the treasures|אוֹצְר֜וֹת\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah—|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb |אֶתֵּן֙\rb* \rb to|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb their enemies.|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb They will plunder them,|וּבְזָזוּם֙\rb* \rb seize them,|וּלְקָח֔וּם\rb* \rb and carry them off|וֶהֱבִיא֖וּם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And you,|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb Pashhur,|פַשְׁח֗וּר\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb who live|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in your house,|בֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb will go|תֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb into captivity.|בַּשֶּׁ֑בִי\rb* \rb You will go|תָּב֗וֹא\rb* \rb to Babylon,|וּבָבֶ֣ל\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb you will die|תָּמוּת֙\rb* \rb and|וְשָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb be buried—|תִּקָּבֵ֔ר\rb*  \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your friends|אֹ֣הֲבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have prophesied|נִבֵּ֥אתָ\rb* \rb these|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb lies.’”|בַּשָּֽׁקֶר׃ס\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah’s Complaint
\q1 \v 7 \rb You have deceived me,|פִּתִּיתַ֤נִי\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and I was deceived.|וָֽאֶפָּ֔ת\rb*
\q2 \rb You have overcome me|חֲזַקְתַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb and prevailed.|וַתּוּכָ֑ל\rb*
\q1 \rb I am|הָיִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb a laughingstock|לִשְׂחוֹק֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long;|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb everyone|כֻּלֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb mocks|לֹעֵ֥ג\rb* \rb me.|לִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb whenever|מִדֵּ֤י\rb* \rb I speak,|אֲדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb I cry out;|אֶזְעָ֔ק\rb*
\q2 \rb I proclaim|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb violence|חָמָ֥ס\rb* \rb and destruction.|וָשֹׁ֖ד\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb has become|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb to me|לִ֛י\rb*
\q2 \rb a reproach|לְחֶרְפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and derision|וּלְקֶ֖לֶס\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb If I say,|וְאָמַרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb “I will not|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb mention Him|אֶזְכְּרֶ֗נּוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb or speak|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb any more|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb in His name,”|בִּשְׁמ֔וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb His message becomes|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a fire|כְּאֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb burning|בֹּעֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb in my heart,|בְלִבִּי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb shut up|עָצֻ֖ר\rb* \rb in my bones,|בְּעַצְמֹתָ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb and I become weary|וְנִלְאֵ֥יתִי\rb* \rb of holding it in,|כַּֽלְכֵ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and I cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb prevail.|אוּכָֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֜עְתִּי\rb* \rb the whispering|דִּבַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of many:|רַבִּים֮\rb*
\q2 \rb “Terror|מָג֣וֹר\rb* \rb is on every side!|מִסָּבִיב֒\rb*
\q2 \rb Report him;|הַגִּ֙ידוּ֙\rb* \rb let us report him!”|וְנַגִּידֶ֔נּוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb All|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb my trusted friends|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |שְׁלוֹמִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb watch for|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb my fall:|צַלְעִ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb “Perhaps|אוּלַ֤י\rb* \rb he will be deceived|יְפֻתֶּה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb so that we may prevail|וְנ֣וּכְלָה\rb* \rb against him|ל֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and take|וְנִקְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb our vengeance|נִקְמָתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb upon him.”|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb But the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb is with me|אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb like a fearsome|עָרִ֔יץ\rb* \rb warrior.|כְּגִבּ֣וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb Therefore,|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb my persecutors|רֹדְפַ֥י\rb* \rb will stumble|יִכָּשְׁל֖וּ\rb* \rb and will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb prevail.|יֻכָ֑לוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb Since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb succeeded,|הִשְׂכִּ֔ילוּ\rb* \rb they will be utterly|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb put to shame,|בֹּ֤שׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb with an everlasting|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb disgrace|כְּלִמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb that will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be forgotten.|תִשָּׁכֵֽחַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb O LORD|וַיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb who examines|בֹּחֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the righteous,|צַדִּ֔יק\rb*
\q2 \rb who sees|רֹאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the heart|כְלָי֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 20:12 \ft Hebrew \fqa kidneys\f* \rb and mind,|וָלֵ֑ב\rb*
\q1 \rb let me see|אֶרְאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb Your vengeance|נִקְמָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb upon them,|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb I have committed|גִּלִּ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my cause.|רִיבִֽי׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Sing|שִׁ֚ירוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD!|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Praise|הַֽלְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD!|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He rescues|הִצִּ֛יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the life|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the needy|אֶבְי֖וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of evildoers.|מְרֵעִֽים׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb Cursed be|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I was born!|יֻלַּ֖דְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb May the day|י֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my mother|אִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb bore me|יְלָדַ֥תְנִי\rb* \rb never|אַל־\rb*\rb |יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb be blessed.|בָרֽוּךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Cursed be|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought|בִּשַּׂ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my father the news,|אָבִי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “A son|זָכָ֑ר\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb is born|יֻֽלַּד־\rb* \rb to you,”|לְךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb bringing him great joy.|שַׂמֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |שִׂמֳּחָֽהוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb May|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb that man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb be|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb like the cities|כֶּֽעָרִ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb overthrew|הָפַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb compassion.|נִחָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb May he hear|וְשָׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb an outcry|זְעָקָה֙\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb and a battle cry|וּתְרוּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb at noon,|צָהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb kill me|מוֹתְתַ֖נִי\rb* \rb in the womb|מֵרָ֑חֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb so that my mother|אִמִּי֙\rb* \rb might have been|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb my grave,|קִבְרִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and her womb|וְרַחְמָ֖הֿ\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb enlarged.|הֲרַ֥ת\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּה֙\rb* \rb did I come out|יָצָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb of the womb|מֵרֶ֣חֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb to see|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb only trouble|עָמָ֖ל\rb* \rb and sorrow,|וְיָג֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and to end|וַיִּכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb my days|יָמָֽי׃פ\rb* \rb in shame?|בְּבֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*
\c 21
\s1 Jerusalem Will Fall to Babylon
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb when King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|בִּשְׁלֹ֨חַ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb Pashhur|פַּשְׁחוּר֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Malchijah|מַלְכִּיָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Maaseiah.|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֛ה\rb* \rb They said,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb inquire|דְּרָשׁ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb on our behalf,|בַעֲדֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb since|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb*\f + \fr 21:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nebuchadrezzar\ft , a variant of \fqa Nebuchadnezzar \ft (king of Babylon), which occurs frequently in Jeremiah. The latter spelling is used throughout Jeremiah for consistency.\f* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb is waging war|נִלְחָ֣ם\rb* \rb against us.|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb Perhaps|אוּלַי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb will perform|יַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb for us|אוֹתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb something like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb His past wonders,|נִפְלְאֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb so that Nebuchadnezzar will withdraw|וְיַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from us.”|מֵעָלֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb But Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb answered,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “You are to tell|תֹאמְרֻ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb that|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \v 4 \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb ‘I will turn|מֵסֵב֮\rb* \rb against you|אֶת־\rb* \rb the weapons|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָה֮\rb* \rb in your hands,|בְּיֶדְכֶם֒\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb are fighting|נִלְחָמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 21:4 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verse 9\f* \rb who besiege|הַצָּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the wall,|לַֽחוֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and I will assemble|וְאָסַפְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb their forces|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the center|תּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb city.|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \v 5 \rb And I Myself|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will fight|וְנִלְחַמְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb against you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֥ד\rb* \rb and a mighty|חֲזָקָ֑ה\rb* \rb arm,|וּבִזְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb with anger,|וּבְאַ֥ף\rb* \rb fury,|וּבְחֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and great|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb wrath.|וּבְקֶ֥צֶף\rb* \v 6 \rb I will strike down|וְהִכֵּיתִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the residents|יֽוֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb city,|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb both man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and beast.|הַבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb They will die|יָמֻֽתוּ׃\rb* \rb in a terrible|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb plague.’|בְּדֶ֥בֶר\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb ‘After that,’|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֣ן\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb ‘I will hand over|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his officers,|עֲבָדָ֣יו׀\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the people|הָעָ֡ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֜את\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֨יר\rb* \rb who survive|הַנִּשְׁאָרִים֩\rb* \rb the plague|הַדֶּ֣בֶר׀\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb and sword|הַחֶ֣רֶב\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb and famine,|הָרָעָ֗ב\rb* \rb to|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and to|וּבְיַד֙\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb their lives.|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb He will put them|וְהִכָּ֣ם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword;|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb he will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb spare|יָח֣וּס\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb show pity|יַחְמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb compassion.’|יְרַחֵֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Furthermore, you are to tell|תֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb I set|נֹתֵן֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you|אֶת־\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of life|הַחַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of death.|הַמָּֽוֶת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Whoever stays|הַיֹּשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֕וּת\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|וּבָרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague,|וּבַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb but whoever goes out|וְהַיּוֹצֵא֩\rb* \rb and surrenders|וְנָפַ֨ל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֜ים\rb* \rb who besiege|הַצָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb you|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb will live;|יִחְיֶה\rb* \rb he will retain|וְהָֽיְתָה־\rb* \rb his|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb life|נַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb like a spoil of war.|לְשָׁלָֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have set|שַׂ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb My face|פָ֠נַי\rb* \rb against this|הַזֹּ֧את\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֨יר\rb* \rb to bring disaster|לְרָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb good,|לְטוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb It will be delivered|תִּנָּתֵ֔ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb who will destroy it|וּשְׂרָפָ֖הּ\rb* \rb with fire.’|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\s1 A Message to the House of David
\p \v 11 \rb Moreover, tell the house|וּלְבֵית֙\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David,|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘Administer|דִּ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb justice every morning,|מִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*\rb |לַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and rescue|וְהַצִּ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb the victim of robbery|גָז֖וּל\rb*
\q1 \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of his oppressor,|עוֹשֵׁ֑ק\rb*
\q2 \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֗י\rb* \rb will go forth|תֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb like fire|כָאֵ֜שׁ\rb*
\q1 \rb and burn|וּבָעֲרָה֙\rb* \rb with no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to extinguish it|מְכַבֶּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb their evil|רֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb deeds.|מַעַלְלֵיהֶם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am against you|אֵלַ֜יִךְ\rb* \rb who dwell|יֹשֶׁ֧בֶת\rb* \rb above the valley,|הָעֵ֛מֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb atop the rocky|צ֥וּר\rb* \rb plateau—|הַמִּישֹׁ֖ר\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD—|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb you who say,|הָאֹֽמְרִים֙\rb* \rb “Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb can come|יֵחַ֣ת\rb* \rb against us?|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can enter|יָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb our dwellings?”|בִּמְעוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb I will punish|וּפָקַדְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb you|עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as your deeds deserve,|כִּפְרִ֥י\rb*\rb |מַעַלְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb I will kindle|וְהִצַּ֤תִּי\rb* \rb a fire|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb in your forest|בְּיַעְרָ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that will consume|וְאָכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb around you.’”|סְבִיבֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*
\c 22
\s1 A Warning to Judah’s Kings
\p \v 1 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “Go down|רֵ֖ד\rb* \rb to the palace|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and proclaim|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb message|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 2 \rb saying,|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘Hear|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb O king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who sits|הַיֹּשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of David—|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and your officials|וַעֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and your people|וְעַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb who enter|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃ס\rb* \rb gates.|בַּשְּׁעָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 3 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Administer|עֲשׂ֤וּ\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּט֙\rb* \rb and righteousness.|וּצְדָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb Rescue|וְהַצִּ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb the victim of robbery|גָז֖וּל\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of his oppressor.|עָשׁ֑וֹק\rb* \rb Do no|אַל־\rb* \rb wrong|תֹּנוּ֙\rb* \rb or violence|תַּחְמֹ֔סוּ\rb* \rb to the foreigner,|וְגֵר֩\rb* \rb the fatherless,|יָת֨וֹם\rb* \rb or the widow.|וְאַלְמָנָ֤ה\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb shed|תִּשְׁפְּכ֖וּ\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֔י\rb* \rb blood|וְדָ֣ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place.|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will indeed carry out|עָשׂוֹ֙\rb*\rb |תַּֽעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb commands,|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb then kings|מְלָכִים֩\rb* \rb who sit|יֹשְׁבִ֨ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb David’s|לְדָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb throne|כִּסְא֗וֹ\rb* \rb will enter|וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb through the gates|בְשַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֡ה\rb* \rb palace|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb riding|רֹֽכְבִים֙\rb* \rb on chariots|בָּרֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb and horses—|וּבַסּוּסִ֔ים\rb*  \rb they|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and their officials|וְעַבְדּוֹ\rb* \rb and their people.|וְעַמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb But if|וְאִם֙\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|תִשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words,|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb then I swear|נִשְׁבַּ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb by Myself,|בִּ֤י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb will become|יִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb a pile of rubble.’”|לְחָרְבָּ֥ה\rb*
\s1 A Warning about the Palace
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית֙\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “You|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb are like Gilead|גִּלְעָ֥ד\rb* \rb to Me,|לִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb like the summit|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of Lebanon;|הַלְּבָנ֑וֹן\rb*
\q1 \rb but I will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb turn you|אֲשִֽׁיתְךָ֙\rb* \rb into a desert,|מִדְבָּ֔ר\rb*
\q2 \rb like cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb that are uninhabited.|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |נוֹשָׁבָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb I will appoint|וְקִדַּשְׁתִּ֥י\rb* \rb destroyers|מַשְׁחִתִ֖ים\rb* \rb against you,|עָלֶ֛יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb with his weapons,|וְכֵלָ֑יו\rb*
\q1 \rb and they will cut down|וְכָֽרְתוּ֙\rb* \rb the choicest|מִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb of your cedars|אֲרָזֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and throw them|וְהִפִּ֖ילוּ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the fire.|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb will pass|וְעָֽבְרוּ֙\rb* \rb by|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and ask|וְאָֽמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb ‘Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֨ה\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb such a thing|כָּ֔כָה\rb* \rb to this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb city?’|לָעִ֥יר\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then people will reply,|וְאָ֣מְר֔וּ\rb* \rb ‘Because|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have forsaken|עָֽזְב֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and have worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֛וּ\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְדֽוּם׃ס\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods.’”|לֵאלֹהִ֥ים\rb*
\s1 A Warning about Shallum
\q1 \v 10 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb weep|תִּבְכּ֣וּ\rb* \rb for him who is dead;|לְמֵ֔ת\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb mourn his loss.|תָּנֻ֖דוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb Weep bitterly|בְּכ֤וּ\rb*\rb |בָכוֹ֙\rb* \rb for him who is exiled,|לַֽהֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he will never|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb return|יָשׁוּב֙\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb*
\q2 \rb to see|וְרָאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his native|מוֹלַדְתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb land.|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb says|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֨ם\rb*\f + \fr 22:11 \fqa Shallum \ft was also called \fqa Jehoahaz\ft .\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah,|יֹאשִׁיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who succeeded|הַמֹּלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb but has gone forth|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place:|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb “He will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb return,|יָשׁ֥וּב\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |עֽוֹד׃\rb* \v 12 \rb but|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb he will die|יָמ֑וּת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in the place|בִּמְק֛וֹם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he was exiled;|הִגְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb he will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb again.”|עֽוֹד׃ס\rb*
