\s1 A Warning to Coniah
\p \v 24 \rb “As surely as I|אָנִי֮\rb* \rb live,”|חַי־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb “even|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you, Coniah|כָּנְיָ֤הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 22:24 \fqa Coniah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; also in verse 28.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהֽוֹיָקִים֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb were|יִהְיֶ֞ה\rb* \rb a signet ring|חוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb My right|יְמִינִ֑י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb hand,|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb I would pull you|אֶתְּקֶֽנְךָּ׃\rb* \rb off.|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \v 25 \rb In fact, I will hand you over|וּנְתַתִּ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb to those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb dread,|יָג֖וֹר\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֛ד\rb* \rb who want to take|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb your life—|נַפְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb* \rb |וּבְיַ֛ד\rb* \rb to Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb and to the Chaldeans.|הַכַּשְׂדִּֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 22:25 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \v 26 \rb I will hurl|וְהֵֽטַלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֗\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb the mother|אִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb gave you birth|יְלָדַ֔תְךָ\rb* \rb into|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb another|אַחֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb land,|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of you were born—|יֻלַּדְתֶּ֖ם\rb*  \rb and there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb you both will die.|תָּמֽוּתוּ׃\rb* \v 27 \rb You will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb return|יָשֽׁוּבוּ׃ס\rb* \rb to|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb for which you|הֵ֛ם\rb* \rb long.”|מְנַשְּׂאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נַפְשָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |לָשׁ֣וּב\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb*
\b 
