\c 23
\s1 David’s Righteous Branch
\p \v 1 \rb “Woe|ה֣וֹי\rb* \rb to the shepherds|רֹעִ֗ים\rb* \rb who destroy|מְאַבְּדִ֧ים\rb* \rb and scatter|וּמְפִצִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb of My pasture!”|מַרְעִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Therefore|לָ֠כֵן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb about|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the shepherds|הָרֹעִים֮\rb* \rb who tend|הָרֹעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people:|עַמִּי֒\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb have scattered|הֲפִצֹתֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִי֙\rb* \rb and driven them away,|וַתַּדִּח֔וּם\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb attended to them.|פְקַדְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will attend|פֹקֵ֧ד\rb* \rb to|עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb you|אֶת־\rb* \rb for the evil|רֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb of your deeds,|מַעַלְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then I Myself|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb will gather|אֲקַבֵּץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of My flock|צֹאנִ֔י\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the lands|הָאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have banished them,|הִדַּ֥חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will return them|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְהֶ֛ן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their pasture,|נְוֵהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb where they will be fruitful|וּפָר֥וּ\rb* \rb and multiply.|וְרָבֽוּ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb I will raise up|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֧י\rb* \rb shepherds|רֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb who will tend them,|וְרָע֑וּם\rb* \rb and they will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֧וֹד\rb* \rb be afraid|יִֽירְא֨וּ\rb* \rb or dismayed,|יֵחַ֛תּוּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb will any go missing,|יִפָּקֵ֖דוּ\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb when I will raise up|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 23:5 \ft Or \fqa up for David’s line\f*
\q2 \rb a righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb* \rb Branch,|צֶ֣מַח\rb*
\q1 \rb and He will reign|וּמָ֤לַךְ\rb* \rb wisely|וְהִשְׂכִּ֔יל\rb* \rb as King|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and will administer|וְעָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the land.|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb In His days|בְּיָמָיו֙\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be saved,|תִּוָּשַׁ֣ע\rb*
\q2 \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will dwell|יִשְׁכֹּ֣ן\rb* \rb securely.|לָבֶ֑טַח\rb*
\q1 \rb And this|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb is His name|שְּׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb by which|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He will be called:|יִקְרְא֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb Our Righteousness.|צִדְקֵֽנוּ׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Tsidqenu\f*
\p \v 7 \rb So|לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb when they will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb say,|יֹ֤אמְרוּ\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites up|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Instead|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they will say,|אִם־\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָה֩\rb* \rb and led|הֵבִ֜יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the descendants|זֶ֨רַע\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb up out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹנָה\rb* \rb and all|וּמִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the other lands|הָֽאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had banished them.’|הִדַּחְתִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Then they will dwell|וְיָשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb once more in|עַל־\rb* \rb their own land.”|אַדְמָתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Lying Prophets
\p \v 9 \rb As for the prophets:|לַנְּבִאִ֞ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb My heart|לִבִּ֣י\rb* \rb is broken|נִשְׁבַּ֧ר\rb* \rb within me,|בְקִרְבִּ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמוֹתַ֔י\rb* \rb tremble.|רָֽחֲפוּ֙\rb*
\q1 \rb I have become|הָיִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb like a drunkard,|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |שִׁכּ֔וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb like a man|וּכְגֶ֖בֶר\rb* \rb overcome|עֲבָ֣רוֹ\rb* \rb by wine,|יָ֑יִן\rb*
\q1 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|וּמִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb His holy|קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb words.|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb is full of|מָלְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb adulterers—|מְנָֽאֲפִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the curse,|אָלָה֙\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb mourns|אָבְלָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and the pastures|נְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wilderness|מִדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb have dried up—|יָבְשׁ֖וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb their course|מְרֽוּצָתָם֙\rb* \rb is|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and their power|וּגְבוּרָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb is misused.|לֹא־\rb*\rb |כֵֽן׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb “For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb both|גַם־\rb* \rb prophet|נָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb and|גַם־\rb* \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb are ungodly;|חָנֵ֑פוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb in My house|בְּבֵיתִ֛י\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb their wickedness,”|רָעָתָ֖ם\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb “Therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb* \rb their path|דַרְכָּ֜ם\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb will become|יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb slick;|כַּחֲלַקְלַקּוֹת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb they will be driven away|יִדַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb into the darkness|בָּֽאֲפֵלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and fall|וְנָ֣פְלוּ\rb* \rb into it.|בָ֑הּ\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will bring|אָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of their punishment,”|פְּקֻדָּתָ֖ם\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb “Among the prophets|וּבִנְבִיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb I saw|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb an offensive thing:|תִפְלָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb They prophesied|הִנַּבְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb by Baal|בַבַּ֔עַל\rb*
\q2 \rb and led My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb* \rb astray.|וַיַּתְע֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb And among the prophets|וּבִנְבִאֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*
\q2 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb a horrible thing:|שַׁעֲרוּרָ֗ה\rb*
\q1 \rb They commit adultery|נָא֞וֹף\rb*
\q2 \rb and walk|וְהָלֹ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in lies.|בַּשֶּׁ֙קֶר֙\rb*
\q1 \rb They strengthen|וְחִזְּקוּ֙\rb* \rb the hands|יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of evildoers,|מְרֵעִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb so that no|לְבִ֨לְתִּי־\rb* \rb one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb turns his back|שָׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb on wickedness.|מֵרָֽעָת֑וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb They are|הָֽיוּ־\rb* \rb all|כֻלָּם֙\rb* \rb like Sodom|כִּסְדֹ֔ם\rb* \rb to Me;|לִ֤י\rb*
\q2 \rb the people of Jerusalem|וְיֹשְׁבֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb are like Gomorrah.”|כַּעֲמֹרָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the prophets:|הַנְּבִאִ֔ים\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “I will feed|מַאֲכִ֤יל\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb wormwood|לַֽעֲנָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and give them poisoned|רֹ֑אשׁ\rb* \rb water|מֵי־\rb* \rb to drink,|וְהִשְׁקִתִ֖ים\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb from the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb ungodliness|חֲנֻפָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb has spread|יָצְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb throughout the land.”|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֞וּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִאִים֙\rb* \rb who prophesy|הַנִּבְּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to you.|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb They are filling you with false hopes.|מַהְבִּלִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb They speak|יְדַבֵּ֔רוּ\rb* \rb visions|חֲז֤וֹן\rb* \rb from their own minds,|לִבָּם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb from the mouth|מִפִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb They keep saying|אֹמְרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אָמוֹר֙\rb* \rb to those who despise Me,|לִֽמְנַאֲצַ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says that|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb you will have|יִֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb peace,’|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb*
\q1 \rb and|אָֽמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb to everyone|וְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb who walks|הֹלֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb in the stubbornness|בִּשְׁרִר֤וּת\rb* \rb of his own heart,|לִבּוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb harm|רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb will come|תָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to you.’|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb which of them|מִ֤י\rb* \rb has stood|עָמַד֙\rb* \rb in the council|בְּס֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb to see|וְיֵ֖רֶא\rb* \rb and hear|וְיִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His word?|דְּבָר֑וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb has given heed|הִקְשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb to His word|דְּבָרִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and obeyed it?|וַיִּשְׁמָֽע׃ס\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the storm|סַעֲרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb has gone out|יָֽצְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb with fury,|חֵמָה֙\rb*
\q1 \rb a whirlwind|מִתְחוֹלֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְסַ֖עַר\rb* \rb swirling down|יָחֽוּל׃\rb*
\q2 \rb upon|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb the heads|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of the wicked.|רְשָׁעִ֖ים\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb The anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb turn back|יָשׁוּב֙\rb*
\q2 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb He has fully accomplished|עֲשֹׂת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb*\rb |הֲקִימ֖וֹ\rb* \rb the purposes|מְזִמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of His heart.|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb In the days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb to come|בְּאַֽחֲרִית֙\rb*
\q2 \rb you will understand|תִּתְבּ֥וֹנְנוּ\rb* \rb this|בָ֖הּ\rb* \rb clearly.|בִּינָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb send|שָׁלַ֥חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these prophets,|הַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb yet they|וְהֵ֣ם\rb* \rb have run with their message;|רָ֑צוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb speak|דִבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb yet they|וְהֵ֥ם\rb* \rb have prophesied.|נִבָּֽאוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb But if|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb they had stood|עָמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb in My council,|בְּסוֹדִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb they would have proclaimed|וְיַשְׁמִ֤עוּ\rb* \rb My words|דְבָרַי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*
\q1 \rb and turned them back|וִֽישִׁבוּם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb from their evil|הָרָ֔ע\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכָּ֣ם\rb* \rb and|וּמֵרֹ֖עַ\rb* \rb deeds.”|מַֽעַלְלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\b 
\p \v 23 \rb “Am I only|אָ֖נִי\rb* \rb a God|הַאֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb nearby,”|מִקָּרֹ֛ב\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb a God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb far away?”|מֵרָחֹֽק׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb “Can|אִם־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb hide|יִסָּתֵ֨ר\rb* \rb in secret places|בַּמִּסְתָּרִ֛ים\rb* \rb where I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see him?”|אֶרְאֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb “Do I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb fill|מָלֵ֖א\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֧יִם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the earth?”|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb “I have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb the sayings|אָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֔ים\rb* \rb who prophesy|הַֽנִּבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb lies|שֶׁ֖קֶר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb in My name:|בִּשְׁמִ֛י\rb* \rb ‘I had a dream!|חָלַ֖מְתִּי\rb* \rb I had a dream!’|חָלָֽמְתִּי׃\rb* \v 26 \rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֗י\rb* \rb will this continue|הֲיֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb in the hearts|בְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of these prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb who prophesy|נִבְּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb falsehood,|הַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb these prophets|וּנְבִיאֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the delusion|תַּרְמִ֥ת\rb* \rb of their own minds?|לִבָּֽם׃\rb* \v 27 \rb They suppose|הַחֹשְׁבִ֗ים\rb* \rb the dreams|בַּחֲל֣וֹמֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they tell|יְסַפְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|לְרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb will make My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb forget|לְהַשְׁכִּ֤יחַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My name,|שְׁמִ֔י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb forgot|שָׁכְח֧וּ\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb through the worship of Baal.|בַּבָּֽעַל׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Let the prophet|הַנָּבִ֞יא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has|אִתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb a dream|חֲלוֹם֙\rb* \rb retell|יְסַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb it,|חֲל֔וֹם\rb* \rb but let him who|וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb has|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb My word|דְּבָרִי֙\rb* \rb speak|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb it|דְּבָרִ֖י\rb* \rb truthfully.|אֱמֶ֑ת\rb* \rb For what|מַה־\rb* \rb is straw|לַתֶּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb compared to|אֶת־\rb* \rb grain?”|הַבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 29 \rb “Is not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb*\rb |כֹ֧ה\rb* \rb My word|דְבָרִ֛י\rb* \rb like fire,”|כָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “and like a hammer|וּכְפַטִּ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb that smashes|יְפֹ֥צֵֽץ\rb* \rb a rock?”|סָֽלַע׃ס\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb “Therefore|לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb behold,”|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “I am against|עַל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb who steal|מְגַנְּבֵ֣י\rb* \rb from one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb words they attribute to Me.”|דְבָרַ֔י\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb “Yes,”|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “I am against|עַל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ם\rb* \rb who wag|הַלֹּקְחִ֣ים\rb* \rb their own tongues|לְשׁוֹנָ֔ם\rb* \rb and proclaim,|וַֽיִּנְאֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb ‘The LORD declares it.’”|נְאֻֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb “Indeed,”|הִ֠נְנִי\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb “I am against|עַֽל־\rb* \rb those who prophesy|נִבְּאֵ֞י\rb* \rb false|שֶׁ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb dreams|חֲלֹמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb and retell them|וַֽיְסַפְּרוּם֙\rb* \rb to lead My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb astray|וַיַּתְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with their reckless|וּבְפַחֲזוּתָ֑ם\rb* \rb lies.|בְּשִׁקְרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb It was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb who sent them|שְׁלַחְתִּ֜ים\rb* \rb or commanded them,|צִוִּיתִ֗ים\rb* \rb and they are of no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb benefit|וְהוֹעֵ֛יל\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb at all|יוֹעִ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people,”|לָֽעָם־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\s1 False Prophecies
\p \v 33 \rb “Now when|וְכִי־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb a prophet|הַנָּבִ֤יא\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb priest|כֹהֵן֙\rb* \rb asks you,|יִשְׁאָלְךָ֩\rb* \rb ‘What|מַה־\rb* \rb is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb of the LORD?’|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאָמַרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb you are to say|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ‘What|מַה־\rb* \rb burden?|מַשָּׂ֔א\rb* \rb I will forsake|וְנָטַשְׁתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.’|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb As for the prophet|וְהַנָּבִ֤יא\rb* \rb or priest|וְהַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb or anyone|וְהָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb claims,|יֹאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb ‘This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb of the LORD,’|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb I will punish|וּפָקַדְתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and his household.|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb each man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb is to say|תֹאמְר֛וּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his friend|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother:|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb ‘What|מֶה־\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb answered?’|עָנָ֣ה\rb* \rb or ‘What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb spoken?’|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \v 36 \rb But refer|תִזְכְּרוּ־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb more|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb to the burden|וּמַשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb each|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb man’s word|דְּבָר֔וֹ\rb* \rb becomes|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb the burden,|הַמַּשָּׂ֗א\rb* \rb so that you pervert|וַהֲפַכְתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb God,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb Thus|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb you are to say|תֹאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet:|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb ‘What|מֶה־\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb answered you?’|עָנָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and ‘What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb spoken?’|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 38 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you claim,|תֹּאמֵרוּ֒\rb* \rb ‘This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb of the LORD,’|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb then|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Because|יַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you have said,|אֲמָרְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb ‘This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb of the LORD,’|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and I specifically told|וָאֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb you not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to make this claim,|תֹאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |מַשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 39 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb I will surely|הִנְנִ֔י\rb* \rb forget|וְנָשִׁ֥יתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |נָשֹׁ֑א\rb* \rb and will cast you|וְנָטַשְׁתִּ֣י\rb* \rb out of|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb My presence,|פָּנָֽי׃\rb* \rb both you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and your fathers.|וְלַאֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \v 40 \rb And I will bring|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb everlasting|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb shame|חֶרְפַּ֣ת\rb* \rb and perpetual|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb humiliation|וּכְלִמּ֣וּת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be forgotten.”|תִשָּׁכֵֽחַ׃ס\rb*
\c 24
\s1 The Good and Bad Figs
\p \v 1 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֡ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had carried away|הַגְל֣וֹת\rb* \rb Jeconiah|יְכָנְיָ֣הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 24:1 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the craftsmen|הֶחָרָ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and metalsmiths|הַמַּסְגֵּר֙\rb* \rb from Jerusalem,|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and had brought them|וַיְבִאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*\f + \fr 24:1 \ft Or \fqa metalsmiths, and had brought them from Jerusalem to Babylon\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb showed me|הִרְאַנִי֮\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb baskets|דּוּדָאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of figs|תְאֵנִ֔ים\rb* \rb placed|מוּעָדִ֕ים\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \v 2 \rb One|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb basket|הַדּ֣וּד\rb* \rb had very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb good|טֹב֣וֹת\rb* \rb figs,|תְּאֵנִים֙\rb* \rb like those that ripen early,|כִּתְאֵנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |הַבַּכֻּר֑וֹת\rb* \rb but the other|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb basket|וְהַדּ֣וּד\rb* \rb contained very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb poor|רָע֣וֹת\rb* \rb figs,|תְּאֵנִים֙\rb* \rb so bad|מֵרֹֽעַ׃ס\rb* \rb they could not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be eaten.|תֵֽאָכַ֖לְנָה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “Jeremiah,”|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb see?”|רֹאֶה֙\rb*
\p \rb “Figs!”|תְּאֵנִ֑ים\rb* \rb I replied.|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb* \rb “The good|הַטֹּבוֹת֙\rb* \rb figs|הַתְּאֵנִ֤ים\rb* \rb are very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb good,|טֹב֣וֹת\rb* \rb but the bad figs|וְהָֽרָעוֹת֙\rb* \rb are very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb bad,|רָע֣וֹת\rb* \rb so bad|מֵרֹֽעַ׃פ\rb* \rb they cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb be eaten.”|תֵאָכַ֖לְנָה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Like these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb good|הַטֹּב֖וֹת\rb* \rb figs,|כַּתְּאֵנִ֥ים\rb* \rb so|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb I regard|אַכִּ֞יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as good|לְטוֹבָֽה׃\rb* \rb the exiles|גָּל֣וּת\rb* \rb from Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have sent away|שִׁלַּ֜חְתִּי\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans.|כַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 24:5 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \v 6 \rb I will keep|וְשַׂמְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My eyes|עֵינִ֤י\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb for good|לְטוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and will return them|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land.|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb I will build them up|וּבְנִיתִים֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb tear them down;|אֶהֱרֹ֔ס\rb* \rb I will plant them|וּנְטַעְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb uproot them.|אֶתּֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּי֩\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb a heart|לֵ֜ב\rb* \rb to know Me,|לָדַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb They will be|וְהָיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people,|לְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and I|וְאָ֣נֹכִ֔י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God,|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they will return|יָשֻׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their heart.|לִבָּֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb But like the bad|הָֽרָע֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb figs,|וְכַתְּאֵנִים֙\rb* \rb so bad|מֵרֹ֑עַ\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb they cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb be eaten,’|תֵאָכַ֖לְנָה\rb*\rb |כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb ‘so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb will I deal with|אֶ֠תֵּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his officials,|שָׂרָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jerusalem—|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb those remaining|הַנִּשְׁאָרִים֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and those living|וְהַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb I will make them|וּנְתַתִּים֙\rb* \rb a horror|לִזְוָעָה\rb* \rb and an offense|לְרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb a disgrace|לְחֶרְפָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and an object of scorn,|וּלְמָשָׁל֙\rb* \rb ridicule,|לִשְׁנִינָ֣ה\rb* \rb and cursing|וְלִקְלָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּקֹמ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb I have banished them.|אַדִּיחֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And I will send|וְשִׁלַּ֣חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against them|בָ֔ם\rb* \rb sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and famine|הָרָעָ֣ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and plague,|הַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they have perished|תֻּמָּם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and their fathers.’”|וְלַאֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 25
\s1 Seventy Years of Captivity
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֞ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the fourth|הָֽרְבִעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|לִיהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb which|הִ֗יא\rb* \rb was the first|הָרִ֣אשֹׁנִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|לִנְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb So|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֜ר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֛ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the residents|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb as follows:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “From|מִן־\rb* \rb the thirteenth|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֡ה\rb* \rb of Josiah|לְיֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amon|אָמוֹן֩\rb* \rb king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb until|וְעַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb this very|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb day—|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb twenty-three|שָׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb years—|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has come|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb and I have spoken|וָאֲדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb again|אַשְׁכֵּ֥ים\rb* \rb and again,|וְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\f + \fr 25:3 \ft Literally \fqa I have spoken to you, rising up early and speaking,\f* \rb but you have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listened.|שְׁמַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb has sent|וְשָׁלַח֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His servants|עֲבָדָ֧יו\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֛ים\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb you|אֶֽת־\rb* \rb again|הַשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb and again,|וְשָׁלֹ֖חַ\rb*\f + \fr 25:4 \ft Literally \fqa to you, rising up early and sending (them),\f* \rb but you have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listened|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb inclined|הִטִּיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb your ear|אָזְנְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to hear.|לִשְׁמֹֽעַ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The prophets told you,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Turn|שֽׁוּבוּ־\rb* \rb now,|נָ֞א\rb* \rb each of you,|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb from your evil|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּמֵרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb deeds,|מַעַלְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and you can dwell|וּשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD has given|נָתַ֧ן\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your fathers|וְלַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |לְמִן־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb ever.|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb follow|תֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb to serve|לְעָבְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and worship|וּלְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb provoke Me to anger|תַכְעִ֤יסוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb with the works|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of your hands.|יְדֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Then I will do you no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb harm.’|אָרַ֖ע\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb ‘But to your own harm,|לְרַ֥ע\rb* \rb you have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listened|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb to Me,’|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb ‘so|לְמַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you have provoked Me to anger|הִכְעִסוּנִי\rb* \rb with the works|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of your hands.’|יְדֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֕ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb ‘Because|יַ֕עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My words,|דְּבָרָֽי׃\rb* \v 9 \rb behold,|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I will summon|שֹׁלֵ֡חַ\rb*\rb |וְלָקַחְתִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the families|מִשְׁפְּח֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the north,|צָפ֜וֹן\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and I will send for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּי֒\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶל֮\rb* \rb whom I will bring|וַהֲבִ֨אֹתִ֜ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb land,|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its residents,|יֹ֣שְׁבֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and against|וְעַ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb surrounding|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb nations.|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb So I will devote them to destruction|וְהַ֣חֲרַמְתִּ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 25:9 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb and make them|וְשַׂמְתִּים֙\rb* \rb an object of horror|לְשַׁמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and contempt,|וְלִשְׁרֵקָ֔ה\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb desolation.|וּלְחָרְב֖וֹת\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Moreover, I will banish|וְהַאֲבַדְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the sounds|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of joy|שָׂשׂוֹן֙\rb* \rb and gladness,|שִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb the voices|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the bride|כַּלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb bridegroom,|חָתָ֖ן\rb*\rb |ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb the sound|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the millstones,|רֵחַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the light|וְא֥וֹר\rb* \rb of the lamp.|נֵֽר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb will become|וְהָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a desolate|לְחָרְבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wasteland,|לְשַׁמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and these|הָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb will serve|וְעָ֨בְד֜וּ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb for seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But when|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֡ה\rb* \rb are complete,|כִמְלֹ֣אות\rb* \rb I will punish|אֶפְקֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֩\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and that|הַה֧וּא\rb* \rb nation,|הַגּ֨וֹי\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans,|כַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 25:12 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \rb for their guilt,|עֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb desolation.|לְשִֽׁמְמ֥וֹת\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb I will bring|וְהֵבֵאיתִי\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֔יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דְּבָרַ֖י\rb* \rb I have pronounced|דִּבַּ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb against it,|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that is written|הַכָּתוּב֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb book,|בַּסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb has prophesied|נִבָּ֥א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations.|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb and great|גְּדוֹלִ֑ים\rb* \rb kings|וּמְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb will enslave|עָֽבְדוּ־\rb* \rb them,|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb and I will repay|וְשִׁלַּמְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb according to their deeds|כְּפָעֳלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and according to the work|וּכְמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of their hands.’”|יְדֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Cup of God’s Wrath
\p \v 15 \rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb This is what|כֹה֩\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֠ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from My hand|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb cup|כּ֨וֹס\rb* \rb of the wine|הַיַּ֧יִן\rb* \rb of wrath,|הַחֵמָ֛ה\rb* \rb and make all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb send|שֹׁלֵ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb drink|וְהִשְׁקִיתָ֤ה\rb* \rb from it.|אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 16 \rb And they will drink|וְשָׁת֕וּ\rb* \rb and stagger|וְהִֽתְגֹּֽעֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb and go out of their minds,|וְהִתְהֹלָ֑לוּ\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the sword|הַחֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb will send|שֹׁלֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb among them.”|בֵּינֹתָֽם׃\rb*
