\s1 A Warning to the Cities of Judah
\p \v 1 \rb At the beginning|בְּרֵאשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb of the reign|מַמְלְכ֛וּת\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb word|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb from the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Stand|עֲמֹד֮\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have commanded|צִוִּיתִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who come|הַבָּאִים֙\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb there.|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb omit|תִּגְרַ֖ע\rb* \rb a word.|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֣י\rb* \rb they will listen|יִשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb and turn—|וְיָשֻׁ֕בוּ\rb* \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb from his evil|הָרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb way of life—|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb so that I may relent|וְנִחַמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb am planning|חֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb to bring|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb upon them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the evil|רֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb of their deeds.|מַעַלְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And you are to tell them|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen|תִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb and walk|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb in My law,|בְּת֣וֹרָתִ֔י\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb before you,|לִפְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and if you do not listen|לִשְׁמֹ֗עַ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets,|הַנְּבִאִ֔ים\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb have sent|שֹׁלֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb again|וְהַשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb and again|וְשָׁלֹ֖חַ\rb*\f + \fr 26:5 \ft Literally \fqa I have sent you, rising up early and sending (them),\f* \rb even though you did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen,|שְׁמַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 6 \rb then I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb like Shiloh,|כְּשִׁלֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will make|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאתָה\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb an object of cursing|לִקְלָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb among all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.’”|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Threatened with Death
\p \v 7 \rb Now the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and prophets|וְהַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֛וּ\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb and as soon as|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb he|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb telling|לְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to say,|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb* \rb and prophets|וְהַנְּבִאִ֛ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb seized him,|וַיִּתְפְּשׂ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb shouting,|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb “You must surely die!|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמֽוּת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb How|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb dare you prophesy|נִבֵּ֨יתָ\rb* \rb in the name|בְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb that|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb will become|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb like Shiloh|כְּשִׁלוֹ֙\rb* \rb and this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb city|וְהָעִ֥יר\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb will be desolate|יוֹשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb and deserted!”|תֶּחֱרַ֖ב\rb*
\p \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקָּהֵ֧ל\rb* \rb against|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When the officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ׀\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb things,|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb they went up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb from the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|מִבֵּית־\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּֽשְׁב֛וּ\rb* \rb there|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|בְּפֶ֥תַח\rb* \rb of the New|הֶחָדָֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb Gate.|שַֽׁעַר־\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb and prophets|וְהַנְּבִאִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “This|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb man|לָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is worthy|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb* \rb of death,|מָ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he has prophesied|נִבָּא֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city,|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have heard|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb with your own ears!”|בְּאָזְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb sent me|שְׁלָחַ֗נִי\rb* \rb to prophesy|לְהִנָּבֵ֞א\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb and against|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have heard.|שְׁמַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb correct|הֵיטִ֤יבוּ\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and deeds,|וּמַ֣עַלְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and obey|וְשִׁמְע֕וּ\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb might relent|וְיִנָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has pronounced|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb against you.|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb As for me,|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb here|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I am in your hands;|בְיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb do|עֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb what you think|בְּעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb is good|כַּטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb and right.|וְכַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \v 15 \rb But|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb know for certain|יָדֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֮\rb* \rb put me to death,|מְמִתִ֣ים\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb will bring|נֹתְנִ֣ים\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֗י\rb* \rb blood|דָ֣ם\rb* \rb upon yourselves,|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb upon|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city,|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb and upon|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb its residents;|יֹשְׁבֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb truly|בֶאֱמֶ֗ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֤נִי\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃ס\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in your hearing.”|בְּאָזְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Spared from Death
\p \v 16 \rb Then the officials|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and prophets,|הַנְּבִיאִ֑ים\rb* \rb “This|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb man|לָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb is not|אֵין־\rb* \rb worthy|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb* \rb of death,|מָ֔וֶת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb he has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֛ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God!”|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Some of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּקֻ֣מוּ\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 18 \rb “Micah|מִיכָיָה\rb* \rb the Moreshite|הַמּ֣וֹרַשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*\rb |הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb prophesied|נִבָּ֔א\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַם֩\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֨ה\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֜ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘Zion|צִיּ֞וֹן\rb* \rb will be plowed|תֵֽחָרֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb like a field,|שָׂדֶ֤ה\rb*
