\q2 \rb and the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb mount|וְהַ֥ר\rb* \rb a wooded|יָֽעַר׃\rb* \rb ridge.’|לְבָמ֥וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 26:18 \ft \ref Micah 3:12|MIC 3:12\ref*\f*
\p \v 19 \rb Did Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb or anyone else|וְכָל־\rb* \rb in Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb put him to death?|הֶהָמֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |הֱ֠מִתֻהוּ\rb* \rb Did Hezekiah not|הֲלֹא֮\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb and seek|וַיְחַל֙\rb* \rb His|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb favor,|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and did not the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb relent|וַיִּנָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had pronounced|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb against them?|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb But we|וַאֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb are about to bring|עֹשִׂ֛ים\rb* \rb great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb harm|רָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb ourselves!”|נַפְשׁוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\s1 The Prophet Uriah
\p \v 20 \rb Now there was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb another man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb prophesying|מִתְנַבֵּא֙\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb from|מִקִּרְיַ֖ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-jearim.|הַיְּעָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb He prophesied|וַיִּנָּבֵ֞א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb and against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb the same things|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb that Jeremiah did.|יִרְמְיָֽהוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 26:20 \ft Literally \fqa according to all the words of Jeremiah\f* \v 21 \rb King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְ֠הוֹיָקִים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his mighty men|גִּבּוֹרָ֤יו\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb officials|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb his words,|דְּבָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to put him to death.|הֲמִית֑וֹ\rb* \rb But when Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb found out about it,|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb he fled|וַיִּבְרַ֖ח\rb* \rb in fear|וַיִּרָ֔א\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֛ים\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to Egypt:|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Elnathan|אֶלְנָתָ֧ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Achbor|עַכְבּ֛וֹר\rb* \rb along with|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb some other men.|וַאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 23 \rb They brought|וַיּוֹצִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and took him|וַיְבִאֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoiakim,|יְהוֹיָקִ֔ים\rb* \rb who had him put|וַיַּכֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to the sword|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb and his body|נִבְלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb thrown|וַיַּשְׁלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the burial place|קִבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the common|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Nevertheless,|אַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan|שָׁפָ֔ן\rb* \rb supported|יַ֚ד\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb so he was not|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb handed over to|תֵּת־\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |בְיַד־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb to be put to death.|לַהֲמִיתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\c 27
\s1 The Yoke of Nebuchadnezzar
\p \v 1 \rb At the beginning|בְּרֵאשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb of the reign|מַמְלֶ֛כֶת\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|יְהוֹיָקִ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 27:1 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac (see also verses 3 and 12, and \ref Jeremiah 28:1|JER 28:1\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Jehoiakim\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאושִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb word|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:1 \ft Most LXX manuscripts do not include this verse.\f* \rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*\v 2 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֔י\rb*
\p \rb “Make|עֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb a yoke|וּמֹט֑וֹת\rb* \rb out of leather straps|מוֹסֵר֖וֹת\rb* \rb and put it|וּנְתַתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your neck.|צַוָּארֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Send|וְשִׁלַּחְתָּם֩\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the kings|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֜וֹם\rb*\rb |מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Moab,|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb Ammon,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Tyre,|צֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Sidon|צִיד֑וֹן\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֤ד\rb* \rb the envoys|מַלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb who have come|הַבָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Give them a message|וְצִוִּיתָ֣\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to relay|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their masters:|אֲדֹֽנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֥ה\rb*\rb |תֹֽאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲדֹֽנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb By My great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb power|בְּכֹחִי֙\rb* \rb and outstretched|הַנְּטוּיָ֑ה\rb* \rb arm,|וּבִזְרוֹעִ֖י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb made|עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the men|הָאָדָ֤ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb beasts|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of it,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and I give it|וּנְתַתִּ֕יהָ\rb* \rb to whom|לַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I please.|יָשַׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָֽי׃\rb* \v 6 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have placed|נָתַ֙תִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb lands|הָאֲרָצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb under the authority|בְּיַ֛ד\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּ֑י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb I have even|וְגַם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb subject|לְעָבְדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb to him.|ל֖וֹ\rb* \v 7 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb will serve him|וְעָבְד֤וּ\rb* \rb and|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and grandson,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb of his own land|אַרְצוֹ֙\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb comes;|בֹּא־\rb* \rb then many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb and great|גְּדֹלִֽים׃\rb* \rb kings|וּמְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb will enslave|וְעָ֤בְדוּ\rb* \rb him.|בוֹ֙\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb |וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb As for the nation|הַגּ֜וֹי\rb* \rb or kingdom|וְהַמַּמְלָכָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb serve|יַעַבְד֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb and does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb place|יִתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its neck|צַוָּאר֔וֹ\rb* \rb under his yoke,|בְּעֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb I will punish|אֶפְקֹ֨ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֤וֹי\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶרֶב֩\rb* \rb and famine|וּבָרָעָ֨ב\rb* \rb and plague,|וּבַדֶּ֜בֶר\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I have destroyed|תֻּמִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb by his hand.|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb But as for you,|וְ֠אַתֶּם\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your prophets,|נְבִיאֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb your diviners,|קֹֽסְמֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb your interpreters of dreams,|חֲלֹמֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb your mediums,|עֹֽנְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb or your sorcerers|כַּשָּׁפֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הֵ֞ם\rb* \rb declare,|אֹמְרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘You will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb serve|תַעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.’|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb prophesy|נִבְּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb a lie|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb that will serve|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb to remove you|הַרְחִ֤יק\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb your land;|אַדְמַתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb I will banish you|וְהִדַּחְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and you will perish.|וַאֲבַדְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb But the nation|וְהַגּ֗וֹי\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb will put|יָבִ֧יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its neck|צַוָּאר֛וֹ\rb* \rb under the yoke|בְּעֹ֥ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and serve him,|וַֽעֲבָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb I will leave|וְהִנַּחְתִּ֤יו\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb its own land,|אַדְמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to cultivate it|וַֽעֲבָדָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and reside|וְיָ֥שַׁב\rb* \rb in it,|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb And to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb I spoke|דִּבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb the same|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb message:|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Put|הָבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your necks|צַוְּארֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb under the yoke|בְּעֹ֣ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon;|בָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb serve|וְעִבְד֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and his people,|וְעַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and live!|וִֽחְיֽוּ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and your people|וְעַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb die|תָמ֙וּתוּ֙\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague,|וּבַדָּ֑בֶר֙\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has decreed|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb any nation|הַגּ֕וֹי\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb serve|יַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon?|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֗ים\rb* \rb who say,|הָאֹמְרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb serve|תַעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,’|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb are prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb a lie.|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \v 15 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb sent them,|שְׁלַחְתִּים֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and yet they|וְהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb are prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb falsely|לַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb in My name;|בִּשְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb therefore|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb I will banish|הַדִּיחִ֤י\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and you will perish—|וַאֲבַדְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb and the prophets|וְהַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb who prophesy|הַֽנִּבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to you.”|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then I said|דִּבַּ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֩\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֨ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּה֮\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your prophets|נְבִֽיאֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb who prophesy|הַֽנִּבְּאִ֤ים\rb* \rb to you,|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Look,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb very soon|מְהֵרָ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the articles|כְלֵ֧י\rb* \rb from the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will be brought back|מוּשָׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb from Babylon.’|מִבָּבֶ֖לָה\rb* \rb They|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb are prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb a lie.|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \v 17 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Serve|עִבְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and live!|וִֽחְי֑וּ\rb* \rb Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb should this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb become|תִֽהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb a ruin?|חָרְבָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are indeed prophets|נְבִאִ֣ים\rb* \rb and|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb with them,|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb let them now|נָא֙\rb* \rb plead with|יִפְגְּעוּ־\rb* \rb the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb that the articles|הַכֵּלִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb in the palace|וּבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem,|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּי־\rb* \rb be taken|בֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pillars,|הָֽעַמֻּדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb the bases,|הַמְּכֹנ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעַל֙\rb* \rb and the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the articles|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb that remain|הַנּוֹתָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb city,|בָּעִ֥יר\rb* \v 20 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶאצַּר֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb take|לְקָחָ֗ם\rb* \rb when he carried|בַּ֠גְלוֹתוֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeconiah|יְכָונְיָ֨ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:20 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֧ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb into exile from Jerusalem|מִירֽוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָּבֶ֑לָה\rb* \rb along with|וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nobles|חֹרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem.|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb* \v 21 \rb Yes,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb that remain|הַנּֽוֹתָרִים֙\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the palace|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem:|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb ‘They will be carried|יוּבָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶ֥לָה\rb* \rb and will remain|יִֽהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb there|וְשָׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb I attend to them again,’|פָּקְדִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb ‘Then I will bring them back|וְהַֽעֲלִיתִים֙\rb* \rb and restore them|וַהֲשִׁ֣יבֹתִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb place.’”|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*
\c 28
\s1 Hananiah’s False Prophecy
\p \v 1 \rb In the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb of that same|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb year,|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb the fourth|הָֽרְבִעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year,|בִּשְׁנַת\rb* \rb near the beginning|בְּרֵאשִׁית֙\rb* \rb of the reign|מַמְלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb of King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָה֩\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Azzur,|עַזּ֨וּר\rb* \rb who was from Gibeon,|מִגִּבְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֡י\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb ‘I have broken|שָׁבַ֞רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the yoke|עֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb |בְּע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb Within two years|שְׁנָתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will restore|מֵשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדנֶאצַּ֤ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb removed|לָקַ֜ח\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb here|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb and carried|וַיְבִיאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \v 4 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will restore|מֵשִׁ֛יב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Jeconiah|יְכָנְיָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 28:4 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְ֠הוּדָה\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the exiles|גָּל֨וּת\rb* \rb from Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb who went|הַבָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to Babylon,’|בָּבֶ֗לָה\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb ‘for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I will break|אֶשְׁבֹּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the yoke|עֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.’”|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |וּלְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb who were standing|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb “Amen!”|אָמֵ֕ן\rb*\rb |הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb said.|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “May the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb do|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb so!|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb fulfill|יָקֵ֤ם\rb* \rb the words|דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have prophesied,|נִבֵּ֗אתָ\rb* \rb and may He restore|לְהָשִׁ֞יב\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֤י\rb* \rb of His|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb house|בֵית־\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb back|אֶל־\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb from Babylon.|מִבָּבֶ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Nevertheless,|אַךְ־\rb* \rb listen|שְׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb now|נָא֙\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb message|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am speaking|דֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb in your hearing|בְּאָזְנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and in the hearing|וּבְאָזְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֗ים\rb* \rb of old|הָֽעוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb preceded|הָי֧וּ\rb*\rb |לְפָנַ֛י\rb* \rb you|מִן־\rb* \rb and me|וּלְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb prophesied|וַיִּנָּ֨בְא֜וּ\rb* \rb war,|לְמִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb disaster,|וּלְרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb and plague|וּלְדָֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb many|רַבּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb lands|אֲרָצ֤וֹת\rb* \rb and great|גְּדֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb kingdoms.|מַמְלָכ֣וֹת\rb* \v 9 \rb As for the prophet|הַנָּבִ֕יא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb prophesies|יִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb peace,|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb only if the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb comes true|בְּבֹא֙\rb* \rb will the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb be recognized|יִוָּדַע֙\rb* \rb as one the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has truly|בֶּאֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \rb sent.”|שְׁלָח֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb the yoke|הַמּוֹטָ֔ה\rb* \rb off|מֵעַ֕ל\rb* \rb the neck|צַוַּ֖אר\rb* \rb of Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb and broke it.|וַֽיִּשְׁבְּרֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֨י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָה֩\rb* \rb proclaimed,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּה֮\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘In this way,|כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb within two years|שְׁנָתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb I will break|אֶשְׁבֹּ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the yoke|עֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻֽכַדְנֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֗ל\rb*\rb |בְּעוֹד֙\rb* \rb off|מֵעַ֕ל\rb* \rb the neck|צַוַּ֖אר\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations.’”|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb At this, Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb on his way.|לְדַרְכּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \v 12 \rb But shortly after|אַ֠חֲרֵי\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had broken|שְׁב֞וֹר\rb* \rb the yoke|הַמּוֹטָ֔ה\rb* \rb off|מֵעַ֗ל\rb* \rb his neck,|צַוַּ֛אר\rb*\rb |יִרְמְיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֑ה\rb* \v 13 \rb “Go|הָלוֹךְ֩\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֜ה\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘You have broken|שָׁבָ֑רְתָּ\rb* \rb a yoke|מוֹטֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of wood,|עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb but in its place|תַחְתֵּיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb you have fashioned|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a yoke|מֹט֥וֹת\rb* \rb of iron.’|בַּרְזֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb ‘I have put|נָתַ֜תִּי\rb* \rb a yoke|עֹ֣ל\rb* \rb of iron|בַּרְזֶ֡ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the neck|צַוַּ֣אר׀\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb to make them serve|לַעֲבֹ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻכַדְנֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and they will serve him.|וַעֲבָדֻ֑הוּ\rb* \rb I have even|וְגַ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb given him control|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb of the beasts|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the field.’”|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִ֛יא\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Hananiah,|חֲנַנְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb “Listen,|שְׁמַֽע־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb Hananiah!|חֲנַנְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb send you,|שְׁלָחֲךָ֣\rb* \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb have persuaded|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb this people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb to trust|הִבְטַ֛חְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb a lie.|שָֽׁקֶר׃\rb* \v 16 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֙\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘I am about to remove you|מְשַֽׁלֵּֽחֲךָ֔\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb will die|מֵ֔ת\rb* \rb this year|הַשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have preached|דִבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb rebellion|סָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.’”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb And in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃פ\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of that very|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb year,|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb died.|וַיָּ֛מָת\rb*
\c 29
\s1 Jeremiah’s Letter to the Exiles
\p \v 1 \rb This|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb is the text|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the letter|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֛ח\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the surviving|יֶ֜תֶר\rb* \rb elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb among the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the prophets,|הַנְּבִיאִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the others|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֛ר\rb* \rb had carried into exile|הֶגְלָ֧ה\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb (This was after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb King|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb Jeconiah,|יְכָנְיָֽה־\rb*\f + \fr 29:2 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \rb the queen mother,|וְהַגְּבִירָ֨ה\rb* \rb the court officials,|וְהַסָּרִיסִ֜ים\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֧ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem,|וִירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb the craftsmen,|וְהֶחָרָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and the metalsmiths|וְהַמַּסְגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb had been exiled|צֵ֣את\rb* \rb from Jerusalem.)|מִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb The letter was entrusted to|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Elasah|אֶלְעָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan|שָׁפָ֔ן\rb* \rb and Gemariah|וּגְמַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah,|חִלְקִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֜ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֛ר\rb* \rb in Babylon.|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*\rb |בָּבֶ֥לָה\rb* \rb It stated:|לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb*
\pmo \v 4 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַ֨גּוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb who were carried away|הִגְלֵ֥יתִי\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon:|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “Build|בְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb houses|בָתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and settle down.|וְשֵׁ֑בוּ\rb* \rb Plant|וְנִטְע֣וּ\rb* \rb gardens|גַנּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and eat|וְאִכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their produce.|פִּרְיָֽן׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Take|קְח֣וּ\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb and have|וְהוֹלִידוּ֮\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and daughters.|וּבָנוֹת֒\rb* \rb Take|וּקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb for your sons|לִבְנֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and give|תְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb your daughters|בְּנֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb in marriage,|לַֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb so that they too may have|וְתֵלַ֖דְנָה\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and daughters.|וּבָנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb Multiply|וּרְבוּ־\rb* \rb there;|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb decrease.|תִּמְעָֽטוּ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Seek|וְדִרְשׁ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the prosperity|שְׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have sent you as exiles.|הִגְלֵ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb Pray|וְהִתְפַּֽלְל֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb on its behalf,|בַעֲדָ֖הּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if it prospers,|בִשְׁלוֹמָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb you too|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will prosper.”|שָׁלֽוֹם׃פ\rb*
\pmo \v 8 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be deceived|יַשִּׁ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb by the prophets|נְבִֽיאֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and diviners|וְקֹֽסְמֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb among you,|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the dreams|חֲלֹמֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you elicit from them.|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |מַחְלְמִֽים׃\rb* \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֛ם\rb* \rb are falsely prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |בְשֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in My name;|בִּשְׁמִ֑י\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb sent them,|שְׁלַחְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 29:9 \ft Some translators close the written portion of this letter later in the chapter.\f*
\p \v 10 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “When|כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |לְפִ֞י\rb* \rb Babylon’s|לְבָבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb are complete,|מְלֹ֧את\rb* \rb I will attend to|אֶפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and confirm|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֤י\rb* \rb My promise|דְּבָרִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַטּ֔וֹב\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to restore|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place.|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \v 11 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֜עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plans|הַמַּחֲשָׁבֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb have|חֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb for you,|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb plans|מַחְשְׁב֤וֹת\rb* \rb to prosper you|שָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to harm you,|לְרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a future|אַחֲרִ֥ית\rb* \rb and a hope.|וְתִקְוָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Then you will call|וּקְרָאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb upon Me|אֹתִי֙\rb* \rb and come|וַֽהֲלַכְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb and pray|וְהִתְפַּלַּלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb and I will listen|וְשָׁמַעְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to you.|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb You will seek|וּבִקַּשְׁתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb and find Me|וּמְצָאתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you search for Me|תִדְרְשֻׁ֖נִי\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart.|לְבַבְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb I will be found|וְנִמְצֵ֣אתִי\rb* \rb by you,|לָכֶם֮\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb and I will restore you|וְשַׁבְתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁבִיתְכֶם\rb*\f + \fr 29:14 \ft Or \fqa restore your fortunes\f* \rb and gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶ֠תְכֶם\rb* \rb from all|מִֽכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֞ם\rb*\rb |וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb and places|הַמְּקוֹמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have banished you,|הִדַּ֧חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb I will restore|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַ֨מָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I sent|הִגְלֵ֥יתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into exile.”|מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Because|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb you may say,|אֲמַרְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has raised up|הֵקִ֨ים\rb* \rb for us|לָ֧נוּ\rb* \rb prophets|נְבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Babylon,”|בָּבֶֽלָה׃ס\rb* \v 16 \rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb who sits|הַיּוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb who remain|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city,|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֕ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|יָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into exile—|בַּגּוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֙\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֙\rb*
\p \rb “I will send|מְשַׁלֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֔ם\rb* \rb sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and famine|הָרָעָ֣ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and plague,|הַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb and I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb like rotten|הַשֹּׁ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb figs,|כַּתְּאֵנִים֙\rb* \rb so bad|מֵרֹֽעַ׃\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb be eaten.|תֵאָכַ֖לְנָה\rb* \v 18 \rb I will pursue|וְרָֽדַפְתִּי֙\rb* \rb them|אַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague.|וּבַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb I will make them|וּנְתַתִּ֨ים\rb* \rb a horror|לִזְוָעָה\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth—|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb a curse,|לְאָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb a desolation,|וּלְשַׁמָּה֙\rb* \rb and an object of scorn|וְלִשְׁרֵקָ֣ה\rb* \rb and reproach|וּלְחֶרְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I banish them.|הִדַּחְתִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb I will do this because|תַּ֛חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb they have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb listened|שָׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb My words,|דְּבָרַ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb which|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb I sent|שָׁלַ֨חְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb again and again|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 29:19 \ft Literally \fqa I sent to them, rising up early and sending (to them)\f* \rb |וְשָׁלֹ֔חַ\rb*\rb through My servants|עֲבָדַ֤י\rb* \rb the prophets.|הַנְּבִאִים֙\rb* \rb And neither have you exiles|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listened,|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb |וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb So hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you exiles|הַ֨גּוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have sent away|שִׁלַּ֥חְתִּי\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃ס\rb* \v 21 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֤ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kolaiah|קֽוֹלָיָה֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Maaseiah,|מַֽעֲשֵׂיָ֔ה\rb* \rb who are prophesying|הַֽנִּבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb lies|שָׁ֑קֶר\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֣י׀\rb* \rb in My name:|בִּשְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb “I will deliver|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb to|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and he will kill them|וְהִכָּ֖ם\rb* \rb before your very eyes.|לְעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Because|וְלֻקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb of them,|מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the exiles|גָּל֣וּת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb are in Babylon|בְּבָבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb will use this curse:|קְלָלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb make|יְשִֽׂמְךָ֤\rb* \rb you like Zedekiah|כְּצִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and Ahab,|וּכְאֶחָ֔ב\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb roasted|קָלָ֥ם\rb* \rb in the fire!’|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb For|יַ֡עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb they have committed|עָשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb an outrage|נְבָלָ֜ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb by committing adultery|וַיְנַֽאֲפוּ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the wives|נְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of their neighbors|רֵֽעֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and speaking|וַיְדַבְּר֨וּ\rb*\rb |דָבָ֤ר\rb* \rb lies|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb in My name,|בִּשְׁמִי֙\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I did not|ל֣וֹא\rb* \rb command them to do.|צִוִּיתִ֑ם\rb* \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am He who knows,|הוּיֹדֵעַ\rb* \rb and I am a witness,|וָעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Message to Shemaiah
\p \v 24 \rb You are to tell|תֹּאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the Nehelamite|הַנֶּחֱלָמִ֖י\rb* \rb that|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 25 \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |יַ֡עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb “In your own name|בְשִׁמְכָ֜ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֩\rb* \rb have sent out|שָׁלַ֨חְתָּ\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Maaseiah,|מַֽעֲשֵׂיָה֙\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the priests.|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb You said to Zephaniah:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*\f + \fr 29:25 \ft Hebrew \fqa You said\ft ; the addressee \fqa Zephaniah \ft is added for clarity.\f*
\pmo \v 26 \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb has appointed|נְתָנְךָ֣\rb* \rb you priest|כֹהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb Jehoiada,|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb to be|לִֽהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb the chief officer|פְּקִדִים֙\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb responsible for any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb madman|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |מְשֻׁגָּ֖ע\rb* \rb who acts like a prophet—|וּמִתְנַבֵּ֑א\rb*  \rb you must put|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb stocks|הַמַּהְפֶּ֖כֶת\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and neck irons.|הַצִּינֹֽק׃\rb* \v 27 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb have you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb rebuked|גָעַ֔רְתָּ\rb* \rb Jeremiah|בְּיִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb of Anathoth,|הָֽעֲנְּתֹתִ֑י\rb* \rb who poses as a prophet|הַמִּתְנַבֵּ֖א\rb* \rb among you?|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 28 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb he has sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb in Babylon,|בָּבֶ֥ל\rb* \rb claiming:|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb Since the exile|הִ֑יא\rb* \rb will be lengthy,|אֲרֻכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb build|בְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb houses|בָתִּים֙\rb* \rb and settle down;|וְשֵׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb plant|וְנִטְע֣וּ\rb* \rb gardens|גַנּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and eat|וְאִכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb their produce.’”|פְּרִיהֶֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb (Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb however, had read|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb letter|הַסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb to|בְּאָזְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet.)|הַנָּבִֽיא׃פ\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 31 \rb “Send|שְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb a message|עַל־\rb* \rb telling|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Nehelamite.|הַנֶּחֱלָמִ֑י\rb* \rb Because|יַ֡עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb has prophesied|נִבָּ֨א\rb* \rb to you—|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb though I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb send him—|שְׁלַחְתִּ֔יו\rb* \rb and has made you trust|וַיַּבְטַ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb a lie,|שָֽׁקֶר׃\rb* \v 32 \rb |לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb ‘I will surely punish|פֹקֵ֜ד\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the Nehelamite|הַנֶּחֱלָמִי֮\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his descendants.|זַרְעוֹ֒\rb* \rb He will have|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb left|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב׀\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb will he see|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the good|בַטּ֛וֹב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will bring|עֹשֶֽׂה־\rb* \rb to My people,|לְעַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has preached|דִבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb rebellion|סָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD.’”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 30
\s1 The Restoration of Israel and Judah
\r \ref Ezekiel 28:25–26|EZK 28:25-26\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb ‘Write|כְּתָב־\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb a book|סֵֽפֶר׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 3 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִים֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb when I will restore|וְ֠שַׁבְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁב֨וּת\rb*\f + \fr 30:3 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of\f* \rb My people|עַמִּ֧י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and Judah,|וִֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb declares|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb I will restore them|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֗ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb to their fathers,|לַאֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and they will possess it.’”|וִֽירֵשֽׁוּהָ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb These|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the words|הַדְּבָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Yes,|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “A cry|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of panic|חֲרָדָ֖ה\rb* \rb is heard—|שָׁמָ֑עְנוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb a cry of terror,|פַּ֖חַד\rb* \rb not|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of peace.|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Ask|שַׁאֲלוּ־\rb* \rb now,|נָ֣א\rb* \rb and see:|וּרְא֔וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Can|אִם־\rb* \rb a male|זָכָ֑ר\rb* \rb give birth?|יֹלֵ֖ד\rb*
\q1 \rb Why then|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb do I see|רָאִ֨יתִי\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb man|גֶּ֜בֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb with his hands|יָדָ֤יו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his stomach|חֲלָצָיו֙\rb* \rb like a woman in labor|כַּיּ֣וֹלֵדָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and every|כָל־\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb turned|וְנֶהֶפְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb pale?|לְיֵרָקֽוֹן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb How|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |גָד֛וֹל\rb* \rb awful|ה֗וֹי\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day will be!|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb None will be|מֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb like it!|כָּמֹ֑הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb It is|הִיא֙\rb* \rb the time|וְעֵֽת־\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|לְיַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb distress,|צָרָ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb but he will be saved|יִוָּשֵֽׁעַ׃\rb* \rb out of it.|וּמִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb |וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb On that|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb day,|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*
\q1 \rb I will break|אֶשְׁבֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb the yoke|עֻלּוֹ֙\rb* \rb off|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their necks|צַוָּארֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and tear off|אֲנַתֵּ֑ק\rb* \rb their bonds,|וּמוֹסְרוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb will strangers|זָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb enslave|יַעַבְדוּ־\rb* \rb them.|ב֥וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb Instead, they will serve|וְעָ֣בְד֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb their king,|מַלְכָּ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will raise up|אָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb for them.|לָהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb As for you,|וְאַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb O Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb My servant,|עַבְדִּ֨י\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,|תִּירָא֩\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהֹוָה֙\rb*
\q1 \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb be dismayed,|תֵּחַ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb O Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb I will surely save you|מוֹשִֽׁיעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb out of a distant place,|מֵֽרָח֔וֹק\rb*
\q2 \rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of their captivity!|שִׁבְיָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb will return|וְשָׁ֧ב\rb* \rb to quiet|וְשָׁקַ֥ט\rb* \rb and ease,|וְשַׁאֲנַ֖ן\rb*
\q2 \rb with no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to make him afraid.|מַחֲרִֽיד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I am|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֥\rb* \rb to save you,|לְהֽוֹשִׁיעֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \rb Though|כִּי֩\rb* \rb I will completely|אֶעֱשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb destroy|כָלָ֜ה\rb* \rb all|בְּכָֽל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I have scattered you,|הֲפִצוֹתִ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb |אַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb completely destroy you.|אֶעֱשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |כָלָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb Yet I will discipline you|וְיִסַּרְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb justly,|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*
\q2 \rb and will by no means|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave you unpunished.”|וְנַקֵּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲנַקֶּֽךָּ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Your injury|לְשִׁבְרֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb is incurable;|אָנ֣וּשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb your wound|מַכָּתֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb is grievous.|נַחְלָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb There is no one|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb to plead your cause,|דָּ֥ן\rb*
\q2 \rb no|דִּינֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb remedy|רְפֻא֥וֹת\rb* \rb for your sores,|לְמָז֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb recovery|תְּעָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb for you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb your lovers|מְאַהֲבַ֣יִךְ\rb* \rb have forgotten|שְׁכֵח֔וּךְ\rb* \rb you;|אוֹתָ֖ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb they no longer|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb seek you,|יִדְרֹ֑שׁוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |מַכַּ֨ת\rb* \rb I have struck you|הִכִּיתִיךְ֙\rb* \rb as an enemy would,|אוֹיֵ֤ב\rb*
\q2 \rb with the discipline|מוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb of someone cruel,|אַכְזָרִ֔י\rb*
\q1 \rb because of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb your great|רֹ֣ב\rb* \rb iniquity|עֲוֺנֵ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and your numerous|עָצְמ֖וּ\rb* \rb sins.|חַטֹּאתָֽיִךְ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Why|מַה־\rb* \rb do you cry out|תִּזְעַק֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb your wound?|שִׁבְרֵ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb Your pain|מַכְאֹבֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb has no cure!|אָנ֖וּשׁ\rb*
\q1 \rb Because of|עַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb your great|רֹ֣ב\rb* \rb iniquity|עֲוֺנֵ֗ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and your numerous|עָֽצְמוּ֙\rb* \rb sins|חַטֹּאתַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb to you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Nevertheless,|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who devour you|אֹכְלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb will be devoured,|יֵאָכֵ֔לוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your adversaries—|צָרַ֥יִךְ\rb* \rb every one of them—|כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb will go off|יֵלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb into exile.|בַּשְּׁבִ֣י\rb*
