\p \v 38 \rb “The days|יָמִ֥יםִָּ֖\rb* \rb are coming,”|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*\f + \fr 31:38 \ft Literally \fqa Behold, the days\ft ; alternate MT reading \fqa Behold, the days are coming\f* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “when this city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb will be rebuilt|וְנִבְנְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb for Me,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the tower|מִמִּגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of Hananel|חֲנַנְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to the Corner|הַפִּנָּֽה׃\rb* \rb Gate.|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \v 39 \rb The measuring|הַמִּדָּה֙\rb* \rb line|קְוֵה\rb* \rb will once again|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb stretch out|וְיָצָ֨א\rb* \rb straight|נֶגְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the hill|גִּבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Gareb|גָּרֵ֑ב\rb* \rb and then turn|וְנָסַ֖ב\rb* \rb toward Goah.|גֹּעָֽתָה׃\rb* \v 40 \rb The whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb valley|הָעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of the dead bodies|הַפְּגָרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb and ashes,|וְהַדֶּ֡שֶׁן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the fields|הַשְּׁרֵמוֹת\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as the Kidron|קִדְר֜וֹן\rb* \rb Valley,|נַ֨חַל\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the corner|פִּנַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of the Horse|הַסּוּסִים֙\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to the east,|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb* \rb will be holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb It will never|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb be uprooted|יִנָּתֵ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb or demolished.”|יֵהָרֵ֛ס\rb*
\c 32
\s1 Jeremiah Buys Hanamel’s Field
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֞ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the tenth|הָעֲשִׂרִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|לְצִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb which|הִ֧יא\rb* \rb was the eighteenth|שְׁמֹנֶֽה־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar.|לִנְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb At that time|וְאָ֗ז\rb* \rb the army|חֵ֚יל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb was besieging|צָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and Jeremiah|וְיִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb imprisoned|כָלוּא֙\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard,|הַמַּטָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb which was|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the palace|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb had imprisoned him,|כְּלָא֔וֹ\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb prophesying|נִבָּ֜א\rb* \rb like this?|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb You claim that|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am about to deliver|נֹתֵ֜ן\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and he will capture it.|וּלְכָדָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Zedekiah|וְצִדְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb escape|יִמָּלֵ֖ט\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans,|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 32:4 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 5, 24, 25, 28, 29, and 43\f* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he will surely be delivered|הִנָּתֹ֤ן\rb*\rb |יִנָּתֵן֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and will speak with him|וְדִבֶּר־\rb* \rb face|פִּ֣יו\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb face|פִּ֔יו\rb* \rb and see him|תִּרְאֶֽינָה׃\rb* \rb eye|וְעֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb to eye.|עֵינוֹ\rb* \v 5 \rb He will take|יוֹלִ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to Babylon,|וּבָבֶ֞ל\rb* \rb where|וְשָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb he will stay|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I attend to|פָּקְדִ֥י\rb* \rb him,|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb If|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb you fight|תִֽלָּחֲמ֛וּ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans,|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb succeed.’”|תַצְלִֽיחוּ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “The word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Behold!|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb Hanamel,|חֲנַמְאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of your uncle|דֹּֽדְךָ֔\rb* \rb Shallum,|שַׁלֻּם֙\rb* \rb is coming|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you to say,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘Buy|קְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my field|שָׂדִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Anathoth,|בַּעֲנָת֔וֹת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb the right|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb of redemption|הַגְּאֻלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to buy it.’|לִקְנֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then, as the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb had said,|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb my cousin|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |דֹּדִ֜י\rb* \rb Hanamel|חֲנַמְאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to me|אֵ֠לַי\rb* \rb in the courtyard|חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַמַּטָּרָה֒\rb* \rb and urged me,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֡י\rb* \rb ‘Please|נָ֠א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb buy|קְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb my field|שָׂדִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Anathoth|בַּעֲנָת֜וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִ֗ין\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you own|לְךָ֞\rb* \rb the right|מִשְׁפַּ֧ט\rb* \rb of inheritance|הַיְרֻשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb and|וּלְךָ֥\rb* \rb redemption.|הַגְּאֻלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Buy it|קְנֵה־\rb* \rb for yourself.’”|לָ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb Then I knew|וָאֵדַ֕ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb this|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb was the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So I bought|וָֽאֶקְנֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb in Anathoth|בַּעֲנָת֑וֹת\rb* \rb from my cousin|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |דֹּדִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Hanamel,|חֲנַמְאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb and I weighed out|וָֽאֶשְׁקֲלָה־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb seventeen|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וַעֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb of silver.|הַכָּֽסֶף׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:9 \fqa 17 shekels \ft is approximately 6.8 ounces or 193.8 grams of silver.\f* \v 10 \rb I signed|וָאֶכְתֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb and sealed|וָֽאֶחְתֹּ֔ם\rb* \rb the deed,|בַּסֵּ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb called in witnesses,|וָאָעֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |עֵדִ֑ים\rb* \rb and weighed out|וָאֶשְׁקֹ֥ל\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb on the scales.|בְּמֹאזְנָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Then I took|וָאֶקַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the deed|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of purchase—|הַמִּקְנָ֑ה\rb* \rb the sealed|הֶֽחָת֛וּם\rb* \rb copy with its terms|הַמִּצְוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and conditions,|וְהַחֻקִּ֖ים\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the open copy—|הַגָּלֽוּי׃\rb* \v 12 \rb and I gave|וָאֶתֵּ֞ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this deed|הַסֵּ֣פֶר\rb*\rb |הַמִּקְנָ֗ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah,|נֵרִיָּה֮\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Mahseiah,|מַחְסֵיָה֒\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb of my cousin|דֹּדִ֔י\rb*\rb |וּלְעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb Hanamel|חֲנַמְאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb and the witnesses|הָֽעֵדִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were signing|הַכֹּתְבִ֖ים\rb* \rb the purchase|הַמִּקְנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לְעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb agreement|בְּסֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb sitting|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the guard.|הַמַּטָּרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb In their sight|לְעֵינֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb I instructed|וָֽאֲצַוֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \v 14 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb Take|לָק֣וֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֡לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb deeds—|הַסְּפָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb both the sealed copy|הֶחָת֗וּם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb and the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb open|הַגָּלוּי֙\rb* \rb copy|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of the|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb deed|סֵפֶר֩\rb* \rb of purchase—|הַמִּקְנָ֨ה\rb* \rb and put them|וּנְתַתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in a clay|חָ֑רֶשׂ\rb* \rb jar|בִּכְלִי־\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb preserve them|יַעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb for a long|רַבִּֽים׃ס\rb* \rb time.|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \v 15 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb Houses,|בָתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb fields,|וְשָׂד֥וֹת\rb* \rb and vineyards|וּכְרָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb will again|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb be bought|יִקָּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּֽאת׃פ\rb* \rb land.”|בָּאָ֥רֶץ\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Prays for Understanding
\p \v 16 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb I had given|תִתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the deed|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of purchase|הַמִּקְנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah,|נֵרִיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb I prayed|וָאֶתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD:|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \v 17 \rb “Oh,|אֲהָהּ֮\rb* \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD!|יְהוִה֒\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have made|עָשִׂ֗יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb by Your great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb power|בְּכֹֽחֲךָ֙\rb* \rb and outstretched|הַנְּטוּיָ֑ה\rb* \rb arm.|וּבִֽזְרֹעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb Nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb is too difficult|יִפָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb for You!|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb You show|עֹ֤שֶׂה\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to thousands|לַֽאֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb but lay|וּמְשַׁלֵּם֙\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of the fathers|אָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the laps|חֵ֥יק\rb*\f + \fr 32:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa into the bosom\f* \rb of their children|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb after them,|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb O great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb and mighty|הַגִּבּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb God|הָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb whose name|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \v 19 \rb the One great|גְּדֹל֙\rb* \rb in counsel|הָֽעֵצָ֔ה\rb* \rb and mighty|וְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb in deed,|הָעֲלִֽילִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |פְקֻח֗וֹת\rb* \rb are on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the ways|דַּרְכֵי֙\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of men,|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb to reward|לָתֵ֤ת\rb* \rb each one|לְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb according to his ways|כִּדְרָכָ֔יו\rb* \rb and according to the fruit|וְכִפְרִ֖י\rb* \rb of his deeds.|מַעֲלָלָֽיו׃\rb*
