\s1 A Promise of Restoration
\r \ref Ezekiel 11:13–21|EZK 11:13-21\ref*)
\p \v 36 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb therefore,|לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֜את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֨יר\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb say,|אֹמְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb ‘It will be delivered|נִתְּנָה֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|וּבָרָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb and plague,’|וּבַדָּֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \v 37 \rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb I will surely gather My people|מְקַבְּצָם֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the lands|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have banished them|הִדַּחְתִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb in My furious anger|בְּאַפִּ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבַחֲמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb and great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb wrath,|וּבְקֶ֣צֶף\rb* \rb and I will return them|וַהֲשִֽׁבֹתִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb and make them dwell|וְהֹשַׁבְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in safety.|לָבֶֽטַח׃\rb* \v 38 \rb They will be|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb My|לִ֖י\rb* \rb people,|לְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God.|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:38 \ft Cited in \ref 2 Corinthians 6:16|2CO 6:16\ref*\f* \v 39 \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb way,|וְדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb so that they will always fear Me|לְיִרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb for their own good|לְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and for the good of their children|וְלִבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb after them.|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 40 \rb I will make|וְכָרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with them:|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb I will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn away|אָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאַ֣חֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb doing good to them,|לְהֵיטִיבִ֖י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and I will put|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb My fear|יִרְאָתִי֙\rb* \rb in their hearts,|בִּלְבָבָ֔ם\rb* \rb so that they will never|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb turn away|ס֥וּר\rb* \rb from Me.|מֵעָלָֽי׃\rb* \v 41 \rb Yes , I will rejoice|וְשַׂשְׂתִּ֥י\rb* \rb in|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb doing them good,|לְהֵטִ֣יב\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will faithfully|בֶּאֱמֶ֔ת\rb* \rb plant them|וּנְטַעְתִּ֞ים\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb land|בָּאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb My heart|לִבִּ֖י\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb My soul.|נַפְשִֽׁי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 42 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have brought|הֵבֵ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb I will|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb bring|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb have promised|דֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb them.|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 43 \rb And fields|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb will be bought|וְנִקְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb about which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are saying,|אֹמְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb ‘It is|הִיא֙\rb* \rb a desolation,|שְׁמָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb without|מֵאֵ֤ין\rb* \rb man|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb or beast;|וּבְהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb it has been delivered|נִתְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans.’|הַכַּשְׂדִּֽים׃\rb* \v 44 \rb Fields|שָׂד֞וֹת\rb* \rb will be purchased|יִקְנ֗וּ\rb* \rb with silver,|בַּכֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and deeds|בַּסֵּ֥פֶר׀\rb* \rb will be signed,|וְכָת֨וֹב\rb* \rb sealed,|וְחָתוֹם֮\rb*\rb |וְהָעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and witnessed|עֵדִים֒\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִ֜ן\rb* \rb in the areas surrounding|וּבִסְבִיבֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb and in the cities|וּבְעָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah—|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb the cities|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the hill country,|הָהָ֔ר\rb*\rb |וּבְעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the foothills,|הַשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 32:44 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Negev—|הַנֶּ֑גֶב\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will restore them|אָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from captivity,|שְׁבוּתָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 32:44 \ft Or \fqa restore their fortunes\f* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*
\c 33
\s1 The Excellence of the Restored Nation
\p \v 1 \rb While Jeremiah|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb was still|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb confined|עָצ֔וּר\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the guard,|הַמַּטָּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb him|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb a second time:|שֵׁנִ֑ית\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Thus|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who made the earth,|עֹשָׂ֑הּ\rb*\f + \fr 33:2 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa who made it\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who formed|יוֹצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb and established it,|לַהֲכִינָ֖הּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb is His name:|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Call|קְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb and I will answer|וְאֶעֱנֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb and show|וְאַגִּ֧ידָה\rb* \rb you|לְּךָ֛\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹל֥וֹת\rb* \rb and unsearchable things|וּבְצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know.|יְדַעְתָּֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the houses|בָּתֵּי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and the palaces|בָּתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb that have been torn down|הַנְּתֻצִ֕ים\rb* \rb for defense against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the siege ramps|הַסֹּלְל֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the sword:|הֶחָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 5 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb The Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb are coming|בָּאִ֗ים\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵם֙\rb*\f + \fr 33:5 \ft Or \fqa They are coming to fight the Chaldeans\ft ; that is, the Babylonians\f* \rb and to fill those places|וּלְמַלְאָם֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the corpses|פִּגְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the men|הָאָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I will strike down|הִכֵּ֥יתִי\rb* \rb in My anger|בְאַפִּ֖י\rb* \rb and in My wrath.|וּבַחֲמָתִ֑י\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have hidden|הִסְתַּ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb My face|פָנַי֙\rb* \rb from this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|מֵהָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb because of|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its wickedness.|רָעָתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Nevertheless,|הִנְנִ֧י\rb* \rb I will bring|מַעֲלֶה־\rb* \rb to it|לָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb health|אֲרֻכָ֥ה\rb* \rb and healing,|וּמַרְפֵּ֖א\rb* \rb and I will heal its people|וּרְפָאתִ֑ים\rb* \rb and reveal|וְגִלֵּיתִ֣י\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the abundance|עֲתֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb and truth.|וֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb I will restore|וַהֲשִֽׁבֹתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and|שְׁב֣וּת\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁב֣וּת\rb*\f + \fr 33:7 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Judah and Israel\f* \rb and will rebuild them|וּבְנִתִ֖ים\rb* \rb as in former times.|כְּבָרִֽאשֹׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And I will cleanse them|וְטִ֣הַרְתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have committed|חָֽטְאוּ־\rb* \rb against Me,|לִ֑י\rb* \rb and will forgive|וְסָלַחְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb all|לְכוֹל\rb*\rb |עֲוֺנֽוֹתֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb their sins|חָֽטְאוּ־\rb* \rb of rebellion|פָּ֥שְׁעוּ\rb* \rb against Me.|בִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So this city will bring|וְהָ֣יְתָה\rb* \rb Me|לִּ֗י\rb* \rb renown,|לְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb joy,|שָׂשׂוֹן֙\rb* \rb praise,|לִתְהִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and glory|וּלְתִפְאֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb before all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb do|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for it.|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb They will tremble|וְרָֽגְז֗וּ\rb* \rb in awe|וּפָחֲד֣וּ\rb* \rb because of|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the goodness|הַטּוֹבָה֙\rb*\rb |וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb prosperity|הַשָּׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will provide|עֹ֥שֶׂה\rb* \rb for it.|לָּֽהּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb In this|הַזֶּה֒\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּקוֹם־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb say|אֹֽמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb is a wasteland|חָרֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb without|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb or|וּמֵאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb beast,|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb that are deserted—|הַֽנְשַׁמּ֗וֹת\rb*  \rb inhabited|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb by neither|וּמֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb nor|וּמֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb beast—|בְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb*  \rb there will be heard|יִשָּׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb again|עוֹד֮\rb* \v 11 \rb the sounds|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of joy|שָׂשׂ֞וֹן\rb* \rb and|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb gladness,|שִׂמְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb the voices|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the bride|כַּלָּה֒\rb* \rb and|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb bridegroom,|חָתָן֮\rb* \rb and the voices|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of those bringing|מְבִאִ֥ים\rb* \rb thank offerings|תּוֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb saying:|אֹמְרִ֡ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘Give thanks|הוֹדוּ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is good;|ט֤וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb endures forever.’|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\p \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will restore|אָשִׁ֧יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁבוּת־\rb*\f + \fr 33:11 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of the land\f* \rb as in former times,|כְּבָרִאשֹׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֒\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֮\rb* \rb In this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb desolate|הֶחָרֵ֛ב\rb* \rb place,|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb without|מֵֽאֵין־\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֥ם\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb or beast,|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and in all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb its cities,|עָרָ֑יו\rb* \rb there will once more|ע֞וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְיֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb pastures|נְוֵ֣ה\rb* \rb for shepherds|רֹעִ֔ים\rb* \rb to rest|מַרְבִּצִ֖ים\rb* \rb their flocks.|צֹֽאן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb In the cities|בְּעָרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the hill country,|הָהָ֜ר\rb*\rb |בְּעָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb the foothills,|הַשְּׁפֵלָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 33:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Negev,|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb in the land|וּבְאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֛ן\rb* \rb and the cities surrounding|וּבִסְבִיבֵ֥י\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and in the cities|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֛אן\rb* \rb will again|עֹ֣ד\rb* \rb pass|תַּעֲבֹ֧רְנָה\rb* \rb under|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the one who counts them,|מוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Covenant with David
\q1 \v 14 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb when I will fulfill|וַהֲקִֽמֹתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gracious|הַטּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb promise|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֛רְתִּי\rb*
\q1 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb In those|הָהֵם֙\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb and at that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb I will cause to sprout|אַצְמִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb a righteous|צְדָקָ֑ה\rb* \rb Branch,|צֶ֣מַח\rb*
\q1 \rb and He will administer|וְעָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb*
\q2 \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the land.|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb In those|הָהֵם֙\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be saved,|תִּוָּשַׁ֣ע\rb*
\q2 \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb will dwell securely,|תִּשְׁכּ֣וֹן\rb*\rb |לָבֶ֑טַח\rb*
\q1 \rb and this|וְזֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is the name|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb by which it will be called:|יִקְרָא־\rb*
\q2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb Our Righteousness.|צִדְקֵֽנוּ׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 33:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Tsidqenu\f*
\p \v 17 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb lack|יִכָּרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb a man|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb to sit|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 18 \rb nor|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb will the priests|וְלַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb who are Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb ever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb fail|יִכָּרֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to have a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb before Me|מִלְּפָנָ֑י\rb* \rb to offer|מַעֲלֶ֨ה\rb* \rb burnt offerings,|עוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb to burn|וּמַקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb grain offerings,|מִנְחָ֛ה\rb* \rb and to present|וְעֹ֥שֶׂה־\rb* \rb sacrifices.”|זֶּ֖בַח\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֽוֹר׃\rb* \v 20 \rb “This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you can break|תָּפֵ֙רוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֣י\rb* \rb with the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with the night,|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb so that day|יֽוֹמָם־\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֖יְלָה\rb* \rb cease|וּלְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to occupy|הֱי֥וֹת\rb* \rb their appointed time,|בְּעִתָּֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb then My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֤י\rb* \rb may also|גַּם־\rb* \rb be broken|תֻפַר֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb and with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My ministers|מְשָׁרְתָֽי׃\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֥ם\rb* \rb who are priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb so that David will not have|מִהְיֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to reign|מֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his throne.|כִּסְא֑וֹ\rb* \v 22 \rb As|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the hosts|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be counted|יִסָּפֵר֙\rb* \rb and as the sand|ח֣וֹל\rb* \rb on the seashore|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be measured,|יִמַּ֖ד\rb* \rb so too|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb will I multiply|אַרְבֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the descendants|זֶ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb and the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֥י\rb* \rb before Me.”|אֹתִֽי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Moreover, the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb “Have you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb noticed|רָאִ֗יתָ\rb* \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb are saying:|דִּבְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has rejected|וַיִּמְאָסֵ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb families|הַמִּשְׁפָּח֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He had chosen’?|בָּחַ֧ר\rb* \rb So they despise|יִנְאָצ֔וּן\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb and no longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb regard them|מִֽהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb as a nation.|גּ֥וֹי\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb* \v 25 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb established|שָֽׂמְתִּי׃\rb* \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with the day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and the night|וָלָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb and the fixed order|חֻקּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb of heaven|שָׁמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and earth,|וָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \v 26 \rb then I would also|גַּם־\rb* \rb reject|אֶמְאַ֗ס\rb* \rb the descendants|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקוֹב֩\rb* \rb and of My servant|עַבְדִּ֜י\rb* \rb David,|וְדָוִ֨ד\rb* \rb so as not to take|מִקַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb from his descendants|מִזַּרְעוֹ֙\rb* \rb rulers|מֹֽשְׁלִ֔ים\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb the descendants|זֶ֥רַע\rb* \rb of Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|יִשְׂחָ֣ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.|וְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will restore them|אָשׁוּב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁבוּתָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 33:26 \ft Or \fqa restore their fortunes\f* \rb and will have compassion on them.”|וְרִחַמְתִּֽים׃ס\rb*
\c 34
\s1 A Prophecy against Zedekiah
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb when Nebuchadnezzar|וּנְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֣ל׀\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his army,|חֵיל֡וֹ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the earthly|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb under his control,|מֶמְשֶׁ֨לֶת\rb*\rb |יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the other nations|הָעַמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb were fighting|נִלְחָמִ֧ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its surrounding cities.|עָרֶ֖יהָ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb The LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb told Jeremiah|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to go|הָלֹךְ֙\rb* \rb and speak|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am about to deliver|נֹתֵ֜ן\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֤יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and he will burn it down.|וּשְׂרָפָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And you yourself|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֚א\rb* \rb escape|תִמָּלֵט֙\rb* \rb his grasp,|מִיָּד֔וֹ\rb* \rb but|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb will surely be captured|תָּפֹ֣שׂ\rb*\rb |תִּתָּפֵ֔שׂ\rb* \rb and delivered|תִּנָּתֵ֑ן\rb* \rb into his hand.|וּבְיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb You will see|תִּרְאֶ֗ינָה\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb* \rb eye|וְֽ֠עֵינֶיךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to eye|עֵינֵ֨י\rb* \rb and speak with him|יְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb face|וּפִ֛יהוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb face;|פִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and you will go|תָּבֽוֹא׃\rb* \rb to Babylon.|וּבָבֶ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Yet|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb hear|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb O Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb concerning you:|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb You will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|תָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb by the sword;|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 5 \rb you will die|תָּמ֗וּת\rb* \rb in peace.|בְּשָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb As spices were burned|וּֽכְמִשְׂרְפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for your fathers,|אֲ֠בוֹתֶיךָ\rb* \rb the former|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֨ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb preceded|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb you,|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb people will burn spices|יִשְׂרְפוּ־\rb* \rb for you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and lament,|יִסְפְּדוּ־\rb* \rb ‘Alas,|וְה֥וֹי\rb* \rb O master!’|אָד֖וֹן\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I Myself|אֲנִֽי־\rb* \rb have spoken|דִבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb this word,|דָבָ֥ר\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb In Jerusalem, then,|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb relayed|וַיְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \v 7 \rb as the army|וְחֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb was fighting|נִלְחָמִים֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעַ֛ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb and the remaining|הַנּֽוֹתָר֑וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah—|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Azekah.|עֲזֵקָ֔ה\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb these were the only|הֵ֗נָּה\rb* \rb fortified|מִבְצָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb remaining|נִשְׁאֲר֛וּ\rb* \rb in Judah.|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*
\s1 Freedom for Hebrew Slaves
\p \v 8 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֡י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb had made|כְּרֹת֩\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֗ית\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to proclaim|לִקְרֹ֥א\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb liberty,|דְּרֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb the word|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \v 9 \rb that each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb should free|לְ֠שַׁלַּח\rb*\rb |חָפְשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb his Hebrew|הָעִבְרִ֥י\rb* \rb slaves,|עַבְדּ֞וֹ\rb* \rb both male and female,|וְהָעִבְרִיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |שִׁפְחָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and no|לְבִלְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֧ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb should hold|עֲבָד־\rb* \rb his fellow|אָחִ֖יהוּ\rb* \rb Jew in bondage.|בִּיהוּדִ֥י\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb into this covenant|בַבְּרִ֗ית\rb* \rb agreed|וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ֩\rb* \rb that they would free|לְ֠שַׁלַּח\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |חָפְשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb their menservants|עַבְדּ֞וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and maidservants|שִׁפְחָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and no longer|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb hold them in bondage.|עֲבָד־\rb*\rb |ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb They obeyed|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb and released them,|וַיְשַׁלֵּֽחוּ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb but later|אַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb they changed their minds|וַיָּשׁ֙וּבוּ֙\rb* \rb and took back|וַיָּשִׁ֗בוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the menservants|הָֽעֲבָדִים֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb maidservants|הַשְּׁפָח֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they had freed,|שִׁלְּח֖וּ\rb*\rb |חָפְשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb and they forced them|וַיַּכְבִּישׁוּם\rb* \rb to become slaves|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb again.|וְלִשְׁפָחֽוֹת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb made|כָּרַ֤תִּֽי\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִית֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your forefathers|אֲב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb when|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb I brought them out|הוֹצִאִ֤י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery,|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Every|מִקֵּ֣ץ\rb* \rb seventh|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb year,|שָׁנִ֡ים\rb* \rb each|אִישׁ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of you must free|תְּֽשַׁלְּח֡וּ\rb* \rb his Hebrew|הָעִבְרִ֜י\rb* \rb brother|אָחִ֨יו\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb has sold himself|יִמָּכֵ֣ר\rb* \rb to you.|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb He may serve|וַעֲבָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb you six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb but then you must let him go|וְשִׁלַּחְתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb free.|חָפְשִׁ֖י\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb But your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֤וּ\rb* \rb or incline|הִטּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ear.|אָזְנָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Recently|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb repented|וַתָּשֻׁ֨בוּ\rb* \rb and did|וַתַּעֲשׂ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what pleased|הַיָּשָׁר֙\rb* \rb Me;|בְּעֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you proclaimed|לִקְרֹ֥א\rb* \rb freedom|דְר֖וֹר\rb* \rb for his neighbor.|לְרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb You made|וַתִּכְרְת֤וּ\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִית֙\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֕יִת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb bears|נִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb My Name.|שְׁמִ֖י\rb*\rb |עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 16 \rb But now you have changed your minds|וַתָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb and profaned|וַתְּחַלְּל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My name.|שְׁמִ֔י\rb* \rb Each of you|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has taken back|וַתָּשִׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb the menservants and maidservants|עַבְדּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שִׁפְחָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you had set|שִׁלַּחְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb at liberty|חָפְשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to go wherever they wanted,|לְנַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and you have again forced|וַתִּכְבְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to be|לִֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb slaves.|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְלִשְׁפָחֽוֹת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Therefore|לָכֵן֮\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb You|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb Me;|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb you have not proclaimed|לִקְרֹ֣א\rb* \rb freedom,|דְר֔וֹר\rb* \rb each man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb for his brother|לְאָחִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and for his neighbor.|לְרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb So now|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I proclaim|קֹרֵא֩\rb* \rb freedom|דְּר֜וֹר\rb* \rb for you,|לָכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD—|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*  \rb freedom to fall|אֶל־\rb* \rb by sword,|הַחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb by|אֶל־\rb* \rb plague,|הַדֶּ֣בֶר\rb* \rb and by|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb famine!|הָרָעָ֔ב\rb* \rb I will make you|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb a horror|לִזְוָעָה\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And those who have transgressed|הָעֹֽבְרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb and have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb fulfilled|הֵקִ֙ימוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the terms|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they made|כָּרְת֖וּ\rb* \rb before Me,|לְפָנָ֑י\rb* \rb I will treat|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb like the calf|הָעֵ֙גֶל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they cut|כָּרְת֣וּ\rb* \rb in two|לִשְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb in order to pass|וַיַּעַבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb its pieces.|בְּתָרָֽיו׃\rb* \v 19 \rb The officials|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb the court officials,|הַסָּֽרִסִים֙\rb* \rb the priests,|וְהַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb who passed|הָעֹ֣בְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֖ין\rb* \rb the pieces|בִּתְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the calf,|הָעֵֽגֶל׃\rb* \v 20 \rb I will deliver|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb their lives.|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Their corpses|נִבְלָתָם֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb food|לְמַֽאֲכָ֔ל\rb* \rb for the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the beasts|וּלְבֶהֱמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will deliver|אֶתֵּן֙\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his officials|שָׂרָ֗יו\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb their lives,|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַד\rb* \rb to the army|חֵ֚יל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb that had withdrawn|הָעֹלִ֖ים\rb* \rb from you.|מֵעֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am going to give the command,|מְצַוֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and I will bring them back|וַהֲשִׁ֨בֹתִ֜ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb city.|הָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb They will fight|וְנִלְחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb against it,|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb capture it,|וּלְכָד֖וּהָ\rb* \rb and burn it down.|וּשְׂרָפֻ֣הָ\rb*\rb |בָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will make|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb a desolation,|שְׁמָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb without|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb inhabitant.”|יֹשֵֽׁב׃פ\rb*
\c 35
\s1 The Obedience of the Rechabites
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֧ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Go|הָלוֹךְ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the Rechabites,|הָרֵכָבִים֒\rb* \rb speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them,|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and bring them|וַהֲבִֽאוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֑וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to offer them a drink|וְהִשְׁקִיתָ֥\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of wine.”|יָֽיִן׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So I took|וָאֶקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jaazaniah|יַאֲזַנְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Habazziniah,|חֲבַצִּנְיָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his sons—|בָּנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the Rechabites—|הָרֵכָבִֽים׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and I brought|וָאָבִ֤א\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a chamber|לִשְׁכַּ֗ת\rb* \rb occupied by the sons|בְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Hanan|חָנָ֥ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Igdaliah,|יִגְדַּלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb This room was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb near|אֵ֙צֶל֙\rb* \rb the chamber|לִשְׁכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the officials,|הַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was above|מִמַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb the chamber|לְלִשְׁכַּ֛ת\rb* \rb of Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֖ם\rb* \rb the doorkeeper.|שֹׁמֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַסַּֽף׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then I set|וָאֶתֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb pitchers|גְּבִעִ֛ים\rb* \rb full|מְלֵאִ֥ים\rb* \rb of wine|יַ֖יִן\rb* \rb and some cups|וְכֹס֑וֹת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the Rechabites,|הָרֵכָבִ֗ים\rb* \rb and I said|וָאֹמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb “Drink|שְׁתוּ־\rb* \rb some wine.”|יָֽיִן׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb “We do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb drink|נִשְׁתֶּה־\rb* \rb wine,”|יָּ֑יִן\rb* \rb they replied,|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb our forefather|אָבִ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb Jonadab|יוֹנָדָ֨ב\rb*\f + \fr 35:6 \fqa Jonadab \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehonadab\ft ; here and throughout this chapter; see \ref 2 Kings 10:15|2KI 10:15\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵכָ֜ב\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb us,|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Neither you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb nor your descendants|וּבְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb are ever to|לֹ֧א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb drink|תִשְׁתּוּ־\rb* \rb wine.|יַ֛יִן\rb* \v 7 \rb Nor are you ever|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to build|תִבְנ֗וּ\rb* \rb a house|וּבַ֣יִת\rb* \rb or|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb sow|תִזְרָ֙עוּ֙\rb* \rb seed|וְזֶ֤רַע\rb* \rb or|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb plant|תִטָּ֔עוּ\rb* \rb a vineyard.|וְכֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb Those things are|יִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb for you.|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Instead,|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb you must live|תֵּֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in tents|בָּאֳהָלִ֤ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your lives,|יְמֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb you may live|תִּֽחְי֜וּ\rb* \rb a long|רַבִּים֙\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb wander.’|גָּרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And we have obeyed|וַנִּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֨וֹל\rb* \rb of our forefather|אָבִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb Jonadab|יְהוֹנָדָ֤ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵכָב֙\rb* \rb in all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he commanded us.|צִוָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb So we have not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb drunk|שְׁתֽוֹת־\rb* \rb wine|יַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our lives—|יָמֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb neither we|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb nor our wives|נָשֵׁ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb nor our sons|בָּנֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and daughters.|וּבְנֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Nor have we|וּלְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb built|בְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb houses|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in which to live,|לְשִׁבְתֵּ֑נוּ\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb and we have not owned|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb any vineyards|וְכֶ֧רֶם\rb* \rb or fields|וְשָׂדֶ֛ה\rb* \rb or crops.|וָזֶ֖רַע\rb* \v 10 \rb But we have lived|וַנֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in tents|בָּֽאֳהָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb and have obeyed|וַנִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb and done|וַנַּ֔עַשׂ\rb* \rb exactly as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb our forefather|אָבִֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb Jonadab|יוֹנָדָ֥ב\rb* \rb commanded us.|צִוָּ֖נוּ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So when|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֮\rb* \rb marched|בַּעֲל֨וֹת\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָרֶץ֒\rb* \rb we said:|וַנֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb ‘Come,|בֹּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb let us go into|וְנָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to escape|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the armies|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 35:11 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f*\rb |וּמִפְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb and the Arameans.’|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb So we have remained|וַנֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.”|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 Judah Rebuked
\p \v 12 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb Go|הָלֹ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb the men|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the residents|וּלְיֽוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem:|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb ‘Will you not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb* \rb accept|תִקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb discipline|מוּסָ֛ר\rb* \rb and obey|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb My words?’|דְּבָרַ֖י\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb The words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jonadab|יְהוֹנָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵ֠כָב\rb* \rb have been carried out.|הוּקַ֡ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֜יו\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to drink|שְׁתֽוֹת־\rb* \rb wine,|יַ֗יִן\rb* \rb and they have not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb drunk it|שָׁתוּ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this very|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they have obeyed|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of their forefather.|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb But I|וְאָ֨נֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb again and again,|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 35:14 \ft Literally \fqa But I have spoken to you, rising up early and speaking,\f* \rb |וְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb and you have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb obeyed Me!|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Again|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ים\rb* \rb and again|וְשָׁלֹ֣חַ׀\rb* \rb I have sent|וָאֶשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 35:15 \ft Literally \fqa Rising up early and sending (you), I have sent you\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets,|הַנְּבִאִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb proclaiming:|לֵאמֹ֡ר\rb* \rb ‘Turn|שֻׁבוּ־\rb* \rb now,|נָ֡א\rb* \rb each of you,|אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb from your wicked|הָרָעָ֜ה\rb* \rb ways,|מִדַּרְכּ֨וֹ\rb* \rb and correct|וְהֵיטִ֣יבוּ\rb* \rb your actions.|מַֽעַלְלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb go after|תֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִים֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb to serve them.|לְעָבְדָ֔ם\rb* \rb Live|וּשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your fathers.’|וְלַאֲבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb But you have not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb inclined|הִטִּיתֶם֙\rb* \rb your ear|אָזְנְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listened|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb to Me.|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 16 \rb Yes,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of Jonadab|יְהוֹנָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵכָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb carried out|הֵקִ֗ימוּ\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb their forefather|אֲבִיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb gave them,|צִוָּ֑ם\rb* \rb but these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people|וְהָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb listened|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to Me.|אֵלָֽי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Therefore|לָ֠כֵן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֨ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנְנִ֧י\rb* \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֣יא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the residents|יֽוֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have pronounced|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb against them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb but they have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb obeyed,|שָׁמֵ֔עוּ\rb* \rb and I have called|וָאֶקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but they have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answered.’”|עָנֽוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the house|וּלְבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb of the Rechabites:|הָרֵכָבִ֜ים\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb ‘Because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of your forefather|אֲבִיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Jonadab|יְהוֹנָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb and have kept|וַֽתִּשְׁמְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and have done|וַֽתַּעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he charged you to do,|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃ס\rb* \v 19 \rb |לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb Jonadab|לְיוֹנָדָ֧ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵכָ֛ב\rb* \rb will never|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb fail to have|יִכָּרֵ֨ת\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb to stand|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb before Me.’”|לְפָנַ֖י\rb*
\c 36
\s1 Jeremiah’s Scroll Read in the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb In the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔ת\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|לִיהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |הָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb word|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \v 2 \rb “Take|קַח־\rb* \rb a scroll|מְגִלַּת־\rb*\rb |סֵפֶר֒\rb* \rb and write|וְכָתַבְתָּ֣\rb* \rb on|אֵלֶ֗יהָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb it all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֧רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb you concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Judah,|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations,|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb from the day|מִיּ֞וֹם\rb* \rb I first spoke|דִּבַּ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb during the reign|מִימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb until today.|וְעַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֤י\rb* \rb when the people|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb hear|יִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the calamity|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb plan|חֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb to bring|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb upon them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb each of them|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb will turn|יָשׁ֗וּבוּ\rb* \rb from his wicked|הָרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb way.|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Then I will forgive|וְסָלַחְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb their iniquity|לַעֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb* \rb and their sin.”|וּלְחַטָּאתָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah,|נֵֽרִיָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and at the dictation|מִפִּ֣י\rb* \rb of Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֜וּךְ\rb* \rb wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֨ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a scroll|מְגִלַּת־\rb*\rb |סֵֽפֶר׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Jeremiah.|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am restricted;|עָצ֔וּר\rb* \rb I cannot|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֔ל\rb* \rb enter|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb so you|אַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb are to go|וּבָאתָ֣\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb on a day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of fasting,|צ֑וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb you are to read|וְקָרָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb from the scroll|בַמְּגִלָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have written|כָּתַֽבְתָּ־\rb* \rb at my dictation.|מִפִּי֩\rb*\rb |וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb Read them|תִּקְרָאֵֽם׃\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb who are coming|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb from their cities.|מֵעָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֞י\rb* \rb they will bring|תִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb their petition|תְּחִנָּתָם֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb one will turn|וְיָשֻׁ֕בוּ\rb* \rb from his wicked|הָרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb way;|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb great are|גָד֤וֹל\rb* \rb the anger|הָאַף֙\rb* \rb and fury|וְהַ֣חֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has pronounced|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb people.”|הָעָ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So Baruch|בָּרוּךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah|נֵ֣רִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֗עַשׂ\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb had commanded him.|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb In the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb he read|לִקְרֹ֥א\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb from the scroll.|בַסֵּ֛פֶר\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb in the ninth|הַתְּשִׁעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fifth|הַ֠חֲמִשִׁית\rb* \rb year|בַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|לִיהוֹיָקִ֨ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb a fast|צ֜וֹם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was proclaimed|קָרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּאִ֛ים\rb* \rb there|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb from the cities|מֵעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \v 10 \rb |יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb From the chamber|בְּלִשְׁכַּ֡ת\rb* \rb of Gemariah|גְּמַרְיָהוּ֩\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan|שָׁפָ֨ן\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֜ר\rb* \rb which was in the upper|הָעֶלְי֗וֹן\rb* \rb courtyard|בֶּחָצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb at the opening|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the New|הֶֽחָדָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb Baruch|בָר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb read|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb from the scroll|בַּסֵּ֛פֶר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah’s Scroll Read in the Palace
\p \v 11 \rb When Micaiah|מִכָ֨יְהוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Gemariah,|גְּמַרְיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַ֠יִּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the scroll,|הַסֵּֽפֶר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb he went down|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the scribe’s|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְהִ֨נֵּה־\rb* \rb chamber|לִשְׁכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּית־\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb were sitting:|יֽוֹשְׁבִ֑ים\rb* \rb Elishama|אֱלִישָׁמָ֣ע\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֡ר\rb* \rb Delaiah|וּדְלָיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shemaiah,|שְׁ֠מַעְיָהוּ\rb* \rb Elnathan|וְאֶלְנָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Achbor,|עַכְבּ֜וֹר\rb* \rb Gemariah|וּגְמַרְיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֛ן\rb* \rb Zedekiah|וְצִדְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hananiah,|חֲנַנְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the other officials.|הַשָּׂרִֽים׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And Micaiah|מִכָ֔יְהוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb reported|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had heard|שָׁמֵ֑עַ\rb* \rb Baruch|בָר֛וּךְ\rb* \rb read|בִּקְרֹ֥א\rb* \rb from the scroll|בַּסֵּ֖פֶר\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֜ים\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלְח֨וּ\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֗וּךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb through Jehudi|יְהוּדִ֡י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,|נְ֠תַנְיָהוּ\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shelemiah,|שֶׁלֶמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Cushi,|כּוּשִׁי֮\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “Bring|קָחֶ֥נָּה\rb*\rb |בְיָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb the scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you read|קָרָ֤אתָ\rb* \rb in|בָּהּ֙\rb* \rb the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and come here.”|וָלֵ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb So Baruch|בָּר֨וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah|נֵרִיָּ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַ֠יִּקַּח\rb*\rb |בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb the scroll|הַמְּגִלָּה֙\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb sit down,”|שֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “and read|וּקְרָאֶ֖נָּה\rb* \rb it in our hearing.”|בְּאָזְנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\p \rb So Baruch|בָר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb read|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb it in their hearing.|בְּאָזְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When they had heard|כְּשָׁמְעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these words,|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb they turned to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb in fear|פָּחֲד֖וּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \rb “Surely we must report|הַגֵּ֤יד\rb*\rb |נַגִּיד֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the king.”|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “Tell|הַגֶּד־\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb now,”|נָ֣א\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb they asked|שָׁאֲל֖וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \rb “how|אֵ֗יךְ\rb* \rb did you write|כָּתַ֛בְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words?|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb Was it at Jeremiah’s dictation?”|מִפִּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb “It was at|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb his dictation,”|מִפִּיו֙\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “He recited|יִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb wrote them|כֹּתֵ֥ב\rb* \rb in ink|בַּדְּיֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the scroll.”|הַסֵּ֖פֶר\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then the officials|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb*\rb |לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jeremiah|וְיִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb must hide yourselves|הִסָּתֵ֖ר\rb* \rb and tell|יֵדַ֖ע\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb where|אֵיפֹ֥ה\rb* \rb you are.”|אַתֶּֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Jehoiakim Burns the Scroll
\p \v 20 \rb So the officials went|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb in the courtyard.|חָצֵ֔רָה\rb* \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb having stored|הִפְקִ֔דוּ\rb* \rb the scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb in the chamber|בְּלִשְׁכַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of Elishama|אֱלִישָׁמָ֣ע\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֑ר\rb* \rb they reported|וַיַּגִּ֙ידוּ֙\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb to|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb Jehudi|יְהוּדִ֗י\rb* \rb to get|לָקַ֙חַת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the scroll,|הַמְּגִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and he took it|וַיִּ֨קָּחֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb from the chamber|מִלִּשְׁכַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of Elishama|אֱלִישָׁמָ֣ע\rb* \rb the scribe.|הַסֹּפֵ֑ר\rb* \rb And Jehudi|יְהוּדִי֙\rb* \rb read it|וַיִּקְרָאֶ֤הָ\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וּבְאָזְנֵי֙\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were standing|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb him.|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Since it was the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the king|וְהַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in his winter|הַחֹ֔רֶף\rb* \rb quarters|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb with a fire|הָאָ֖ח\rb* \rb burning|מְבֹעָֽרֶת׃\rb* \rb before him.|לְפָנָ֥יו\rb* \v 23 \rb And|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb as soon as Jehudi|יְהוּדִ֗י\rb* \rb had read|כִּקְר֣וֹא\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb or four|וְאַרְבָּעָה֒\rb* \rb columns,|דְּלָתוֹת֮\rb* \rb Jehoiakim would cut them off|יִֽקְרָעֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb with a scribe’s|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb knife|בְּתַ֣עַר\rb* \rb and throw them|וְהַשְׁלֵ֕ךְ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the firepot,|הָאָ֑ח\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb had been consumed|תֹּם֙\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the fire.|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הָאָֽח׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Yet in hearing|הַשֹּׁ֣מְעִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words,|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb become frightened|פָחֲד֔וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or tear|קָרְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their garments.|בִּגְדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \v 25 \rb Even though|וְגַם֩\rb* \rb Elnathan,|אֶלְנָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb Delaiah,|וּדְלָיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb and Gemariah|וּגְמַרְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb urged|הִפְגִּ֣עוּ\rb* \rb the king|בַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb to burn|שְׂרֹ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the scroll,|הַמְּגִלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Instead, the king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb Jerahmeel,|יְרַחְמְאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb a son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the king,|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Seraiah|שְׂרָיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Azriel|עַזְרִיאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Shelemiah|שֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Abdeel,|עַבְדְּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to seize|לָקַ֙חַת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet.|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb But the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb had hidden them.|וַיַּסְתִּרֵ֖ם\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Rewrites the Scroll
\p \v 27 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had burned|שְׂרֹ֣ף\rb* \rb the scroll|הַמְּגִלָּה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb containing the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֛וּךְ\rb* \rb had written|כָּתַ֥ב\rb* \rb at Jeremiah’s|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb dictation,|מִפִּ֥י\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah:|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 28 \rb “Take|קַח־\rb* \rb another|אַחֶ֑רֶת\rb* \rb scroll|מְגִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb rewrite|וּכְתֹ֣ב\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֗יהָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the very words|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were|הָי֗וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the original|הָרִ֣אשֹׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb scroll,|הַמְּגִלָּה֙\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb has burned.|שָׂרַ֖ף\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb You are to proclaim|תֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb concerning|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֤ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb You|אַ֠תָּה\rb* \rb have burned|שָׂרַ֜פְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Why|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb have you written|כָּתַ֨בְתָּ\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb that|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb would surely come|בֹּֽא־\rb*\rb |יָב֤וֹא\rb* \rb and destroy|וְהִשְׁחִית֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and deprive it|וְהִשְׁבִּ֥ית\rb* \rb of|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast?’|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהֽוֹיָקִים֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb He will have|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb one to sit|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb throne,|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb and his body|וְנִבְלָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb thrown out|מֻשְׁלֶ֔כֶת\rb* \rb and exposed to heat|לַחֹ֥רֶב\rb* \rb by day|בַּיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb and frost|וְלַקֶּ֥רַח\rb* \rb by night.|בַּלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb* \v 31 \rb I will punish|וּפָקַדְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb him|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his descendants|זַרְע֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for their iniquity.|עֲוֺנָ֑ם\rb* \rb I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֣י\rb* \rb on them,|עֲ֠לֵיהֶם\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the residents|יֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb and on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the calamity|הָרָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb about which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I warned them|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen.”|שָׁמֵֽעוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb Then Jeremiah|וְיִרְמְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֣ח׀\rb* \rb another|אַחֶ֗רֶת\rb* \rb scroll|מְגִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and gave|וַֽיִּתְּנָהּ֮\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵר֒\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah,|נֵרִיָּהוּ֮\rb* \rb and at Jeremiah’s|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb dictation|מִפִּ֣י\rb* \rb he wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the scroll|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb had burned|שָׂרַ֛ף\rb* \rb in the fire.|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb And many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |כָּהֵֽמָּה׃ס\rb* \rb similar|וְע֨וֹד\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb were added|נוֹסַ֧ף\rb* \rb to them.|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*
\c 37
\s1 Jeremiah Warns Zedekiah
\p \v 1 \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb made Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹֽאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb the king|הִמְלִ֛יךְ\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb and he reigned|וַיִּ֨מְלָךְ־\rb*\rb |מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֗חַת\rb* \rb of Coniah|כָּנְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 37:1 \fqa Coniah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft .\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim.|יְה֣וֹיָקִ֔ים\rb* \v 2 \rb But he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and his officers|וַעֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and the people|וְעַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to obey|שָׁמַ֛ע\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet.|הַנָּבִֽיא׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Yet King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb Jehucal|יְהוּכַ֣ל\rb*\f + \fr 37:3 \fqa Jehucal \ft is a variant of \fqa Jucal\ft ; see \ref Jeremiah 38:1|JER 38:1\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shelemiah|שֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Maaseiah,|מַֽעֲשֵׂיָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb with the message,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb pray|הִתְפַּלֶּל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb for us!”|בַעֲדֵ֔נוּ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Now Jeremiah|וְיִרְמְיָ֕הוּ\rb* \rb was free to come|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb and go|וְיֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb for they had not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb yet put|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in prison.|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַכְּלִיא׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb army|וְחֵ֥יל\rb* \rb had left|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and when the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֜ים\rb*\f + \fr 37:5 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 8, 9, 13, and 14\f* \rb who were besieging|הַצָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֨וּ\rb* \rb the report,|שִׁמְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb they withdrew|וַיֵּ֣עָל֔וּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet:|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 7 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb that|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb you are to tell|תֹֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who sent|הַשֹּׁלֵ֧חַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to|לְדָרְשֵׁ֑נִי\rb* \rb Me:|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb army,|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb which has marched out|הַיֹּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to help|לְעֶזְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb you,|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb will go back|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb to its own land|לְאַרְצ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb will return|וְשָׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb and fight|וְנִלְחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city.|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb They will capture|וּלְכָדֻ֖הָ\rb* \rb it and burn it down.|וּשְׂרָפֻ֥הָ\rb*\rb |בָאֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb deceive|תַּשִּׁ֤אוּ\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹֽׁתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb by saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb* \rb will go away for good,’|הָלֹ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |יֵלְכ֥וּ\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb they will not!|לֹ֖א\rb*\rb |יֵלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Indeed,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you were to strike down|הִכִּיתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵ֤יל\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּים֙\rb* \rb that is fighting|הַנִּלְחָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb against you,|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and only wounded|מְדֻקָּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb remained|וְנִ֨שְׁאֲרוּ\rb*\rb |בָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb in their tents,|בְּאָהֳלוֹ֙\rb* \rb they would still get up|יָק֔וּמוּ\rb* \rb and burn this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb down.”|וְשָֽׂרְפ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Imprisoned
\p \v 11 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When the Chaldean|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb army|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb withdrew|בְּהֵֽעָלוֹת֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb for fear|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹֽה׃ס\rb* \rb army,|חֵ֥יל\rb* \v 12 \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb started to leave|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb to claim his portion|לַחֲלִ֥ק\rb* \rb there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 37:12 \ft Literally \fqa to divide from there\f* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb But when he|ה֞וּא\rb* \rb reached|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb the Gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* \rb the captain|בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb of the guard,|פְּקִדֻ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb whose name|וּשְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb was Irijah|יִרְאִיָּ֔יה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shelemiah,|שֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hananiah,|חֲנַנְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb seized|וַיִּתְפֹּ֞שׂ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb him|יִרְמְיָ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb and said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are deserting|נֹפֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans!”|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb “That is a lie,”|שֶׁ֗קֶר\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “I am not|אֵינֶ֤נִּי\rb* \rb deserting|נֹפֵל֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans!”|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*
\p \rb But Irijah|יִרְאִיָּיה֙\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to him;|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb instead, he arrested|וַיִּתְפֹּ֤שׂ\rb* \rb Jeremiah|בְּיִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and took him|וַיְבִאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officials.|הַשָּׂרִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb The officials|הַשָּׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb were angry|וַיִּקְצְפ֧וּ\rb* \rb with|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and they beat|וְהִכּ֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and placed|וְנָתְנ֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb in jail|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הָאֵס֗וּר\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb it had been made|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb into a prison.|לְבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַכֶּֽלֶא׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb So|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb went|בָ֧א\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a cell|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַבּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb in|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the dungeon|הַֽחֲנֻ֑יוֹת\rb* \rb and remained|וַיֵּֽשֶׁב־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb a long time.|רַבִּֽים׃פ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֥ים\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Later, King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb sent for Jeremiah|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb and received him|וַיִּקָּחֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb in his palace,|בְּבֵיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb where he asked him|וַיִּשְׁאָלֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb privately,|בַּסֵּ֔תֶר\rb* \rb “Is there|הֲיֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD?”|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb “There is,”|יֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “You will be delivered|תִּנָּתֵֽן׃ס\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon.”|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah,|צִדְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb “How|מֶה֩\rb* \rb have I sinned|חָטָ֨אתִֽי\rb* \rb against you|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb or your servants|וְלַעֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb or these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people,|וְלָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have put|נְתַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb prison?|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַכֶּֽלֶא׃\rb* \v 19 \rb Where|וְאַיּוֹ\rb* \rb are your prophets|נְבִ֣יאֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb prophesied|נִבְּא֥וּ\rb* \rb to you,|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb claiming,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֤א\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb or this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb land’|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* ? \v 20 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb listen,|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb O my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb May my petition|תְחִנָּתִי֙\rb* \rb come|תִּפָּל־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb before you.|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb send me back|תְּשִׁבֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb I will die|אָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb there.”|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיְצַוֶּ֞ה\rb* \rb for Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָהוּ֮\rb* \rb to be placed|וַיַּפְקִ֣דוּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַמַּטָּרָה֒\rb* \rb and given|וְנָתֹן֩\rb* \rb a loaf|כִכַּר־\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb daily|לַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the street|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb of the bakers,|הָאֹפִ֔ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the bread|הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb was gone.|תֹּ֥ם\rb* \rb So Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the guard.|הַמַּטָּרָֽה׃\rb*
\c 38
\s1 Jeremiah Cast into the Cistern
\p \v 1 \rb Now Shephatiah|שְׁפַטְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Mattan,|מַתָּ֗ן\rb* \rb Gedaliah|וּגְדַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Pashhur,|פַּשְׁח֔וּר\rb* \rb Jucal|וְיוּכַל֙\rb*\f + \fr 38:1 \fqa Jucal \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehucal\ft ; see \ref Jeremiah 37:3|JER 37:3\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shelemiah,|שֶׁ֣לֶמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and Pashhur|וּפַשְׁח֖וּר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Malchijah|מַלְכִּיָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֞ע\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb had been telling|מְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb* \v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּה֮\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Whoever stays|הַיֹּשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֕וּת\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague,|וּבַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb but whoever surrenders|וְהַיֹּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּים֙\rb*\f + \fr 38:2 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 18, 19, and 23\f* \rb will live;|יִחְיֶה\rb* \rb he will retain|וְהָיְתָה־\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb like a spoil of war,|לְשָׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb and he will live.|וָחָֽי׃ס\rb* \v 3 \rb This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb This|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will surely be delivered|הִנָּתֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |תִּנָּתֵ֜ן\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֛ד\rb* \rb of the army|חֵ֥יל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and he will capture it.”|וּלְכָדָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb “This|הַזֶּה֒\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb ought to die,|י֣וּמַת\rb*\rb |נָא֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb is discouraging|מְרַפֵּ֡א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יְדֵי֩\rb* \rb the warriors|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb*\rb |הַמִּלְחָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb who remain|הַֽנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֗את\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb city,|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb as well as all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb by speaking|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb such|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|כַּדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to them;|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is not|אֵינֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb seeking|דֹרֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb the well-being|לְשָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb of these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people,|לָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb their ruin.”|לְרָעָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb “Here|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb he is,”|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah.|צִדְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “He is in your hands,|בְּיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb can do nothing|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to stop you.”|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So they took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and dropped|וַיַּשְׁלִ֨כוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cistern|הַבּ֣וֹר׀\rb* \rb of Malchiah,|מַלְכִּיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb son,|בֶן־\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb was in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard.|הַמַּטָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb They lowered|וַיְשַׁלְּח֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with ropes|בַּחֲבָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb into the cistern,|וּבַבּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb which had no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb but only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb mud,|טִ֔יט\rb* \rb and Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb sank down|וַיִּטְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb into the mud.|בַּטִּֽיט׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb |עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb Now Ebed-melech|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb the Cushite,|הַכּוּשִׁ֜י\rb*\f + \fr 38:7 \ft Probably from the upper Nile region\f*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb a court official|סָרִ֗יס\rb*\f + \fr 38:7 \ft Or \fqa eunuch\f*\rb |וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb in the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb palace,|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֡ע\rb* \rb that Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb had been put|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cistern.|הַבּ֑וֹר\rb* \rb While the king|וְהַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb at the Gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb |עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb Ebed-melech|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb from the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb have acted wickedly|הֵרֵ֜עוּ\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they have done|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb to Jeremiah|לְיִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet.|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb They have dropped him|הִשְׁלִ֖יכוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cistern,|הַבּ֑וֹר\rb* \rb where|תַּחְתָּיו֙\rb* \rb he will starve to death,|וַיָּ֤מָת\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽרָעָ֔ב\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb more|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb bread|הַלֶּ֛חֶם\rb* \rb in the city.”|בָּעִֽיר׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb Ebed-melech|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb the Cushite,|הַכּוּשִׁ֖י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb here|מִזֶּה֙\rb* \rb with you|בְּיָדְךָ֤\rb* \rb and pull|וְֽהַעֲלִ֜יתָ\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֛יא\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb out of the cistern|הַבּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb he dies.”|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb Then Ebed-melech|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח׀\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb with him|בְּיָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb palace,|בֵית־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a place below|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the storehouse.|הָאוֹצָ֔ר\rb* \rb From there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb old|בְּלוֹיֵ֣\rb* \rb rags|הַסְּחָבוֹת\rb* \rb and worn-out|וּבְלוֹיֵ֖\rb* \rb clothes|מְלָחִ֑ים\rb* \rb and lowered them|וַיְשַׁלְּחֵ֧ם\rb* \rb with ropes|בַּחֲבָלִֽים׃\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cistern.|הַבּ֖וֹר\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb |עֶבֶד־\rb* \rb Ebed-melech|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֜י\rb* \rb cried out|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb “Put|שִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |נָ֠א\rb* \rb these worn-out|בְּלוֹאֵ֨י\rb* \rb rags|הַסְּחָב֤וֹת\rb* \rb and clothes|וְהַמְּלָחִים֙\rb*\rb |תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb under your arms|אַצִּל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb to pad the ropes.”|לַחֲבָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb so,|כֵּֽן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and they pulled him|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb up|וַיִּמְשְׁכ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb with the ropes|בַּֽחֲבָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb and lifted|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the cistern.|הַבּ֑וֹר\rb* \rb And Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the guard.|הַמַּטָּרָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb sent for|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb and received|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb him|אֶֽת־\rb* \rb at|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb entrance|מָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb am going to ask|שֹׁאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb you something,”|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah.|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hide|תְּכַחֵ֥ד\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb from me.”|מִמֶּ֖נִּי\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “If|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I tell you,”|אַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |צִדְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb |הֲל֖וֹא\rb* \rb “you will surely put me to death.|הָמֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |תְּמִיתֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb And even if|וְכִי֙\rb* \rb I give you advice,|אִיעָ֣צְךָ֔\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|תִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to me.”|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֞ע\rb* \rb secretly|בַּסֵּ֣תֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb has given|עָשָׂה־\rb* \rb us|לָ֨נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb life,|הַנֶּ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb kill you,|אֲמִיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb nor|וְאִם־\rb* \rb will I deliver you|אֶתֶּנְךָ֗\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb are seeking|מְבַקְשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your life.”|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zedekiah,|צִדְקִיָּ֡הוּ\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘If|אִם־\rb* \rb you indeed surrender|יָצֹ֨א\rb*\rb |תֵצֵ֜א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officers|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb then you|נַפְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb* \rb will live,|וְחָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|וְהָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be burned down,|תִשָּׂרֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and your household|וּבֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will survive.|וְחָיִ֖תָה\rb* \v 18 \rb But if|וְאִ֣ם\rb* \rb you do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb surrender|תֵצֵ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officers|שָׂרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb then this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb will be delivered|וְנִתְּנָ֞ה\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans.|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb They will burn it down,|וּשְׂרָפ֖וּהָ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb yourself will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb escape|תִמָּלֵ֥ט\rb* \rb their grasp.’”|מִיָּדָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֧י\rb* \rb am afraid|דֹאֵ֣ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb have deserted|נָֽפְלוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans,|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb for the Chaldeans|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb may deliver|יִתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb into their hands|בְּיָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to abuse|וְהִתְעַלְּלוּ־\rb* \rb me.”|בִֽי׃פ\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “They will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb hand you over,”|יִתֵּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb “Obey|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א׀\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb in what|לַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am telling you,|דֹּבֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that it may go well|וְיִ֥יטַב\rb* \rb with you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb and you|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb may live.|וּתְחִ֥י\rb* \v 21 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb refuse|מָאֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to surrender,|לָצֵ֑את\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the word|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has shown me:|הִרְאַ֖נִי\rb* \v 22 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb remain|נִשְׁאֲרוּ֙\rb* \rb in the palace|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be brought out|מוּצָא֕וֹת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb and those women|וְהֵ֣נָּה\rb* \rb will say:|אֹמְר֗וֹת\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘They misled you|הִסִּית֜וּךָ\rb* \rb and overcame|וְיָכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb you—|לְךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb those trusted|שְׁלֹמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb friends of yours.|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*
\q1 \rb Your feet|רַגְלֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb sank|הָטְבְּע֥וּ\rb* \rb into the mire,|בַבֹּ֛ץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and they deserted|נָסֹ֥גוּ\rb* \rb you.’|אָחֽוֹר׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb your wives|נָשֶׁ֣יךָ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb children|בָּנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb will be brought out|מֽוֹצִאִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans.|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb yourself will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb escape|תִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb* \rb their grasp,|מִיָּדָ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will be seized|תִּתָּפֵ֔שׂ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb by|בְיַ֤ד\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb and this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb will be burned down.”|תִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb warned|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let anyone|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb know|יֵדַ֥ע\rb* \rb about this|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb conversation,|בַּדְּבָֽרִים־\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb you will die.|תָמֽוּת׃\rb* \v 25 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִים֮\rb* \rb hear|יִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִבַּ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb with you,|אִתָּךְ֒\rb* \rb and they come|וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and demand|וְֽאָמְר֪וּ\rb* \rb of you,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb ‘Tell|הַגִּֽידָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֨א\rb* \rb us|לָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb you said|דִּבַּ֧רְתָּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and what|וּמַה־\rb* \rb he|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to you;|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hide it|תְּכַחֵ֥ד\rb* \rb from us,|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb we will kill you,’|נְמִיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \v 26 \rb then tell them,|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb was presenting|מַפִּיל־\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb my petition|תְחִנָּתִ֖י\rb* \rb that he not|לְבִלְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb return me|הֲשִׁיבֵ֛נִי\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֥וּת\rb* \rb there.’”|שָֽׁם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and questioned him,|וַיִּשְׁאֲל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb he relayed|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb the exact|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb had commanded him to say.|צִוָּ֖ה\rb* \rb So they said no more|וַיַּחֲרִ֣שׁוּ\rb* \rb to him,|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb no one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb had overheard|נִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb the conversation.|הַדָּבָֽר׃פ\rb* \v 28 \rb And Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַמַּטָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑םס\rb* \rb was captured.|נִלְכְּדָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |נִלְכְּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 39
\s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\r \ref 2 Kings 25:1–12|2KI 25:1-12\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 36:15–21|2CH 36:15-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the ninth|הַ֠תְּשִׁעִית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|לְצִדְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb in the tenth|הָעֲשִׂרִ֗י\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֨ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb marched|בָּ֠א\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb with his entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|חֵילוֹ֙\rb* \rb and laid siege|וַיָּצֻ֖רוּ\rb* \rb to the city.|עָלֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb* \v 2 \rb And on the ninth|בְּתִשְׁעָ֣ה\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Zedekiah’s|לְצִדְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb eleventh|בְּעַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb year,|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb was breached.|הָבְקְעָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Middle|הַתָּ֑וֶךְ\rb* \rb Gate:|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb*\rb |נֵרְגַ֣ל\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb Nergal-sharezer|אֶ֠צֶר\rb* \rb of Samgar,|סַֽמְגַּר־\rb*\rb |נְב֞וּ\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb Nebo-sarsekim|סְכִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Or \fqa Nergal-sharezer, Samgar-nebo, Sarsekim\f*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabsaris,|סָרִ֗יס\rb*\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabsaris \ft is the title of the chief eunuch in the Assyrian military; also in verse 13.\f*\rb |נֵרְגַ֤ל\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb Nergal-sharezer|אֶ֙צֶר֙\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabmag,|מָ֔ג\rb*\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabmag \ft is the title of the chief soothsayer or chief of princes in the Assyrian military; also in verse 13.\f* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the rest|שְׁאֵרִ֔ית\rb* \rb of the officials|שָׂרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the soldiers|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb saw them,|רָ֠אָם\rb* \rb they fled.|וַֽ֠יִּבְרְחוּ\rb* \rb They left|וַיֵּצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb at night|לַ֤יְלָה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb garden,|גַּ֣ן\rb* \rb through the gate|בְּשַׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the two walls,|הַחֹמֹתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and they went out|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb along the route|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to the Arabah.|הָעֲרָבָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 39:4 \ft Or \fqa the Jordan Valley\f* \v 5 \rb But the army|חֵיל־\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֜ים\rb*\f + \fr 39:5 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verse 8\f* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדְּפ֨וּ\rb* \rb them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and overtook|וַיַּשִּׂ֣גוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּהוּ֮\rb* \rb in the plains|בְּעַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jericho.|יְרֵחוֹ֒\rb* \rb They seized|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb and brought him up|וַֽ֠יַּעֲלֻהוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֧ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb at Riblah|רִבְלָ֖תָה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hamath,|חֲמָ֑ת\rb* \rb where he pronounced|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb judgment|מִשְׁפָּטִֽים׃\rb* \rb on him.|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb There at Riblah|בְּרִבְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחַט֩\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb before his eyes,|לְעֵינָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and he|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \rb also killed|שָׁחַ֖ט\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nobles|חֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \v 7 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Then he put out|עִוֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb Zedekiah’s|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb and bound him|וַיַּאַסְרֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with bronze chains|בַּֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb to take|לָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb The Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb set fire to|שָׂרְפ֥וּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb the palace|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb to the houses|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they broke down|נָתָֽצוּ׃\rb* \rb the walls|חֹמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then|וְאֵת֩\rb*\rb |נְבֽוּזַר־\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|אֲדָ֥ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb carried|הֶגְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb away to Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \rb the remnant|יֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb who had remained|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the city,|בָּעִ֗יר\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the deserters|הַנֹּֽפְלִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had defected|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb to|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb him.|וְאֵ֛ת\rb*\rb |יֶ֥תֶר\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֑ים\rb* \v 10 \rb But Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֥ן\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb*\rb |טַבָּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb left behind|הִשְׁאִ֛יר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the poor|הַדַּלִּ֗ים\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb had no property,|אֵין־\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb*\rb |מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb and at that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb time|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb he gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb vineyards|כְּרָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb and fields.|וִֽיגֵבִ֖ים\rb*
\s1 Jeremiah Delivered
\p \v 11 \rb Now Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb had given orders|וַיְצַ֛ו\rb* \rb about|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֛ד\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֥ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard,|טַבָּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb “Take him,|קָחֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb look after|וְעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb him,|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb let any|מְא֣וּמָה\rb* \rb harm|רָּ֑ע\rb*\rb |כִּ֗י\rb* \rb come|תַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb to him;|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb do|עֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb whatever|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb he says.”|יְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb |וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb So Nebuzaradan|נְבֽוּזַרְאֲדָ֣ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard,|טַבָּחִ֗ים\rb* \rb Nebushazban|וּנְבֽוּשַׁזְבָּן֙\rb*\f + \fr 39:13 \fqa Nebushazban \ft is possibly a variant of \fqa Nebo-sarsekim\ft ; see verse 3.\f*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabsaris,|סָרִ֔יס\rb*\rb |וְנֵרְגַ֥ל\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb Nergal-sharezer|אֶ֖צֶר\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabmag,|מָ֑ג\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the captains|רַבֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb* \v 14 \rb had Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּשְׁלְחוּ֩\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְח֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb from the courtyard|מֵחֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard,|הַמַּטָּרָ֗ה\rb* \rb and they turned him over|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֔ן\rb* \rb to take|לְהוֹצִאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb him|אֶל־\rb* \rb home.|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb So Jeremiah remained|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb his own people.|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb And while Jeremiah had been|בִּֽהְיֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb confined|עָצ֔וּר\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the guard,|הַמַּטָּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb had come|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb him:|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 16 \rb “Go|הָל֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֡\rb*\rb |לְעֶבֶד־\rb* \rb Ebed-melech|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb the Cushite that|הַכּוּשִׁ֜י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘I am about to fulfill|מֵבִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My words|דְּבָרַ֜י\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb for harm|לְרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb for good,|לְטוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb and on that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb they will be fulfilled|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb before your eyes.|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 17 \rb But I will deliver you|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb on that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day,|בַיּוֹם־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and you will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb be delivered|תִנָּתֵן֙\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb fear.|יָג֖וֹר\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I will surely rescue you|מַלֵּט֙\rb*\rb |אֲמַלֶּטְךָ֔\rb* \rb so that you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb fall|תִפֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb by the sword.|וּבַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have trusted|בָטַ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb in Me,|בִּ֖י\rb* \rb you will escape|וְהָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb with|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb* \rb like a spoil of war,|לְשָׁלָ֔ל\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.’”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 40
\s1 Jeremiah Remains in Judah
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֞ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֛ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb had released|שַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb at|מִן־\rb* \rb Ramah,|הָֽרָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb having found|בְּקַחְתּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb him|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb bound|אָס֤וּר\rb* \rb in chains|בָּֽאזִקִּים֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֨וֹךְ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the captives|גָּל֤וּת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who were being exiled|הַמֻּגְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb The captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb found|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb Jeremiah|לְיִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb decreed|דִּבֶּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place,|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \v 3 \rb and now the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has fulfilled it;|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb He has done|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He said.|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you people have sinned|חֲטָאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb His voice,|בְּקוֹל֔וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb thing|דָּבָר\rb* \rb has happened|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to you.|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \v 4 \rb But now,|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb I am freeing|פִתַּחְתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb you today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb the chains|הָאזִקִּים֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were on|עַל־\rb* \rb your wrists.|יָדֶךָ֒\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֨וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb you to come|לָב֧וֹא\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb then come,|בֹּ֚א\rb* \rb and I will take care of|וְאָשִׂ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינִי֙\rb* \rb you.|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it seems wrong|רַ֧ע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb to you to come|לָבֽוֹא־\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֥י\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb go no farther.|חֲדָ֑ל\rb* \rb Look,|רְאֵה֙\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb is before you.|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Wherever it seems|בְּעֵינֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb good|ט֨וֹב\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and right to you,|הַיָּשָׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb go|לֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb there.”|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb But before Jeremiah|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |וְעוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb turned to go,|יָשׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|וְשֻׁ֡בָה\rb* \rb added,|אֶל־\rb* \rb “Return to Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֡ן\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb* \rb has appointed|הִפְקִ֨יד\rb* \rb over the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and stay|וְשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb with him|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb or|א֠וֹ\rb* \rb go|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb anywhere else|אֶל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb that seems right.”|הַיָּשָׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |לֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb Then the captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֛ים\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֧וֹ\rb* \rb a ration|אֲרֻחָ֥ה\rb* \rb and a gift|וּמַשְׂאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and released him.|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֑תָה\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb with him|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb who were left|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the land.|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Gedaliah Governs in Judah
\r \ref 2 Kings 25:22–24|2KI 25:22-24\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb*\rb |הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb and men|וְאַנְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb of the armies|הַחֲיָלִ֜ים\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ֩\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had appointed|הִפְקִ֧יד\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb over the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and that|וְכִ֣י׀\rb* \rb he had put him in charge|הִפְקִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb of the men,|אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb women,|וְנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and children|וָטָ֔ף\rb* \rb who were the poorest|וּמִדַּלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been exiled|הָגְל֖וּ\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb they came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Mizpah—|הַמִּצְפָּ֑תָה\rb*  \rb Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,|נְתַנְיָ֡הוּ\rb* \rb Johanan|וְיוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וְיוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָ֠רֵחַ\rb* \rb Seraiah|וּשְׂרָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Tanhumeth,|תַּנְחֻ֜מֶת\rb* \rb the sons|וּבְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of Ephai|עוֹפַי\rb* \rb the Netophathite,|הַנְּטֹפָתִ֗י\rb* \rb and Jezaniah|וִֽיזַנְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 40:8 \fqa Jezaniah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jaazaniah\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 25:23|2KI 25:23\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the Maacathite—|הַמַּ֣עֲכָתִ֔י\rb*  \rb they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and their men.|וְאַנְשֵׁיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֤ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָן֙\rb* \rb swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֨ע\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and their men,|וּלְאַנְשֵׁיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb assuring them,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb to serve|מֵעֲב֣וֹד\rb* \rb the Chaldeans.|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 40:9 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verse 10\f* \rb Live|שְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and serve|וְעִבְד֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and it will go well|וְיִיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb with you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb As for me,|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb I will|הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb stay|יֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in Mizpah|בַּמִּצְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb to represent|לַֽעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb you before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to us.|אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb As for you,|וְאַתֶּ֡ם\rb* \rb gather|אִסְפוּ֩\rb* \rb wine grapes,|יַ֨יִן\rb* \rb summer fruit,|וְקַ֜יִץ\rb* \rb and oil,|וְשֶׁ֗מֶן\rb* \rb place them|וְשִׂ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb in your storage jars,|בִּכְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and live|וּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵיכֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have taken.”|תְּפַשְׂתֶּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb When|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֡ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Moab,|בְּמוֹאָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb Ammon,|וּבִבְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֨וֹן\rb* \rb Edom,|וּבֶאֱד֜וֹם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb and all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the other lands|הָֽאֲרָצוֹת֙\rb* \rb heard|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb had left|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb a remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb in Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְכִי֙\rb* \rb and had appointed|הִפְקִ֣יד\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֥ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָֽן׃\rb* \rb over them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 12 \rb they|הַיְּהוּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the places|הַמְּקֹמוֹת֙\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had been banished|נִדְּחוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb to the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah.|הַמִּצְפָּ֑תָה\rb* \rb And they gathered|וַיַּאַסְפ֛וּ\rb* \rb an abundance|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃פ\rb* \rb of wine grapes|יַ֥יִן\rb* \rb and summer fruit.|וָקַ֖יִץ\rb*
\s1 The Plot against Gedaliah
\p \v 13 \rb Meanwhile, Johanan|וְיֽוֹחָנָן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah|קָרֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the armies|הַחֲיָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּֽתָה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and said to him,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “Are you aware|הֲיָדֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb Baalis|בַּעֲלִ֣יס׀\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb* \rb has sent|שָׁלַח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb to take|לְהַכֹּתְךָ֖\rb* \rb your life?”|נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb*
\p \rb But Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam|אֲחִיקָֽם׃\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb believe|הֶאֱמִ֣ין\rb* \rb them.|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then Johanan|וְיוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah|קָרֵ֡חַ\rb* \rb spoke|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb privately|בַסֵּ֨תֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָהוּ֩\rb* \rb at Mizpah.|בַּמִּצְפָּ֜ה\rb* \rb “Let me go|אֵ֤לְכָה\rb*\rb |נָּא֙\rb* \rb and kill|וְאַכֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,”|נְתַנְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb he said.|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “No|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb will know it.|יֵדָ֑ע\rb* \rb Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb should he take|יַכֶּ֣כָּה\rb* \rb your life|נֶּ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and scatter|וְנָפֹ֙צוּ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who have gathered|הַנִּקְבָּצִ֣ים\rb* \rb to you,|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb so that the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb would perish?”|וְאָבְדָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam|אֲחִיקָם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Johanan|יוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָרֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb “Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb do|תַּעַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb such a thing!|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb What you are|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb saying|דֹבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵֽאל׃ס\rb* \rb is a lie.”|שֶׁ֛קֶר\rb*
\c 41
\s1 The Murder of Gedaliah
\r \ref 2 Kings 25:25–26|2KI 25:25-26\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb In the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,|נְתַנְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Elishama,|אֱלִישָׁמָ֣ע\rb* \rb who was a member of the royal|הַ֠מְּלוּכָה\rb* \rb family|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb* \rb and one of the king’s|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb chief officers,|וְרַבֵּ֨י\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb with|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb ten|וַעֲשָׂרָ֨ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb at Mizpah,|הַמִּצְפָּ֑תָה\rb* \rb and they ate|וַיֹּ֨אכְלוּ\rb* \rb a meal|לֶ֛חֶם\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֖ו\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |בַּמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Then Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֨אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָ֜ה\rb* \rb and the ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים׀\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb and struck down|וַ֠יַּכּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֧ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֛ן\rb* \rb with the sword,|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb killing|וַיָּ֣מֶת\rb* \rb the one|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb had appointed to govern|הִפְקִ֥יד\rb* \rb the land.|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵֽאל׃\rb* \rb also|וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb killed|הִכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were|הָי֨וּ\rb* \rb with|אִתּ֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb at Mizpah,|בַּמִּצְפָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb as well as the Chaldean|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 41:3 \ft Or \fqa Babylonian\f* \rb soldiers|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |נִמְצְאוּ־\rb* \rb were there.|שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb On the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb after the murder|לְהָמִ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Gedaliah,|גְּדַלְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb when no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb yet knew about it,|יָדָֽע׃\rb* \v 5 \rb eighty|שְׁמֹנִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb men|אֲ֠נָשִׁים\rb* \rb who had shaved off|מְגֻלְּחֵ֥י\rb* \rb their beards,|זָקָ֛ן\rb* \rb torn|וּקְרֻעֵ֥י\rb* \rb their garments,|בְגָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and cut themselves|וּמִתְגֹּֽדְדִ֑ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb from Shechem,|מִשְּׁכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb Shiloh,|מִשִּׁל֤וֹ\rb* \rb and Samaria,|וּמִשֹּֽׁמְרוֹן֙\rb*\rb |בְּיָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb carrying|לְהָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb grain offerings|וּמִנְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb and frankincense|וּלְבוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb for the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֨אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb went out|וַ֠יֵּצֵא\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb to meet them,|לִקְרָאתָם֙\rb* \rb weeping|וּבֹכֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb as he went.|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |הָלֹ֖ךְ\rb*
\p \rb When Ishmael encountered the men,|כִּפְגֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Come|בֹּ֖אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam.”|אֲחִיקָֽם׃ס\rb* \v 7 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb And when they came|כְּבוֹאָ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֤אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָה֙\rb* \rb and the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb slaughtered them|וַיִּשְׁחָטֵ֞ם\rb* \rb and threw them into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb a cistern.|הַבּ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb But ten|וַעֲשָׂרָ֨ה\rb* \rb of the men|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb among them|בָ֗ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ishmael,|יִשְׁמָעֵאל֙\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb kill us,|תְּמִתֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb hidden treasure|מַטְמֹנִים֙\rb* \rb in the field—|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb wheat,|חִטִּ֥ים\rb* \rb barley,|וּשְׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb oil,|וְשֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and honey!”|וּדְבָ֑שׁ\rb* \rb So he refrained|וַיֶּחְדַּ֕ל\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb from killing them|הֱמִיתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the others.|אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Now the cistern|וְהַבּ֗וֹר\rb* \rb into which|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵאל֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb had thrown|הִשְׁלִ֨יךְ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the bodies|פִּגְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb he had struck down|הִכָּה֙\rb* \rb along with|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb was a large one that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֔א\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb for fear|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֣א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֥אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb filled it|מִלֵּ֛א\rb* \rb with the slain.|חֲלָלִֽים׃\rb*
