\c 42
\s1 A Warning against Going to Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the forces,|הַחֲיָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb along with Johanan|וְיֽוֹחָנָן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָרֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb Jezaniah|וִֽיזַנְיָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 42:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Azariah\ft ; see \ref Jeremiah 43:2|JER 43:2\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hoshaiah,|הוֹשַֽׁעְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb from the least|מִקָּטֹ֥ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the greatest,|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb approached|וַֽיִּגְּשׁוּ֙\rb* \v 2 \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb “May our petition|תְחִנָּתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb come|תִּפָּל־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb before you;|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb pray|וְהִתְפַּלֵּ֤ל\rb*\rb |בַּעֲדֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb on behalf of|בְּעַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb remnant.|הַשְּׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb few|מְעַט֙\rb* \rb of us remain|נִשְׁאַ֤רְנוּ\rb* \rb of the many,|מֵֽהַרְבֵּ֔ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you can see|רֹא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb with your own eyes.|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 3 \rb Pray that the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will tell|וְיַגֶּד־\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we should walk|נֵֽלֶךְ־\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the thing|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we should do.”|נַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb “I have heard you,”|שָׁמַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet.|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb “I will surely|הִנְנִ֧י\rb* \rb pray|מִתְפַּלֵּ֛ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as you request,|כְּדִבְרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְֽהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb and I will tell you|אַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb everything|כָּֽל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb answers.|יַעֲנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb withhold|אֶמְנַ֥ע\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb from you.”|מִכֶּ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then they|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb said|אָמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֤י\rb* \rb a true|אֱמֶ֣ת\rb* \rb and faithful|וְנֶאֱמָ֑ן\rb* \rb witness|לְעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb against us|בָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb we do not|לֹ֡א\rb* \rb act upon|נַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb every|כְּֽכָל־\rb* \rb word|הַ֠דָּבָר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb sends you|יִֽשְׁלָחֲךָ֜\rb* \rb to tell us.|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \v 6 \rb Whether|אִם־\rb* \rb it is pleasant|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb unpleasant,|רָ֔ע\rb* \rb we will obey|נִשְׁמָ֑ע\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb we|אֲנוּ\rb* \rb are sending|שֹׁלְחִ֥ים\rb* \rb you,|אֹתְךָ֛\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb it may go well with us|יִֽיטַב־\rb* \rb when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we obey|נִשְׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God!”|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb After|מִקֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb and he summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Johanan|יֽוֹחָנָן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָרֵ֔חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the forces|הַחֲיָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were with him,|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb from the least|לְמִקָּטֹ֥ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the greatest.|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Jeremiah told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Thus|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb to|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you sent|שְׁלַחְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִי֙\rb* \rb to present|לְהַפִּ֥יל\rb* \rb your petition:|תְּחִנַּתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \v 10 \rb ‘If|אִם־\rb*\rb |שׁ֤וֹב\rb* \rb you will indeed stay|תֵּֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land,|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb then I will build|וּבָנִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb you up|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb tear you down;|אֶהֱרֹ֔ס\rb* \rb I will plant|וְנָטַעְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb uproot you,|אֶתּ֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I will relent|נִחַ֙מְתִּי֙\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have brought|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb upon you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֗וּ\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb now fear;|יְרֵאִ֖ים\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֤וּ\rb* \rb of him,|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb am with|אִתְּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb you to save|לְהוֹשִׁ֧יעַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and deliver|וּלְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from him.|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And I will show|וְאֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb compassion,|רַחֲמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and he will have compassion|וְרִחַ֣ם\rb* \rb on you|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and restore|וְהֵשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your own land.’|אַדְמַתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb say,|אֹמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb ‘We will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb stay|נֵשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land,’|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |לְבִלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb and you thus disobey|שְׁמֹ֔עַ\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and if you say,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘No,|לֹ֚א\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we will go|נָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and live|נֵשֵֽׁב׃\rb* \rb there,|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb we will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|נִרְאֶה֙\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb or hear|נִשְׁמָ֑ע\rb* \rb the sound|וְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb or hunger|נִרְעָ֖ב\rb* \rb for bread,’|וְלַלֶּ֥חֶם\rb* \v 15 \rb then|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*\rb |לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb hear|שִׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb O remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah!|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb ‘If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַ֠תֶּם\rb* \rb are determined|שׂ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |תְּשִׂמ֤וּן\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to go|לָבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וּבָאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and reside|לָג֥וּר\rb* \rb there,|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 16 \rb |וְהָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb then the sword|הַחֶ֗רֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb fear|יְרֵאִ֣ים\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֔נָּה\rb* \rb will overtake|תַּשִּׂ֥יג\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֛ם\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and the famine|וְהָרָעָ֞ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb dread|דֹּאֲגִ֣ים\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb will follow on your heels|יִדְבַּ֧ק\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb into Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and you will die|תָּמֻֽתוּ׃\rb* \rb there.|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \v 17 \rb So all|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb resolve|שָׂ֨מוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to go|לָב֤וֹא\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to reside there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |לָג֣וּר\rb* \rb will|וְיִֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb die|יָמ֕וּתוּ\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague.|וּבַדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb Not one|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb of them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb will|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb survive|שָׂרִ֣יד\rb* \rb or escape|וּפָלִ֔יט\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the disaster|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb upon them.’|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֮\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb ‘Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּ֜י\rb* \rb and wrath|וַחֲמָתִ֗י\rb* \rb were poured out|נִתַּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the residents|יֹֽשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb will My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb be poured out|תִּתַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb on you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb if you go|בְּבֹאֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to Egypt.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb You will become|וִהְיִיתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb an object of cursing|לְאָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb and horror,|וּלְשַׁמָּה֙\rb* \rb of vilification|וְלִקְלָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and disgrace,|וּלְחֶרְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and you will never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb again.’|ע֔וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb has told|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb you,|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb O remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb go|תָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt.’|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Know for sure|יָדֹ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |תֵּֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I have warned|הַעִידֹ֥תִי\rb* \rb you|בָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today!|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|בְּנַפְשֽׁוֹתֵיכֶם֒\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb have deceived|הִתְעֵתֶים\rb* \rb yourselves|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb by sending|שְׁלַחְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Pray|הִתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb on our behalf,|בַּעֲדֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and as for all|וּכְכֹל֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֛ינוּ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb says,|יֹאמַ֜ר\rb* \rb tell it|הַגֶּד־\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and we will do it.’|וְעָשִֽׂינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb For I have told|וָאַגִּ֥ד\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today,|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb but you have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb the voice|בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in all|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֥נִי\rb* \rb to tell you.|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Now therefore,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb know|יָדֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb for sure|תֵּֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb and plague|וּבַדֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb you will die|תָּמ֑וּתוּ\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you desire|חֲפַצְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb to go|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to reside.”|לָג֥וּר\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃ס\rb*
\c 43
\s1 Jeremiah Taken to Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb telling|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God—|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb everything that|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָאֵֽלֶּה׃ס\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb had sent him|שְׁלָח֛וֹ\rb* \rb to say—|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \v 2 \rb Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hoshaiah,|הוֹשַֽׁעְיָה֙\rb* \rb Johanan|וְיוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָרֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the arrogant|הַזֵּדִ֑ים\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb are lying!|שֶׁ֚קֶר\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sent you|שְׁלָחֲךָ֞\rb* \rb to say,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|תָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to reside there.’|שָֽׁם׃\rb*\rb |לָג֥וּר\rb* \v 3 \rb Rather,|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּרוּךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah|נֵ֣רִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb is inciting|מַסִּ֥ית\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb against us|בָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb to|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb deliver|תֵּ֨ת\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֤נוּ\rb* \rb into the hands|בְיַֽד־\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans,|הַכַּשְׂדִּים֙\rb*\f + \fr 43:3 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \rb so that they may put us to death|לְהָמִ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb or exile|וּלְהַגְל֥וֹת\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon!”|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Johanan|יוֹחָנָ֨ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah|קָרֵ֜חַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the forces|הַחֲיָלִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb disobeyed|שָׁמַע֩\rb* \rb the command|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb to stay|לָשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Instead, Johanan|יוֹחָנָ֤ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah|קָרֵ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the forces|הַחֲיָלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb those who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had returned|שָׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb to the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had been scattered,|נִדְּחוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |לָג֖וּר\rb* \v 6 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the men,|הַ֠גְּבָרִים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the women,|הַנָּשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the children,|הַטַּף֮\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb daughters,|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֣ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֔ים\rb* \rb had allowed to remain|הִנִּ֙יחַ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֑ן\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Baruch|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Neriah.|נֵרִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So they entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and they went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Tahpanhes.|תַּחְפַּנְחֵֽס׃ס\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb at Tahpanhes:|בְּתַחְפַּנְחֵ֖ס\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “In the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb of the Jews,|יְהוּדִֽים׃\rb* \rb pick up|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |בְּיָדְךָ֞\rb* \rb some large|גְּדֹל֗וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and bury them|וּטְמַנְתָּ֤ם\rb* \rb in the clay|בַּמֶּ֙לֶט֙\rb* \rb of the brick pavement|בַּמַּלְבֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb at the entrance|בְּפֶ֥תַח\rb* \rb to Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb palace|בֵּית־\rb* \rb at Tahpanhes.|בְּתַחְפַּנְחֵ֑ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then tell them|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֲלֵיהֶ֡ם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb ‘I will send for|שֹׁלֵ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |וְ֠לָקַחְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֤ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb and I will set|וְשַׂמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb his throne|כִסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb over|מִמַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb stones|לָאֲבָנִ֥ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have embedded,|טָמָ֑נְתִּי\rb* \rb and he will spread|וְנָטָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his royal pavilion|שַׁפְרוּרוֹ\rb* \rb over them.|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb He will come|וּבָאָה\rb* \rb and strike down|וְהִכָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb bringing death|לַמָּ֗וֶת\rb* \rb to those|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb destined for death,|לַמָּ֣וֶת\rb* \rb captivity|לַשֶּׁ֔בִי\rb* \rb to those|וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb destined for captivity,|לַשְּׁבִי֙\rb* \rb and the sword|לֶחָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb to those|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb destined for the sword.|לַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb I will kindle|וְהִצַּ֣תִּי\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb in the temples|בְּבָתֵּי֙\rb* \rb of the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and Nebuchadnezzar will burn those temples|וּשְׂרָפָ֖ם\rb* \rb and take their gods as captives.|וְשָׁבָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 43:12 \ft Literally \fqa and he will burn them and take them captive\f* \rb So he will wrap himself|וְעָטָה֩\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb a shepherd|הָֽרֹעֶה֙\rb* \rb wraps himself|יַעְטֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his garment,|בִּגְד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he will depart|וְיָצָ֥א\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb unscathed.|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He will demolish|וְשִׁבַּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the sacred pillars|מַצְּבוֹת֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the temple of the sun|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 43:13 \ft LXX \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Heliopolis in On \ft or \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Heliopolis in Egypt\ft ; Hebrew \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Beth-shemesh in the land of Egypt\f* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he will burn down|יִשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb the temples|בָּתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of the gods|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Egypt.’”|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*
\c 44
\s1 Judgment on the Jews in Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb concerning|אֶ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 44:1 \ft Or \fqa Lower Egypt \ft or \fqa northern Egypt\ft ; also in verse 15\f*—\rb |הַיֹּשְׁבִ֤ים\rb* \rb in Migdol,|בְּמִגְדֹּל֙\rb* \rb Tahpanhes,|וּבְתַחְפַּנְחֵ֣ס\rb* \rb and Memphis|וּבְנֹ֔ף\rb*\f + \fr 44:1 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa Noph\f*— \rb and in the land|וּבְאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Pathros:|פַּתְר֖וֹס\rb*\f + \fr 44:1 \ft Or \fqa Upper Egypt \ft or \fqa southern Egypt\ft ; also in verse 15\f* \rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb*\v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have seen|רְאִיתֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I brought|הֵבֵ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah;|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and behold,|וְהִנָּ֤ם\rb* \rb they lie today in ruins|חָרְבָּה֙\rb*\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb and|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb desolation|וְאֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |בָּהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |יוֹשֵֽׁב׃\rb* \v 3 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the evil|רָעָתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they have done.|עָשׂוּ֙\rb*
\p \rb They provoked Me to anger|לְהַכְעִסֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb by continuing|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְקַטֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb and to serve|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb that neither|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb nor you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb nor your fathers|וַאֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb ever knew.|יְדָע֔וּם\rb* \v 4 \rb Yet I sent|וָאֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb again and again,|הַשְׁכֵּ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 44:4 \ft Literally \fqa the prophets, rising up early and sending (them),\f* \rb |וְשָׁלֹ֖חַ\rb*\rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb detestable|הַתֹּעֵבָ֥ה\rb* \rb thing|דְּבַֽר־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I hate.’|שָׂנֵֽאתִי׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb But they did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb or incline|הִטּ֣וּ\rb* \rb their ears;|אָזְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb they did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb from their wickedness|מֵרָֽעָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb or stop|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb burning incense|קַטֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods.|לֵאלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \v 6 \rb Therefore My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb and anger|וְאַפִּ֔י\rb* \rb poured out|וַתִּתַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and burned|וַתִּבְעַר֙\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb so that they have become|וַתִּהְיֶ֛ינָה\rb* \rb the desolate|לְחָרְבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb ruin|לִשְׁמָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb they are today.|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Why|לָמָה֩\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb doing|עֹשִׂ֜ים\rb* \rb such great|גְדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb harm|רָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁ֣תֵכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by cutting off|לְהַכְרִ֨ית\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb and woman,|וְאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb child|עוֹלֵ֥ל\rb* \rb and infant,|וְיוֹנֵ֖ק\rb* \rb leaving|הוֹתִ֥יר\rb* \rb yourselves|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb without|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb a remnant?|שְׁאֵרִֽית׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Why are you provoking Me to anger|לְהַכְעִסֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb by the work|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of your hands|יְדֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by burning incense|לְקַטֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִים֙\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb have gone|בָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb to reside?|לָג֣וּר\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb As a result,|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb you will be cut off|הַכְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb and|וּלְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb will become|הֱיֽוֹתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb an object of cursing|לִקְלָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and reproach|וּלְחֶרְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb among all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Have you forgotten|הַֽשְׁכַחְתֶּם֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wickedness|רָע֨וֹת\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |רָע֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |רָע֣וֹת\rb* \rb their wives,|נָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the wickedness that|רָעֹ֣תֵכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and|רָעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb your wives|נְשֵׁיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb committed|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem?|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb To|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb humbled themselves|דֻכְּא֔וּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb shown reverence,|יָרְא֗וּ\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb have they followed|הָלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb My instruction|בְתֽוֹרָתִי֙\rb* \rb or the statutes|וּבְחֻקֹּתַ֔י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I set|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb your fathers.|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb I will set|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֛י\rb* \rb to bring disaster|לְרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb and to cut off|וּלְהַכְרִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And I will take away|וְלָקַחְתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have resolved|שָׂ֨מוּ\rb*\rb |פְנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to go|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֮\rb* \rb to reside there;|שָׁם֒\rb*\rb |לָג֣וּר\rb* \rb they will meet their end.|וְתַ֨מּוּ\rb* \rb They will all|כֹ֜ל\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֧רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֣יִם\rb* \rb fall|יִפֹּ֗לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb or be consumed|יִתַּ֔מּוּ\rb* \rb by famine.|בָּֽרָעָב֙\rb* \rb From the least|מִקָּטֹן֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the greatest,|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb they will die|יָמֻ֑תוּ\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb or famine;|וּבָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb and they will become|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb an object of cursing|לְאָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and horror,|לְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb of vilification|וְלִקְלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and reproach.|וּלְחֶרְפָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb I will punish|וּפָקַדְתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |עַ֤ל\rb* \rb those who live|הַיּֽוֹשְׁבִים֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I punished|פָּקַ֖דְתִּי\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb and plague,|וּבַדָּֽבֶר׃\rb* \v 14 \rb so that none of|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb the remnant|לִשְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who have gone|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to reside|לָגֽוּר־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb will|יִהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb escape|פָּלִ֤יט\rb* \rb or survive|וְשָׂרִיד֙\rb* \rb to return|וְלָשׁ֣וּב׀\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb long|מְנַשְּׂאִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נַפְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb to return|לָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb and live;|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb none|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb will return|יָשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb except|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb a few fugitives.”|פְּלֵטִֽים׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Stubbornness of the People
\p \v 15 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb who knew|הַיֹּֽדְעִים֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their wives|נְשֵׁיהֶם֙\rb* \rb were burning incense|מְקַטְּר֤וֹת\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb standing by—|הָעֹמְד֖וֹת\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb assembly—|קָהָ֣ל\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and in Pathros,|בְּפַתְר֥וֹס\rb*\f + \fr 44:15 \ft That is, in Lower and Upper Egypt; possibly \fqa in the land of Egypt at Pathros\f*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb said|וַיַּעֲנ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb to Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \v 16 \rb “As for the word|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have spoken|דִּבַּ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb we will not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb listen|שֹׁמְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb to you!|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Instead,|כִּ֩י\rb* \rb we will do|עָשֹׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |נַעֲשֶׂ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb we vowed|הַדָּבָ֣ר׀\rb* \rb to do:|יָצָ֣א\rb*\rb |מִפִּ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb We will burn incense|לְקַטֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to the Queen|לִמְלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of Heaven|הַשָּׁמַיִם֮\rb* \rb and offer|וְהַסֵּֽיךְ־\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִים֒\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֣הּ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb we,|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb* \rb our fathers,|וַאֲבֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb our kings,|מְלָכֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb and our officials|וְשָׂרֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb did|עָשִׂ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb At that time we had plenty|וַנִּֽשְׂבַּֽע־\rb* \rb of food|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*\rb |וַנִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and good things,|טוֹבִ֔ים\rb* \rb and we saw|רָאִֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb disaster.|וְרָעָ֖ה\rb* \v 18 \rb But from the time|וּמִן־\rb*\rb |אָ֡ז\rb* \rb we stopped|חָדַ֜לְנוּ\rb* \rb burning incense|לְקַטֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to the Queen|לִמְלֶ֧כֶת\rb* \rb of Heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and pouring out|וְהַסֵּֽךְ־\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֥הּ\rb* \rb we have lacked|חָסַ֣רְנוּ\rb* \rb everything|כֹ֑ל\rb* \rb and have been perishing|תָּֽמְנוּ׃\rb* \rb by sword|וּבַחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb and famine.”|וּבָרָעָ֖ב\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “Moreover,” said the women, “when|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb* \rb burned incense|מְקַטְּרִים֙\rb* \rb to the Queen|לִמְלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of Heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and poured out|וּלְהַסֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִ֑ים\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb was it without|הֲמִֽבַּלְעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb our husbands’ knowledge|אֲנָשֵׁ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb that we made|עָשִׂ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb sacrificial cakes|כַּוָּנִים֙\rb* \rb in her image|לְהַ֣עֲצִבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and poured out|וְהַסֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb to her?”|לָ֖הּ\rb*
\s1 Calamity for the Jews
\p \v 20 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb both men|הַגְּבָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb women,|הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb* \rb who were answering|הָעֹנִ֥ים\rb* \rb him,|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 21 \rb “As for the incense|קִטַּרְתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb you burned|הַקִּטֵּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and in the streets|וּבְחֻצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem—|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb you,|אַתֶּ֧ם\rb* \rb your fathers,|וַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb your kings,|מַלְכֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb your officials,|וְשָׂרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and the people|וְעַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land—|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb did the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb remember|זָכַ֣ר\rb* \rb and bring|וַֽתַּעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb this to|עַל־\rb* \rb mind?|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 22 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb could|יוּכַל֩\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb endure|לָשֵׂ֗את\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the evil|רֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb deeds|מַעַלְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and detestable acts|הַתּוֹעֵבֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you committed,|עֲשִׂיתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and your land|אַ֠רְצְכֶם\rb* \rb became|וַתְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb a desolation,|לְחָרְבָּ֨ה\rb* \rb a horror,|וּלְשַׁמָּ֧ה\rb* \rb and an object of cursing,|וְלִקְלָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb without|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb inhabitant,|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb as it is this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day.|כְּהַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \v 23 \rb Because|מִפְּנֵי֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you burned incense|קִטַּרְתֶּ֜ם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb and sinned|חֲטָאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb obey|שְׁמַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb walk|הֲלַכְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb His instruction,|וּבְתֹרָת֧וֹ\rb* \rb His statutes,|וּבְחֻקֹּתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and His testimonies,|וּבְעֵדְוֺתָ֖יו\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb has befallen you,|קָרָ֥את\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as you see today.”|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb including all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the women,|הַנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֕ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb are in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb* \v 25 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָאוֹת֩\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb As for you|אַתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb and your wives,|וּנְשֵׁיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb you have spoken|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣רְנָה\rb* \rb with your mouths|בְּפִיכֶם֮\rb* \rb and fulfilled|מִלֵּאתֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb with your hands|וּבִידֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb your words:|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb ‘We will surely perform|עָשֹׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |נַעֲשֶׂ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our vows|נְדָרֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb we have made|נָדַ֙רְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְקַטֵּר֙\rb* \rb to the Queen|לִמְלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of Heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and to pour out|וּלְהַסֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb drink offerings|נְסָכִ֑ים\rb* \rb to her.’|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Go ahead, then,|הָקֵ֤ים\rb* \rb do|תָּקִ֙ימְנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what you have promised!|נִדְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעָשֹׂ֥ה\rb* \rb Keep|תַעֲשֶׂ֖ינָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your vows!|נִדְרֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Nevertheless,|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb all you|כָּל־\rb* \rb people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֕ה\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb in Egypt:|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֜עְתִּי\rb* \rb by My great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb name,|בִּשְׁמִ֤י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that never|אִם־\rb* \rb again|ע֨וֹד\rb* \rb will|יִהְיֶה֩\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb living|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb invoke|נִקְרָ֣א׀\rb*\rb |בְּפִ֣י׀\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֜י\rb* \rb or say,|אֹמֵ֛ר\rb* \rb ‘As surely as the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb* \rb lives.’|חַי־\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am watching|שֹׁקֵ֧ד\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb for harm|לְרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb for good,|לְטוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb and every|כָל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb is in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb will meet his end|וְתַמּוּ֩\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb or famine,|וּבָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they are finished off.|כְּלוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Those who escape|וּפְלִיטֵ֨י\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֜רֶב\rb* \rb will return|יְשֻׁב֨וּן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |אֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb to Judah,|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb few|מְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb in number,|מִסְפָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who went|הַבָּאִ֤ים\rb* \rb to dwell|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |לָג֣וּר\rb* \rb in the land|לְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb will know|וְֽיָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb whose|מִ֥י\rb* \rb word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb will stand,|יָק֖וּם\rb* \rb Mine|מִמֶּ֥נִּי\rb* \rb or theirs!|וּמֵהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb This|וְזֹאת־\rb* \rb will be a sign|הָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb will punish|פֹקֵ֥ד\rb* \rb you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place,|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb you may know|תֵּֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb My threats|דְבָרַ֛י\rb* \rb of harm|לְרָעָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will surely stand.|ק֨וֹם\rb*\rb |יָק֧וּמוּ\rb* \v 30 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I will deliver|נֹ֠תֵן\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֨ה\rb* \rb Hophra|חָפְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of his enemies|אֹֽיְבָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb his life,|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I delivered|נָתַ֜תִּי\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֨ד\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֧ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb the enemy|אֹיְב֖וֹ\rb* \rb who was seeking|וּמְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb his life.”|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*
\c 45
\s1 Jeremiah’s Message to Baruch
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baruch|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Neriah|נֵֽרִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb when he wrote|בְּכָתְבוֹ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a scroll|סֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb at the dictation|מִפִּ֣י\rb* \rb of Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb in the fourth|הָֽרְבִעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|לִיהוֹיָקִ֧ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah,|יֹאשִׁיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to you,|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb Baruch:|בָּרֽוּךְ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb You have said,|אָמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘Woe is|אֽוֹי־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has added|יָסַ֧ף\rb* \rb sorrow|יָג֖וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb my pain!|מַכְאֹבִ֑י\rb* \rb I am worn out|יָגַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb with groaning|בְּאַנְחָתִ֔י\rb* \rb and have found|מָצָֽאתִי׃ס\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb rest.’”|וּמְנוּחָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Thus|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Jeremiah was to say|תֹּאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to Baruch:|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\f + \fr 45:4 \ft Literally \fqa Thus you shall say to him:\f* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will demolish|הֹרֵ֔ס\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have built|בָּנִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb and uproot|נֹתֵ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have planted.|נָטַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֲנִ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \v 5 \rb But as for you,|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb do you seek|תְּבַקֶּשׁ־\rb* \rb great things|גְדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb for yourself?|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb Stop|אַל־\rb* \rb seeking!|תְּבַקֵּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creature,|בָּשָׂר֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb but wherever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּקֹמ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you go,|תֵּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb I will grant|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |לְךָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb* \rb as a spoil of war.”|לְשָׁלָ֔ל\rb*\rb |עַ֥ל\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃ס\rb*
\c 46
\s1 Judgment on Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the nations—|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \rb the word that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \v 2 \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|לְמִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and the army|חֵ֨יל\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֤ה\rb* \rb Neco|נְכוֹ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb was defeated|הִכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb at Carchemish|בְּכַרְכְּמִ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on the Euphrates|פְּרָ֖ת\rb* \rb River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb by Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּר֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb in the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|לִיהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb “Deploy|עִרְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb your shields, small|מָגֵן֙\rb* \rb and large;|וְצִנָּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb advance|וּגְשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb for battle!|לַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*
