\q1 \v 10 \rb For that|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb day belongs|וְֽהַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb to the Lord|לַאדֹנָ֧י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb a day|י֤וֹם\rb* \rb of vengeance|נְקָמָה֙\rb* \rb against|לְהִנָּקֵ֣ם\rb* \rb His foes.|מִצָּרָ֔יו\rb*
\q1 \rb The sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb will devour|וְאָכְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb until it is satisfied,|וְשָׂ֣בְעָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb until it is quenched|וְרָוְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb with their blood.|מִדָּמָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Lord|לַאדֹנָ֨י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb* \rb will hold a sacrifice|זֶ֠בַח\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb by|אֶל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Euphrates.|פְּרָֽת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Go up|עֲלִ֤י\rb* \rb to Gilead|גִלְעָד֙\rb* \rb for|וּקְחִ֣י\rb* \rb balm,|צֳרִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb O Virgin|בְּתוּלַ֖ת\rb* \rb Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Egypt!|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*
\q1 \rb In vain|לַשָּׁוְא֙\rb* \rb you try many|הִרְבֵּיתִי\rb* \rb remedies,|רְפֻא֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb but for you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb healing.|תְּעָלָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb The nations|גוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb have heard|שָׁמְע֤וּ\rb* \rb of your shame,|קְלוֹנֵ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and your outcry|וְצִוְחָתֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb fills|מָלְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb the earth,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb warrior|גִבּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb stumbles|כָּשָׁ֔לוּ\rb* \rb over warrior|בְּגִבּוֹר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and both|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb of them have fallen|נָפְל֥וּ\rb* \rb together.”|יַחְדָּ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb This is the word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb about the coming|לָב֗וֹא\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְרֶאצַּר֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb to strike|לְהַכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt:|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb “Announce it|הַגִּ֤ידוּ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְמִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and proclaim|וְהַשְׁמִ֣יעוּ\rb* \rb it in Migdol;|בְמִגְדּ֔וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb proclaim|וְהַשְׁמִ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb it in Memphis|בְנֹ֖ף\rb*\f + \fr 46:14 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa Noph\ft ; also in verse 19\f* \rb and Tahpanhes:|וּבְתַחְפַּנְחֵ֑ס\rb*\rb |אִמְר֗וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Take your positions|הִתְיַצֵּב֙\rb* \rb and prepare|וְהָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb yourself,|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb devours|אָכְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb those around you.’|סְבִיבֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb have your warriors|אַבִּירֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb been laid low?|נִסְחַ֣ף\rb*
\q2 \rb They cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb stand,|עָמַ֔ד\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has thrust them down.|הֲדָפֽוֹ׃\rb*
