\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he vaunted himself|הִגְדִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 43 \rb Terror|פַּ֥חַד\rb* \rb and pit|וָפַ֖חַת\rb* \rb and snare|וָפָ֑ח\rb* \rb await you,|עָלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb O dweller|יוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb of Moab,”|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 44 \rb “Whoever flees|הַנִּיס\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the panic|הַפַּ֙חַד֙\rb*
\q2 \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pit,|הַפַּ֔חַת\rb*
\q1 \rb and whoever climbs|וְהָֽעֹלֶה֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the pit|הַפַּ֔חַת\rb*
\q2 \rb will be caught|יִלָּכֵ֖ד\rb* \rb in the snare.|בַּפָּ֑ח\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will bring|אָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb upon|אֵלֶ֧יהָ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Moab|מוֹאָ֛ב\rb*
\q2 \rb the year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of their punishment,”|פְּקֻדָּתָ֖ם\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 45 \rb “Those who flee|נָסִ֑ים\rb* \rb will stand|עָמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb helpless|מִכֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb in Heshbon’s|חֶשְׁבּ֛וֹן\rb* \rb shadow,|בְּצֵ֥ל\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֞שׁ\rb* \rb has gone forth|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb from Heshbon|מֵחֶשְׁבּ֗וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and a flame|וְלֶֽהָבָה֙\rb* \rb from within|מִבֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb Sihon.|סִיח֔וֹן\rb*
\q1 \rb It devours|וַתֹּ֙אכַל֙\rb* \rb the foreheads|פְּאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*
\q2 \rb and the skulls|וְקָדְקֹ֖ד\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of tumult.|שָׁאֽוֹן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 46 \rb Woe|אוֹי־\rb* \rb to you,|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb O Moab!|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*
\q2 \rb The people|עַם־\rb* \rb of Chemosh|כְּמ֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb have perished;|אָבַ֖ד\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your sons|בָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb have been taken|לֻקְּח֤וּ\rb* \rb into exile|בַּשֶּׁ֔בִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and your daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb have gone into captivity.|בַּשִּׁבְיָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 47 \rb Yet in the latter|בְּאַחֲרִ֥ית\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb I will restore|וְשַׁבְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb Moab|מוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb from captivity,|שְׁבוּת־\rb*\f + \fr 48:47 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Moab\f*”
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb Here|הֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb ends|עַד־\rb* \rb the judgment|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb on Moab.|מוֹאָֽב׃ס\rb*
\c 49
\s1 Judgment on the Ammonites
\p \v 1 \rb Concerning the Ammonites,|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Has Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb no|אֵין֙\rb* \rb sons?|הֲבָנִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb Is he without|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb heir?|יוֹרֵ֖שׁ\rb*
\q1 \rb Why then|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb has Milcom|מַלְכָּם֙\rb*\f + \fr 49:1 \ft Or \fqa their king\ft ; \fqa Milcom \ft is a variant of \fqa Molech\ft ; also in verse 3; see \ref Leviticus 18:21|LEV 18:21\ref* and 1 Kings 11:7.\f* \rb taken possession|יָרַ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Gad?|גָּ֔ד\rb*
\q2 \rb Why have his people|וְעַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb settled|יָשָֽׁב׃\rb* \rb in their cities?|בְּעָרָ֥יו\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Therefore,|לָכֵ֡ן\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֨ים\rb* \rb are coming,|בָּאִ֜ים\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q1 \rb when I will sound|וְ֠הִשְׁמַעְתִּי\rb* \rb the battle|מִלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb cry|תְּרוּעַ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rabbah|רַבַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of the Ammonites.|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb*
\q1 \rb It will become|וְהָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a heap|לְתֵ֣ל\rb* \rb of ruins,|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and its villages|וּבְנֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb will be burned.|תִּצַּ֑תְנָה\rb*
\q1 \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will drive out|וְיָרַ֧שׁ\rb* \rb their dispossessors,|יֹרְשָׁ֖יו\rb*
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Wail,|הֵילִ֨ילִי\rb* \rb O Heshbon,|חֶשְׁבּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Ai|עַ֗י\rb* \rb has been destroyed;|שֻׁדְּדָה־\rb*
\q2 \rb cry out,|צְעַקְנָה֮\rb* \rb O daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Rabbah!|רַבָּה֒\rb*
\q1 \rb Put on|חֲגֹ֣רְנָה\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and mourn;|סְפֹ֕דְנָה\rb*
\q2 \rb run back and forth|וְהִתְשׁוֹטַ֖טְנָה\rb* \rb within your walls,|בַּגְּדֵר֑וֹת\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Milcom|מַלְכָּם֙\rb* \rb will go|יֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb into exile|בַּגּוֹלָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb together with|יַחְדָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb his priests|כֹּהֲנָ֥יו\rb* \rb and officials.|וְשָׂרָ֖יו\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Why|מַה־\rb* \rb do you boast|תִּתְהַֽלְלִי֙\rb* \rb of your valleys—|בָּֽעֲמָקִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb your valleys|עִמְקֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb so fruitful,|זָ֣ב\rb*\f + \fr 49:4 \ft Or \fqa your valleys flowing\f*
\q2 \rb O faithless|הַשּֽׁוֹבֵבָ֑ה\rb* \rb daughter?|הַבַּ֖ת\rb*
\q1 \rb You trust|הַבֹּֽטְחָה֙\rb* \rb in your riches and say,|בְּאֹ֣צְרֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘Who|מִ֖י\rb* \rb can come against|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb me?’|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb I am about to bring|מֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb terror|פַּ֗חַד\rb* \rb upon you,|עָלַ֜יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֧י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֛ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb from all those|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb around you.|סְבִיבָ֑יִךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb You will each be driven|וְנִדַּחְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb headlong,|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb with no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to regather|מְקַבֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb the fugitives.|לַנֹּדֵֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Yet afterward|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb I will restore|אָשִׁ֛יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb from captivity,|שְׁב֥וּת\rb*\f + \fr 49:6 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of the Ammonites\f*”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 Judgment on Edom
\r \ref Obadiah 1:1–14|OBA 1-14\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb Concerning Edom,|לֶאֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֙\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Is there no|הַאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Teman?|בְּתֵימָ֑ן\rb*
\q2 \rb Has counsel|עֵצָה֙\rb* \rb perished|אָבְדָ֤ה\rb* \rb from the prudent?|מִבָּנִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb Has their wisdom|חָכְמָתָֽם׃\rb* \rb decayed?|נִסְרְחָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Turn|הָפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb and run!|נֻ֤סוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Lie|לָשֶׁ֔בֶת\rb* \rb low,|הֶעְמִ֣יקוּ\rb* \rb O dwellers|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Dedan,|דְּדָ֑ן\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I will bring|הֵבֵ֥אתִי\rb* \rb disaster|אֵ֥יד\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb*
\q2 \rb at the time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb I punish him.|פְּקַדְתִּֽיו׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb grape gatherers|בֹּֽצְרִים֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to you,|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb would they not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave|יַשְׁאִ֖רוּ\rb* \rb some gleanings?|עֽוֹלֵל֑וֹת\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*
\q1 \rb Were thieves|גַּנָּבִ֥ים\rb* \rb to come in the night,|בַּלַּ֖יְלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb would they not steal|הִשְׁחִ֥יתוּ\rb* \rb only what they wanted?|דַיָּֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb But|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will strip Esau|עֵשָׂ֗ו\rb* \rb bare;|חָשַׂ֣פְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb I will uncover|גִּלֵּ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hiding places,|מִסְתָּרָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and he will be unable|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יוּכָ֑ל\rb* \rb to conceal himself.|וְנֶחְבָּ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \rb His descendants|זַרְע֛וֹ\rb* \rb will be destroyed|שֻׁדַּ֥ד\rb*
\q2 \rb along with his relatives|וְאֶחָ֥יו\rb* \rb and neighbors,|וּשְׁכֵנָ֖יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and he will be no more.|וְאֵינֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Abandon|עָזְבָ֥ה\rb* \rb your orphans;|יְתֹמֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will preserve their lives.|אֲחַיֶּ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Let your widows|וְאַלְמְנֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb trust|תִּבְטָֽחוּ׃ס\rb* \rb in Me.”|עָלַ֥י\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “If|הִ֠נֵּה\rb* \rb those who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb do not|אֵ֨ין\rb* \rb deserve|מִשְׁפָּטָ֜ם\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb the cup|הַכּוֹס֙\rb* \rb must drink it,|שָׁת֣וֹ\rb*\rb |יִשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb* \rb can you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb possibly remain unpunished?|נָקֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |תִּנָּקֶ֑ה\rb* \rb You will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go unpunished,|תִנָּקֶ֔ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you must drink it too.|שָׁתֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb by Myself|בִ֤י\rb* \rb I have sworn,|נִשְׁבַּ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Bozrah|בָצְרָ֑ה\rb* \rb will become|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a desolation,|לְשַׁמָּ֧ה\rb* \rb a disgrace,|לְחֶרְפָּ֛ה\rb* \rb a ruin,|לְחֹ֥רֶב\rb* \rb and a curse,|וְלִקְלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb her cities|עָרֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb will be|תִהְיֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb in ruins|לְחָרְב֥וֹת\rb* \rb forever.”|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb a message|שְׁמוּעָ֤ה\rb* \rb from the LORD;|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb an envoy|וְצִ֖יר\rb* \rb has been sent|שָׁל֑וּחַ\rb* \rb to the nations:|בַּגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb*
\q1 \rb “Assemble yourselves|הִֽתְקַבְּצוּ֙\rb* \rb to march|וּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb against her!|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb Rise up|וְק֖וּמוּ\rb* \rb for battle!”|לַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb “For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb I will make you|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb small|קָטֹ֛ן\rb* \rb among nations,|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb despised|בָּז֖וּי\rb* \rb among men.|בָּאָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb The terror you cause|תִּֽפְלַצְתְּךָ֞\rb*
\q2 \rb and the pride of your|זְד֣וֹן\rb* \rb heart|לִבֶּ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb have deceived|הִשִּׁ֤יא\rb* \rb you,|אֹתָךְ֙\rb*
\q1 \rb O dwellers|שֹֽׁכְנִי֙\rb* \rb in the clefts|בְּחַגְוֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the rocks,|הַסֶּ֔לַע\rb*\f + \fr 49:16 \ft Or \fqa of Sela\f*
\q2 \rb O occupiers|תֹּפְשִׂ֖י\rb* \rb of the mountain|גִּבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb summit.|מְר֣וֹם\rb*
\q1 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you elevate|תַגְבִּ֤יהַ\rb* \rb your nest|קִנֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb like the eagle,|כַּנֶּ֙שֶׁר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb even from there|מִשָּׁ֥ם\rb* \rb I will bring you down,”|אֽוֹרִידְךָ֖\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb “Edom|אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb an object of horror.|לְשַׁמָּ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb All|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb who pass|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb by|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb will be appalled|יִשֹּׁ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and will scoff|וְיִשְׁרֹ֖ק\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her wounds.|מַכּוֹתֶֽהָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb As Sodom|סְדֹ֧ם\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֛ה\rb* \rb were overthrown|כְּֽמַהְפֵּכַ֞ת\rb*
\q2 \rb along with their neighbors,”|וּשְׁכֵנֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\qr \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb “no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb will dwell|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb there;|שָׁם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb man|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb will abide|יָג֥וּר\rb* \rb there.|בָּ֖הּ\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb Behold,|הִ֠נֵּה\rb* \rb one will come up|יַעֲלֶ֨ה\rb* \rb like a lion|כְּאַרְיֵ֞ה\rb*
