\s1 Jeremiah’s Message to Seraiah
\p \v 59 \rb This is the message|הַדָּבָ֞ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|צִוָּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |וּשְׂרָיָ֖ה\rb*\rb |שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb to the quartermaster|מְנוּחָֽה׃\rb* \rb Seraiah|שְׂרָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Neriah,|נֵרִיָּה֮\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Mahseiah,|מַחְסֵיָה֒\rb* \rb when he went|בְּלֶכְתּ֞וֹ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb in the fourth|הָרְבִעִ֖ית\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Zedekiah’s reign.|לְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb* \v 60 \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb had written|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb scroll|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb would come|תָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Babylon—|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*  \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb that had been written|הַכְּתֻבִ֖ים\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 61 \rb And Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Seraiah,|שְׂרָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb “When you get|כְּבֹאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb see|וְֽרָאִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb that you read all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb aloud,|וְֽקָרָ֔אתָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \v 62 \rb and say,|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb ‘O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb have promised|דִבַּ֜רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to cut off|לְהַכְרִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb so that no one|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb will remain—|יוֹשֵׁ֔ב\rb*  \rb neither man|לְמֵאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb nor|וְעַד־\rb* \rb beast.|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb Indeed,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it will be|תִּֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb desolate|שִׁמְמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb forever.’|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 63 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb When you finish|כְּכַלֹּ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb reading|לִקְרֹ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb scroll,|הַסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb tie|תִּקְשֹׁ֤ר\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb to it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and cast it|וְהִשְׁלַכְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Euphrates.|פְּרָֽת׃\rb* \v 64 \rb Then you are to say,|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb ‘In the same way|כָּ֠כָה\rb* \rb Babylon|בָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb will sink|תִּשְׁקַ֨ע\rb* \rb and never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb rise again,|תָקוּם֙\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb will bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb upon her.|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb And her people will grow weary.’”|וְיָעֵ֑פוּ\rb*
\p \rb Here|הֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb end|עַד־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jeremiah.|יִרְמְיָֽהוּ׃ס\rb*
\c 52
\s1 The Fall of Jerusalem Recounted
\r \ref Psalm 74:1–23|PSA 74:1-23\ref*; \ref Psalm 79:1–13|PSA 79:1-13\ref*; \ref 2 Kings 24:18–20|2KI 24:18-20\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 36:11–14|2CH 36:11-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-one|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb eleven|וְאַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Hamutal|חֲמִיטַל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּֽת־\rb* \rb of Jeremiah;|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb she was from Libnah.|מִלִּבְנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb And Zedekiah did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִֽים׃\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \v 3 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb* \rb of the anger|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb all this happened|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֣ם\rb* \rb and Judah,|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb He finally banished|הִשְׁלִיכ֥וֹ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb His presence.|פָּנָ֑יו\rb*
\p \rb And Zedekiah also|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb rebelled|וַיִּמְרֹ֥ד\rb* \rb against the king|בְּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb in the ninth|הַתְּשִׁעִ֜ית\rb* \rb year|בַשָּׁנָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Zedekiah’s reign,|לְמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb* \rb on the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |לַחֹדֶשׁ֒\rb* \rb day of the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִי֮\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֨ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb marched|בָּ֠א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb with his entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army.|חֵילוֹ֙\rb* \rb They encamped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb outside the city|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּבְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a siege wall|דָּיֵ֖ק\rb* \rb all|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb around it.|עָלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \v 5 \rb And the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb was kept|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb under siege|בַּמָּצ֑וֹר\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah’s|צִדְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb By the ninth day|בְּתִשְׁעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִי֙\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֑יר\rb* \rb was so severe|וַיֶּחֱזַ֥ק\rb* \rb that the people|לְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb had|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb food.|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \v 7 \rb Then the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb was breached;|וַתִּבָּקַ֣ע\rb* \rb and though the Chaldeans|וְכַשְׂדִּ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 52:7 \ft That is, the Babylonians; similarly in verses 8, 9, 14, and 17 \f*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb had surrounded|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֡ה\rb* \rb fled|יִבְרְחוּ֩\rb*\rb |וַיֵּצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb the city|מֵהָעִ֜יר\rb* \rb by night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb the two walls|הַחֹמֹתַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb garden.|גַּ֣ן\rb*
\p \rb They headed|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb the Arabah,|הָעֲרָבָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 52:7 \ft Or \fqa the Jordan Valley\f* \v 8 \rb but the army|חֵיל־\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּים֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדְּפ֤וּ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and overtook|וַיַּשִּׂ֥יגוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the plains|בְּעַֽרְבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jericho,|יְרֵח֑וֹ\rb* \rb and his whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb deserted|נָפֹ֖צוּ\rb* \rb him.|מֵעָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The Chaldeans seized|וַֽיִּתְפְּשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and brought him up|וַיַּעֲל֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb at Riblah|רִבְלָ֖תָה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hamath,|חֲמָ֑ת\rb* \rb where he pronounced|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb judgment|מִשְׁפָּטִֽים׃\rb* \rb on Zedekiah.|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb There at Riblah|בְּרִבְלָֽתָה׃\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחַ֧ט\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb before his eyes,|לְעֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb and he also|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb killed|שָׁחַ֥ט\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \v 11 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Then he put out|עִוֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb Zedekiah’s|צִדְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb eyes,|עֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb bound|וַיַּאַסְרֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb him|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb with bronze shackles,|בַֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb and took him|וַיְבִאֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb where|בָּבֶ֔לָה\rb* \rb he kept him|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb in custody|בְבֵית\rb*\rb |הַפְּקֻדֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb his dying|מוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb day.|י֥וֹם\rb*
\s1 The Temple Destroyed
