\p \v 12 \rb On the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day of the fifth|הַֽחֲמִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb month,|וּבַחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הִ֗יא\rb* \rb in the nineteenth|תְּשַֽׁע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַת֙\rb*\rb |לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar’s|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb reign|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb over Babylon,|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבֽוּזַרְאֲדָן֙\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard,|טַבָּחִ֔ים\rb* \rb a servant|עָמַ֛ד\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֗א\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He burned down|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the houses|בָּתֵּ֧י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem—|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb |שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb significant|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb building.|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \v 14 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb under|אֶת־\rb* \rb the captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִֽים׃\rb* \rb broke down|נָֽתְצוּ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the walls|חֹמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֖ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִֽים׃\rb* \rb carried into exile|הֶגְלָ֕ה\rb* \rb some of the poorest|וּמִדַּלּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb and|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb those who remained|יֶ֥תֶר\rb*\rb |הָעָ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the city,|בָּעִ֗יר\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the deserters|הַנֹּֽפְלִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb had defected|נָֽפְלוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the craftsmen.|הָֽאָמ֑וֹן\rb* \v 16 \rb But Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֖ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֑ים\rb* \rb left behind|הִשְׁאִ֕יר\rb* \rb some of the poorest|וּמִדַּלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to tend the vineyards|לְכֹרְמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and fields.|וּלְיֹגְבִֽים׃\rb*
