\p \v 31 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb On the twenty-fifth|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day of the twelfth|בִּשְׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb month|חֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the thirty-seventh|בִשְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֜בַע\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb of the exile|לְגָלוּת֙\rb* \rb of Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֣ן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the first year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|מַלְכֻת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֱוִ֣יל\rb* \rb of Evil-merodach|מְרֹדַךְ֩\rb* \rb king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he pardoned|נָשָׂ֡א\rb*\f + \fr 52:31 \ft Literally \fqa he lifted up the head of\f* \rb |רֹאשׁ֙\rb*\rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and released him|וַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb from|אוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb prison.|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַכְּלִיא׃\rb* \v 32 \rb And he spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb kindly|טֹב֑וֹת\rb* \rb to Jehoiachin|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and set|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb the thrones|לְכִסֵּ֧א\rb* \rb of the other kings|מְלָכִים\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Babylon.|בְּבָבֶֽל׃\rb*
